hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"35071","(35071) Ibn Sirin: Abu Bakr."
"35072","(35072) Al-Hasan: Abu Saeed."
"35073","(35073) Al-Sha’abi: Abu Amr."
"35074","(35074) Ibrahim Al-Nakha’i: Abu Imran."
"35075","(35075) Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila: Abu Issa."
"35076","(35076) Abdullah bin Ukaym: Abu Ma’bad."
"35077","(35077) Al-Hakam bin Utaiba: Abu Abdullah."
"35078","(35078) Hammad bin Abi Suleiman: Abu Ismail."
"35079","(35079) Al-Muhallab bin Abi Safari: Abu Saeed."
"35080","(35080) Waqi’ bin Sahban: Abu Aqeel."
"35081","(35081) Ata bin Abi Maimunah: Abu Muadh."
"35082","(35082) Saad bin Muadh: Abu Amr."
"35083","(35083) Amr bin Shuaib: Abu Ibrahim."
"35084","(35084) Abdullah bin Amr: Abu Muhammad."
"35085","(35085) Abdullah bin Al-Harith, nickname: Abu Al-Walid."
"35086","(35086) On the authority of Sufyan bin Uyaynah, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The land of the jinn is made of paper. And its soil is musk, and the roots of its trees are gold and silver, and its roots are pearls and aquamarines and rubies, and the leaves and the fruit are under Thus, whoever eats while standing will not be harmed by him, and whoever eats while sitting will not be harmed by him, and whoever eats while lying down will not be harmed by him: {And you are humbled. He cut it off in humiliation}"
"35087","(35087) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Ali bin Salih told us, on the authority of Omar bin Rabi’a, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibn Omar said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about Paradise: How is it? He said: Whoever enters Paradise will live and not die, and will enjoy blessings and will not be distressed, and his clothes will not wear out, and he will not be worn out. His youth, it was said: O Messenger of God, how was it built? He said: Its brick is made of silver, its brick is made of gold, its clay is musk, its pebbles are pearls and rubies, and its dirt Saffron \n(Muslim 2181, Ahmad 369)"
"35088","(35088) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri; That Ibn Sayyad asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the soil of Paradise? He said: White perfume, pure musk.\n(Muslim 2243. Ahmad 4)"
"35089","(35089) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of Hakim bin Jabir, he said: God Almighty has not touched with His hand any of His creation except three things; He planted the garden with His hand, then He made its soil roses and saffron, and its mountains musk, and He created Adam with His hand, and wrote the Torah. To Moses."
"35090","(35090) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murra, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, He said: The rivers of Paradise gush out from a mountain of musk. (Abu Naim 306)"
"35091","(35091) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Masruq, who said: Anhar Paradise flows through no grooves, and its fruits are like small fruits. Whenever one fruit is removed, another returns, and the clusters are twelve. An arm"
"35092","(35092) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Amr said: Al-Anqud is farther than Sana’a. (Ibn Hibban 7416. Tabarani 312)"
"35093","(35093) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The fronds of the jinn. From it are their clothes and their pieces, he said: And Ibn Abbas said: And its fruit has no stones. (Hakim 475)"
"35094","(35094) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Al-Hasan Al-Arni, on the authority of Huzail bin Sharhabeel, on the authority of Abdullah; In his saying: {Sidrāt al-Muntaha}, he said: The patience of the jinn, meaning its moderation, upon it are the virtues of Sundus and Istabraq."
"35095","(35095) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed me, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Habib, on the authority of Marthad bin Abdullah Al-Yazani, on the authority of a woman’s son selling to Ka’b, said: The jinn is falsified, then it is decorated, then it is seen. There are none of God’s creation, whether Muslim, Jew, or Christian, except for two men. A man who killed a believer intentionally, or a man who killed a covenant intentionally."
"35096","(35096) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Salman, who said: Trees and palm trees have their roots. Its markets are pearls and gold, and its highest yield is fruit. (Tirmidhi 2525. Abu Ali 6167)"
"35097","(35097) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Salman, who said: Trees and palm trees have their roots. Its market is pearls."
"35098","(35098) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When I came to the Sidra when its leaves were like the ears of an elephant, and when its leaves were like the ears of a goat, then when it was covered by the command of God Its cover changed and I remembered rubies. (Ahmed 148)"
"35099","(35099) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Mughith bin Sumayyah; Concerning his saying: (Blessed), he said: It is a tree in Paradise. None of the people of Paradise has a home except that a branch of Its branches, in which there are many colors of fruit, and birds like a flock of birds fall on them. He said: If a man desires a bird, he calls it. Then he comes until he meets his brothers, he said: Then he eats part of one of his sides, and some part of the other side, and then returns as he was. It was, so it flies. (Abu Nu’aym 68. Tabari 147)"
"35100","(35100) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Abdul-Karim, who said: I heard Ibn Sabit saying: The Messenger will come To the tree from the trees of Paradise, and he says: Indeed, my Lord commands you to follow this as He wills. Indeed, the Messenger will come to the man. From the people of Paradise, and the robe will be spread over him, and he will say: I have seen the robe, but I have never seen anything like this."
"35101","(35101) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, who said: Blessed is a tree in Paradise, if it has a rider. He mounted his trunk, or his trunk, and circumambulated it, until he reached the place from which he rode until he reached the pyramid."
"35102","(35102) Zayd ibn al-Hubab told us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Salih informed us, he said: Amr ibn Qays informed me, he said: A man from the people of Paradise will crave the fruit, and it will come until it flows in it, and it is in its origin. The tree"
"35103","(35103) Abu Usama told us, he said: Zakaria told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Awsaja, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, said: The jinn is a smog in which there is no rest, nor is it free."
"35104","(35104) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, on the authority of al-Nu’man ibn Sa’d, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Indeed, in Paradise there is a market in which there is neither buying nor selling, except images of men and women. A man desired images and entered into them, and indeed in them is a gathering of the beautiful houris, raising them with voices the like of which no creation has seen. They say: We are the immortal ones, so we will not perish. We are the contented ones, so we will not be displeased. We are the gentle ones, so we will not despair. So blessed is he who is For us, and we were for Him. (Tirmidhi 2550)"
"35105","(35105) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, on the authority of al-Nu’man ibn Sa’d, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Indeed, in Paradise there are rooms whose backs can be seen from their bellies, and whose bellies can be seen from their backs. He said: So he stood up. A Bedouin, so he said: To whom is this, O Messenger of God? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: This is for the one who speaks kindly, gives food, spreads greetings, and prays at night. And the people are sleeping."
"35106","(35106) Zaid bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Sa’id bin Abdul Rahman narrated to me, saying: Abu Hazim narrated to us, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, and he mentioned the Garden, and he said: Therein is what neither eye has seen nor ear. I heard, and it has not come to the heart of man.\n And in Paradise there is a tree in whose shade the rider travels for a hundred years without interruption. Recite, if you wish: {and an extended shadow} and for a place A whip in Paradise is better than this world and what is in it. Recite, if you wish: {So whoever is saved from the Fire and admitted to Paradise has certainly succeeded} Verse (Muslim 2175. Ahmad 334)"
"35107","(35107) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: God Almighty says: I have prepared for My righteous servants what no eye has seen and no ear has heard. And it has not entered the heart of mankind. Recite, if you wish: {And not a soul knows what has been hidden for them from the comfort of eyes, a recompense for what they did. They work}"
"35108","(35108) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, who said: The people of the jinn They will say: Take us to the market, and they will bring mountains of musk, or ropes of musk, or dunes of musk. Then God will send a wind upon them, and you will enter their homes, and their families will say to them: Indeed, you have increased in goodness after us. And they say the same to their families. (Bayhaqi 375)"
"35109","(35109) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Sabbah bin Abdullah Al-Bajlili, who said: Yahya bin Al-Jazzar narrated to us, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The birds of the jinn are like the birds of the jinn."
"35110","(35110) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Al-Hasan; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, one day described the jinn and the noble things that are in it, and he said, among other things, that he said: “Indeed, therein is A bird like a vulture."
"35111","(35111) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Khalid bin Ma’dan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: The jinn. A folded brochure hung from the horns of the sun, which is published every year, and the souls of the believers are in birds like starlings, and they get to know one another. They are provided with the fruits of Paradise."
"35112","(35112) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Al-Walid, who said: Mujahid was asked, and he was told: Is there anything in Is heaven listening? He said: In Paradise there are trees with hearing the likes of which the listeners have never heard."
"35113","(35113) Rawad bin Al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Ismail bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ali bin Abdullah bin Abbas; In His saying: {And your Lord will give it to you, and you will be satisfied}. He said: A thousand palaces of white pearls, the dust of which is musk, and in them is What is good for them?"
"35114","(35114) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: The closest family Paradise is the abode of one who has a thousand palaces, and in it are seventy thousand servants. Not one of them is a servant except that in His hand are pages of something else. In the hands of its owner, its door cannot be opened with anything it wants. If all the people of the world were to join it, it would expand it."
"35115","(35115) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: The length of a man is The people of Paradise will be ninety miles long, and the length of the mirror will be thirty miles long, and her seat will be grave, and indeed her desire will run into it. Her body is seventy years, she finds pleasure. (Ahmed 537)"
"35116","(35116) Ali bin Ubaid told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khalid told us, on the authority of Ziyad, the client of Banu Makhzum, He said: I heard Abu Hurairah say: In Paradise there is a tree in the shade of which the rider will travel for a hundred years. If you wish: {And a shadow stretched out.} So that reached Ka`b, and he said: He has spoken the truth. By the One who sent down the Torah on the tongue of Moses, and the Criterion on the tongue of Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, if a man were to ride his saddle, or his trunk, and then turn around towards the root of that tree, he would not have reached it. Until it falls into old age. Indeed, God planted it with His own hand, and breathed into it of His Spirit, and indeed He destroyed it from beyond the wall of Paradise. And there is no river in Paradise that does not issue from the root of that tree."
"35117","(35117) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, he said: Hammam bin Yahya narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Imran Al-Junai, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Musa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The tent is a round, sixty years in length. An incline, in every corner of which there is a family for the believer, no one else sees them. (Bukhari 3243. Muslim 23)"
"35118","(35118) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Hassan, on the authority of Yazid al-Raqqashi, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: If One of the women of Paradise looked at her wrists and was dazzled by the sunlight."
"35119","(35119) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Salama bin Nubait, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: If only a woman from the family Paradise has spread its palms, illuminating what is between the heavens and the earth. (Bukhari 6568 and Tirmidhi 1651)"
"35120","(35120) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Indeed, there is a woman’s scent from the houris. Al-Ain, from his journey of fifty years."
"35121","(35121) Shababah ibn Siwar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of someone who heard a person say: Indeed, the beautiful virgin is in Paradise. Let them sing, saying: We are the good and beautiful women, imprisoned for honorable husbands. (Tabarani 6493)"
"35122","(35122) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Amr bin Maimun, he said: Abdullah bin Masoud narrated to us; The woman of the jinn will wear seventy pieces of silk, and one will see the whiteness of her legs and the beauty of her legs. And the marrow of her legs behind all of that, and that is because God says: {As if they were rubies and coral}. Indeed, it is only Sapphire is a stone, so if you take a wire and put it in that stone, then straighten it, you will see the wire behind the stone. \n(Tirmidhi 2533)"
"35123","(35123) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Ayyub al-Azdi, or Shahr ibn Hawshab, Shakak Hammam, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: In Paradise, from freeing horses and honoring the noble ones who ride them He welcomed her and said: Henna is the master of the essence of Paradise."
"35124","(35124) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Al-Masoudi informed us, on the authority of Alqamiya bin Marthad, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, On the authority of his father; A man said: O Messenger of God, I am a man who loves horses. Are there any horses in Paradise? He said: O Abdullah, if God admits you to Paradise, do not wish to ride a horse made of ruby that will fly you into heaven. Paradise, whatever you want, do it. The man said: O Messenger of God, are there camels in Paradise? He said: O Abdullah, if God admits you to Paradise, you will have in it whatever your soul desires and what your eyes delight in. (Bayhaqi 395. Ahmad 352)"
"35125","(35125) Ismail bin Aliyah told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Laqit bin Al-Muthanna Al-Baili, he said: It was said: O Abu Umamah, will the people of Paradise visit one another? He said: Yes, and God is upon her. (Abdul Razzaq 2088)"
"35126","(35126) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Minhal ibn Amr, on the authority of Qays ibn Sakan, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: A man from the people of Paradise will be brought a cup while he is sitting with his wife, and he will drink it, then turn to it. His wife, and he says: Your beauty has increased seventy-fold in my eyes."
"35127","(35127) Waki’ and Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Thumama ibn Uqba Al-Muhallami, on the authority of Zaid Ibn Arqam said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A man from the people of Paradise will be given the strength of a hundred men in Eating, drinking, sexual intercourse, and lust. Then one of the Jews said: Whoever eats and drinks will have Hajj? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: One of you experienced a sweat gushing out from his skin, and then his stomach became atrophied. \n(Ahmad 367, Darami 2825)"
"35128","(35128) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: God Almighty said: God Almighty said: I have prepared for My righteous servants what no eye has seen, no ear heard, and no thought has occurred to me. A human heart. Abu Hurairah said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Yes, what God has revealed to you, read. If you wish: {But no soul knows what has been hidden from them of the comfort of eyes} the verses, and Abu Hurairah used to recite them: Qurrat My eyes\n(Muslim 2175. Ibn Majah 4328)"
"35129","(35129) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: The first group of people from my nation to enter Paradise will be in the form of the moon on the night of the full moon, then those They will be colored like the brightest star in the sky, and after that they will go to resting places, neither defecating nor urinating, nor They blow their nose, but they do not spit. Their combs are gold, and their censers are made of aloe. Abu Bakr said: He means the oud, and their nostrils. Musk, their morals are like the creation of one man, in the image of their father Adam, sixty cubits long. (Muslim 2179. Ahmad 253)"
"35130","(35130) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The people of Paradise will eat and drink therein, and they will not defecate nor urinate. They do not spit, nor do they blow their nose. Their food is sputum and a phlegm like the phlegm of musk. (Muslim 2181, Ahmed 316)"
"35131","(35131) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: The lowest abode among the people of Paradise is a man who has an abode made of single pearls, and among them are two chambers. And its doors.\n(Tirmidhi 2562. Ahmad 76)"
"35132","(35132) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: Indeed, the lowest in rank among the people of Paradise is On the Day of Resurrection, his lunch will be brought in seventy thousand plates, each plate having a color not like the other, and he will find For the last is the same as the first, and there is no shame in it."
"35133","(35133) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Indeed, the person closest to the dwelling place among the people of Paradise is the one who makes a wish upon God, and it will be said to him: That. And the like of it is for you, and he is taught such-and-such, and it is said to him: That is for you and the like of it is with him. Abu Sa’id said: Al-Khudri: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: That is for you and ten times like it. (Ahmed 4500 Dharmi 2829)"
"35134","(35134) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Ibn Abjar, on the authority of Thawār, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Indeed, the lowest of the people of Paradise is His abode, whoever looks at His kingdom of two thousand years, will see the farthest part as well as the lowest, and indeed the best of the inhabitants of Paradise are His status, whoever looks at the face of God twice every day. (Tirmidhi 2553. Ahmad 64)"
"35135","(35135) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Hariz bin Othman told me, he said: Suleiman bin Samir told us. Al-Alani, he said: Kathir bin Mara Al-Hadrami told us, he said: The Companions (...)"
"35136","(35136) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Hariz bin Othman told us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Amir, on the authority of Sufyan bin Umar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Umar, said: A man from the people of the jinn will come and the women will look over him and say: O so-and-so. Ibn so-and-so, you are not one of the people from whom you left with someone more worthy of you than us. Then he says: Who are you? So they say: We are among those whom God Almighty said: {But no soul knows what has been hidden for them from the comfort of eyes, as a recompense for what they did. They work}"
"35137","(35137) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, he said: Abdullah said: It is written in Torah: God has prepared for those whose sides turn away from their beds, which eye has not seen, and ear has not heard, and it has not occurred to me. The heart of a human being, and what no angel or messenger knows. He said: And We recite it: {So no soul knows what has been hidden from them of the Qur’an. Ayin} until the end of the verse."
"35138","(35138) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim ibn Damra, he said: I heard Ali He says: {And those who fear their Lord will be led into Paradise in groups} until, when they come to one of the gates of Paradise, they find At its gate is a tree, and two eyes emerge from under its legs, so they go to one of them as if they had been commanded to do so, and purify themselves. From it, and He will bestow upon them His gaze of bliss. He said: Their skin will never change after that, nor will their hair become disheveled. after it forever, as if they had been anointed with oil. He said: Then they go to the afterlife, and drink from it, and it vanishes with what is in it. Their bellies are free from harm or filth.\n And the angels will meet them, and they will say: {Peace be upon you, may you be well, so enter it to abide forever}. He said: And every boy will meet you. Their companion, they go around with him. The verb to give birth to an intimate partner comes from the unseen: Be glad, God has prepared for you from The noblewoman is such and such. He said: And two young men will go ahead of him to his wives from among the virgins, and they will say to them: This is so-and-so. In His name in this world, He has come to you. He said: They will say: Have you seen Him? They say: Yes. He said: Then their joy becomes light, until they go out to the corners of the door.\n He said: And he will enter Paradise, and behold, we will see something lined up, cups placed, and carpets spread out, and he will recline on One of his couches. He said: Then he looks at the foundation of his building, and behold, it was founded on the pearly cluster. Yellow, red, green, and every color. He said: Then he raises his limbs to his roof. If God had not destined him for him, he would have suffered. With his foresight that he would be struck by lightning, then he recited: {And they say: Praise be to God who has guided us to this, and we would not have been guided had it not been for him. That God has guided us}"
"35139","(35139) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Abu Khalid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said By the One who sent down the Book to Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, the people of Paradise will increase in beauty and goodness, as They will increase in ugliness and poverty in this world."
"35140","(35140) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salma, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The people of Paradise will enter Paradise stripped, stripped, white, Curly, with kohl, thirty-three sons, according to the creation of Adam, sixty cubits long and seven cubits wide.\n(Tirmidhi 2539. Ahmad 343)"
"35141","(35141) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: He says Boys of the people of Paradise: Where do we pick your food from? Where will we give you water?"
"35142","(35142) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Dhudhail; That Moses, or another of the prophets, said: O Lord, how can this be from You? Your guardians on earth are afraid, they will be killed, they will be hunted down, and they will be cut off, and your enemies will eat whatever they want and drink whatever they want. They wished, and something like this, and He said: Take My servant to Paradise, and he will see the likes of which he has never seen before, to cups. Placed, and we spread out arrays of carpets and carpets, and to the virgins, and to the fruits, and to the servants as if they were A hidden pearl. He said: What harm has befallen my friends in this world if their fate is this? Then he said: Take my servant, and he will be taken to Hell, and a neck will emerge from it. The servant will be struck by shock, then he will recover and say: It is of no use. My enemies, what have I given them in this world if their fate is this? He said: Nothing."
"35143","(35143) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Anbasa ibn Sa`id, the judge of Rayy, narrated to me, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Abi al-Mughirah, On the authority of Shimr ibn Atiyya, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: Indeed, Allah has a kingdom. From the day He was created, He fashions the adornments of the people of Paradise until you arise. Al-Saa’i, even if a heart from the jewels of the people of Paradise were taken out, it would be dazzled by the light of the sun’s rays, so do not ask after it about its jewellery. People of Paradise\n(Ahmed 169)"
"35144","(35144) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Balaj, who said: I heard Abraham say: In Paradise there is sexual intercourse. They wanted, and there was no child. He said: Then he turns and looks, and the desire is created for him. Then he looks, and the vision is created for him. Other desires"
"35145","(35145) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, he said: Ibn Abbas was asked: Does the jinn give birth? ? He said: If they want. (Tirmidhi 2563. Ahmed 9)"
"35146","(35146) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Musa ibn Ubaidah, he said: Muhammad ibn Ka’b narrated to me, on the authority of Awf ibn Malik. Al-Ashja’i, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: I know that the last of the people of Paradise to enter Paradise is a man who was He asks God to remove him from Hell, so that when the people of Paradise enter Paradise, and the people of Hell, the Fire will be between them. That, so he said: O Lord, bring me close to the gate of Paradise. It was said: O son of Adam, did you not ask to be removed from the Fire? He said: O Lord, and who is like you? Bring me closer to the gate of Paradise. It was said: O son of Adam, did you not ask to be removed from the Fire? He said: Who is like you? Bring me closer to the gate of Paradise.\n Then he looked at a tree at the gate of Paradise and said: I will bring me close to it so that I may seek shade from its shade and eat from its fruit. He said: O son of Adam, didn't you say? He said: O Lord, and who is like you? He brought me closer to it, and he saw something better than that, so he said: O Lord, bring me closer to it, so he said: O son of Adam, did you not say? Until he said: O Lord, who is like you, so bring me near.\n So it was said: “Read.” Abu Bakr said: “Al-Add” means “strengthening,” so you will have what your feet have reached and your eyes have seen. He said: “So he will run even when he gets wet.” Meaning, he is tired. He said: O Lord, this is for me, and this is for me? So it is said: You have something like it or twice as much. So it is said: My Lord has been pleased with me, so if He had given me permission to clothe the people of this world And their food is sufficient for them. (Tabarani 143)"
"35147","(35147) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Zuhair bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Abi Ayyash, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The closest to the dwellers of Paradise is a man whose face God has turned away from Hell. He faced Paradise, and a tree with shade appeared to him, and he said: O Lord, bring me to this tree so that I may be in its shade, and he said God: Is it possible that, if I did that, you would ask Me for something else? He said: No, and I glorify you. So God presented him to it and made it appear to him as a tree. Another one has shade and fruit. He said: Oh Lord, bring me to this tree so that I may be in its shade and eat of its fruit. He said God: Is it possible that, if I give you that, you will ask Me for something else? He said: No, and I glorify you, so God will present him to her. Then another tree with shade, fruit, and water will appear to him, and he will say: O Lord, bring me to this tree, so that I may be in it. Its shade, and I will eat of its fruit, and drink of its water. He will say: Is it possible that if I do that, someone else will ask me about it? He will say: No. By Your glory, I do not ask you for anything else, so God will present it to it.\n He said: Then the gate of Paradise will appear to him, and he will say: O Lord, bring me to the gate of Paradise, so that I will be under the purity of Paradise. And I look at its people, and God brings him to it, and he sees the people of Paradise and what is in it, and he says: Yes, my Lord. Admit you to Paradise, and God will admit you to Paradise. When he enters Paradise, he will say: This is for you and this is for you. Then God will say: He wished, and he wished, and God reminded him: Ask of such-and-such, until when his hopes ceased, God said: It is yours. And ten times as much. He said: Then he enters his house, and his two wives from among the beautiful virgins enter upon him, and they say to him: Praise be to him. To God who chose you for us, and we chose for you, and He says: No one has been given anything like what I have given you. (Muslim 1751, Ahmad 27)"
"35148","(35148) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, on the authority of al-Nu’man ibn Sa’d, on the authority of Ali; In these verses: {On the Day when We will gather the righteous to the Most Gracious as a delegation}. He said: Then he said: Do you know what they will be gathered upon? By God, they will not be gathered on their feet, but rather they will be brought with camels the like of which no creation has seen, on saddles. Gold, and its edges are aquamarine, so they sit on it, then they are taken away until they knock on the door of Paradise. (Tabari 16)"
"35149","(35149) Qarad Abu Nuh narrated to us, he said: Shu’abi narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of a man, on the authority of my father"
"35150","(35150) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ubaydah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Indeed, I know the last of the people of Hell to emerge from Hell, a man crawling out of it, and it will be said to him: Go and enter Paradise. He said: Then he will go and enter Paradise, and he will find the people have taken abodes. He said: Then he will return and say: O Lord, the people have taken the dwellings. He said: Then it will be said to him: Do you remember the time in which you were? He says: Yes, he said: Then it is said to him: Make a wish, so he makes a wish, and it is said: You will have that which you wished for and ten times the worldly reward. He said: So he says to him: Are you mocking me when you are the king? He said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughing until his molars were visible.\n(Bukhari 6571, Muslim 174)"
"35151","(35151) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Atiya, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: The first group to enter Paradise will be in the shape of the moon on a full-moon night, and the second will be in the color of The most beautiful shining star in the sky. Each one of them has two wives, on each of the wives there are seventy shades. It appears The brain of her legs behind her. (Tirmidhi 2522)"
"35152","(35152) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Al-Mugheerah bin Shu’bi, he said: Musa said: Oh My Lord, what is the closest place to the people of Paradise? He said: A man stays in the dungeon where people are imprisoned. He said: Then it is said to him: Arise and enter the Garden. He said: Where can I enter, and I may enter? People preceded me? He said: Then it will be said to him: “Wish for four kings of the world, of whom you wished for like their kingship and authority.” He said: He says: So-and-so, he said: Then he counts four, then it is said to him: Wishing with your heart whatever you wish, he said: Then he wishes you, he said: Then it is said He said: You may desire whatever you wish. He said: Then you may desire it. He said: Then it will be said: This is for you ten times as much. He said: Then Moses said: O Lord. So what are the people of your elite? He said: So it was said: This is what I wanted. He said: I created their dignity and made it with my own hand, and I sealed its treasures such as no eye has seen. And it did not occur to the heart of any human being. Then he recited: {So no soul knows what has been hidden from them from the comfort of eyes, a recompense for what they used to do}"
"35153","(35153) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Asim bin Badla, on the authority of Khaythamiah; Abdullah bin Amr said: The people of Aliyah have windows overlooking it, so when one of them looks up, Paradise shines. He said: Then the people of Paradise will say: A man from the people of Aliyin has risen as honor."
"35154","(35154) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The title of a bow I am one of you, and his rank is from Paradise, better than this world and all that is in it. (Abdul Razzaq 20888)"
"35155","(35155) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir; In his saying: {In a meadow they will be inhabited} He said: Inhabitant is the one who hears in Paradise."
"35156","(35156) Affan told us, he said: Rabi’ah bin Kulthum told us, he said: I heard Al-Hasan, saying: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, if a woman from among the women of the people of Heaven were to supervise the people of the earth, It will fill the earth with the scent of musk, and a woman from among the wives of the people of Heaven will be better than the world and all that is in it. Do you know what Al-Nasif? This is the veil. (Bukhari 2796 and Tirmidhi 1651)"
"35157","(35157) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: An inch of Paradise is better than the world and what is in it. (Ibn Majah 4329)"
"35158","(35158) Yahya bin Issa told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Thawair, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The lowest of the inhabitants of the jinn is His abode, a man who has a thousand palaces, and between each two palaces there is a distance of a year, the farthest of which is seen as the lowest, In every palace of the beautiful virgins, the winds, and the children, he does not call for anything but it will be brought to him. (Tabari 29)"
"35159","(35159) Muhammad bin Abi Ubaidah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Harith, he said: Mughith said Ibn Sumayyah: Indeed, in Paradise there are palaces of gold, palaces of silver, palaces of ruby, and palaces of aquamarine, its mountains. Musk, and its soil is rose and saffron. (Abu Naim 68)"
"35160","(35160) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, he said: Qatad narrated to us, on the authority of Anas, he said: Indeed, he said: “The people of the jinn” To say: Go with us to the market, and they will bring mountains of musk, and they will sit and talk to you. (Abdul Razzaq 20881)"
"35161","(35161) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymi, who said: I have been informed that he swears an oath. For a man from among the people of Paradise, he will eat, eat, and sleep. If he eats, he will be given a drink of pure water, and he will emerge from His skin oozes like musk, then his lust returns. (Ibn Jarir 29)"
"35162","(35162) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Kathir, On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: They will gather, and it will be said: Where are the poor and poor of this nation? He said: Then they emerge, and it is said: What do you have? And they say: O Lord, You have tested us and we have been patient, and You know best. He said: And I see it. He said: You have given control over wealth and authority other than us. He said: Then it will be said: You have told the truth, and they will enter Paradise before the rest of the people for a time, and the severity of the reckoning will remain on those with wealth and authority. He said: I said: Where will the believers be on that day? He said: Chairs of light will be placed for them, and clouds will shade them, and that day will be shorter for them than an hour. Day (Ibn Hibban 7419)"
"35163","(35163) Zaid bin Harun told us, saying: Humaid told us, on the authority of Anas; Abdullah bin Salam came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at the beginning of Medina, and asked him: What is the first thing to eat? The people of Paradise? He said: Gabriel told me earlier: The first thing the people of Paradise will eat is its offal, like the liver of a whale. (Bukhari 3329)"
"35164","(35164) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Usama ibn Zayd, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ka’b, who said: He was seen in Paradise. Like lightning. It was said: What is this? It was said: A man from the people of Aliyin moved from one room to another."
"35165","(35165) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak; {Those are the ones who divide the rooms} He said: The rooms are the paradise."
"35166","(35166) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Ali bin Muslim, on the authority of Mujahid; Omar bin Al-Khattab read on the pulpit: {The Gardens of Eden}, and he said: Do you know what the Gardens of Eden are? He said: A palace in Paradise with five thousand gates, and on each gate there are twenty-five thousand beautiful virgins. No one can enter it except A prophet, congratulations to the owner of the grave, and he pointed to the grave of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a friend, congratulations to my father. A virgin, and a witness, and indeed Omar is a witness. Then he said: By the one who brought me out of my house, he is capable of He will drive her to me."
"35167","(35167) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah; {The Gardens of Eden}, he said: The interior of Paradise."
"35168","(35168) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, on the authority of Bashir bin Ka’b, who said: He said: Kaab: Indeed, in Paradise there is a ruby, in which there is no crack or connection, in it there are seventy thousand houses, in each house seventy thousand Of the beautiful virgins, no one can enter it except a prophet, a truthful person, a witness, a just imam, or someone who is arbitrator in his own right. He said: We said: O Ka’b, and what is the arbiter in itself? He said: The man is captured by the enemy, and they judge him between him becoming a disbeliever, or committing to Islam and being killed, so he chooses to It requires Islam."
"35169","(35169) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Amr bin Aws, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who reported With it, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, those who are just with God are on platforms of light, at the right hand of the Most Gracious, and both His hand is the right hand, those who are just in their judgment and to their families and to what they have loyal to. (Muslim 1458, Ahmed 203)"
"35170","(35170) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, those who are just in this world will be on podiums of pearls on the Day of Resurrection. The hands of the Most Gracious, for what they did justly in this world. (Ahmed 203)"
"35171","(35171) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Abu Hayyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Zur’a, ??n Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, what is between the two doors of Paradise is for you both. Between Mecca and Hijr, or as between Mecca and Busra."
"35172","(35172) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Qurayh, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, on the authority of Khaled bin Umair (h) and on the authority of Abu Naama, He heard it from Khaled bin Umair. He said: Utbah bin Ghazwan addressed us and said: What is between the two doors is one of the gates of Paradise. Their journey will last for forty years, and a day will come at the gates of Paradise, and there will be no gate therein except that it is harsh. (Muslim 2279. Ahmad 61)"
"35173","(35173) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: What is between the two gates of Paradise? Forty autumns for the glorious rider, and there will come upon him a day of intense crowding."
"35174","(35174) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Muhazim, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah, he said: He turned The believer is in Paradise of pearls, in it are forty houses, in the middle of which there are trees that grow trees, so he comes to it. Then he takes with his finger seventy jewels garnished with pearls and coral."
"35175","(35175) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, He said: The Companions of Al-A`raf will lead them to a river, and it will be said to it: Al-Hayah, its borders are golden reeds. He said: I see it. He said: It is crowned with pearls, and they bathe with it, and a white mole appears on their throats. Then they come back and bathe, Whenever they wash themselves, they become whiter, and it is said to them: “Wish for whatever you wish.” Then they wish for whatever they wish, and it is said: “You have whatever you wish.” If you wish seventy-fold, then they will be poor people of Paradise. (Tabari 191)"
"35176","(35176) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid; {And among them are women whose limbs are limited}. He said: Their limbs are limited to their wives, so they will not reject anyone else."
"35177","(35177) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Ad-Dahhak; {As if they were rubies and coral}. He said: Their colors are like rubies and pearls in their purity."
"35178","(35178) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Al-Hurr bin Jarmuz, who said: I heard Abdullah bin Al-Harith say: {As if they were rubies and coral} He said: As if they were pearls on a string."
"35179","(35179) Yunus bin Muhammad told us, he said: Dawud bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: I heard Sulaim Aba Abdullah, on the authority of Mujahid {As if they were rubies and coral}. He said: The marrow of their stems can be seen from behind the garment, just as the thread in a ruby is seen."
"35180","(35180) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Mughirah bin Muslim, on the authority of Ikrimah; {No human being before them, nor any jinn, had intercourse with them.} He said: He had intercourse with them."
"35181","(35181) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: He trampled on them."
"35182","(35182) Abd ibn Sulaiman and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Jariyah ibn Sulaiman. On the authority of Ibn Al-Zubayr: {Two piles}, he said: Two greens from irrigation."
"35183","(35183) Yazeed told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Abu Salih, he said: Khadrawan."
"35184","(35184) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; {Two piles}: green."
"35185","(35185) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Amr bin Qays, on the authority of Salama, on the authority of Mujahid; Concerning his saying: {two green ones}, he said: two green ones from their rain."
"35186","(35186) Ishaq bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: Two black ones from the rain."
"35187","(35187) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Atiyya, who said: Khadrawan."
"35188","(35188) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Two vegetables from irrigation."
"35189","(35189) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Qays, on the authority of Salamah, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: {two fresh ones} with all goodness."
"35190","(35190) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: {two fountains}, with water And fruits"
"35191","(35191) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abi Bazza, on the authority of Abi Ubaidah, on the authority of Abd God; {In them are good things, good}, He said: In every tent there is good."
"35192","(35192) I narrated on the authority of Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abu Salih; {In them are good things, beautiful}, he said: virgins of Paradise."
"35193","(35193) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The pearly tent is hollow, one league upon another, and it has four thousand golden leaves."
"35194","(35194) Othman bin Ali told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abu Salih; {Hours enclosed in tents} He said: Virgins of the Garden."
"35195","(35195) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said about: {Hour enclosed in tents}, He said: a hollow round, or hollow. (Tabari 27)"
"35196","(35196) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abdul Malik bin Misra, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: hollow pearl"
"35197","(35197) Muhammad bin Marwan Al-Basri narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Awwam, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; {Hours enclosed in tents}, he said: Ibn Abbas said: A tent is a hollow circle, a farsakh within a farsakh, in which there are four thousand. shutter\n(Ibn Jarir 27)"
"35198","(35198) Muhammad bin Marwan told us, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Ikrimah; {Hoor enclosed in tents}, he said: hollow pearls."
"35199","(35199) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hazan ibn Bashir, who said: I heard Amr ibn Maymun say: Al-Khaymah. hollow pearl"
"35200","(35200) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Abu Jafar, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah; {Hoor enclosed in tents}, he said: confined."
"35201","(35201) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Abi Ma’shar, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b Al-Qurazi; Concerning his statement: “Hour enclosed in tents,” he said: “In hijāl.”"
"35202","(35202) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Salama, on the authority of Al-Dahhak; Regarding his saying: {Hower enclosed in tents}, he said: a hollow pearl."
"35203","(35203) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The tent is a hollow pearl."
"35204","(35204) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr; In his saying: {reclining on a green tree and a beautiful creature}, he said: The tree is the garden of the jinn, and the genius is freed. The carpets."
"35205","(35205) Abdou bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: The flaps are the valves, and the genius is the carpets."
"35206","(35206) Qabisa narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Harun bin Antar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; {Reclining on a green platform}, he said: loose locks, rugs, and furniture."
"35207","(35207) Qubaisa narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Rabah ibn Abi Ma’ruf, on the authority of Mujahid {and a handsome genius} who said: Al-Dibaj."
"35208","(35208) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abu Raja’, on the authority of Al-Hasan; {Reclining on a green cover} He said: rugs. The people of the pre-Islamic era used to say: rugs."
"35209","(35209) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: Istibraq is brocade. The thick one"
"35210","(35210) Abd ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: Istibraq is thick brocade."
"35211","(35211) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hammam told us, he said: Zayd bin Aslam told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, On the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: Paradise is a hundred levels, between every two levels. Just as between the heavens and the earth, and Paradise is the highest level, and above it is the Throne, and from it rivers gush out. The Four Paradise, so if you ask God for Paradise, ask Him for Firdaus. (Ahmad 316. Tirmidhi 2530)"
"35212","(35212) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid; {On beds facing each other}. He said: Do not look at each other’s backs."
"35213","(35213) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; {They will not be torn from it, nor will they bleed.} He said: Their heads will not be torn apart, nor will their minds bleed."
"35214","(35214) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abu Jafar, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Mujahid; {And a cup of fresh wine}, he said: white wine, {they will not break from it nor will it bleed}. He will destroy her."
"35215","(35215) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Utba, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr (h) and on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Mujahid; Regarding his saying: {made in style}, one of them said: Al-Marmaliya, and the other said: Al-Marmaliya in gold."
"35216","(35216) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hassan bin Abi Al-Ashras, on the authority of Mughith bin Sumayyah: He said: The birds come and perch on the tree, and they eat some old meat from one side, and some roast from the other."
"35217","(35217) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Abu Umamah; (And raised beds), he said: If a bed had fallen from its top, such-and-such a sheep would have returned to its resting place."
"35218","(35218) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’; {Qutoofaa Daniyah}, he said: A man eats from its fruits while standing."
"35219","(35219) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’; {close}, he said: I came close to them."
"35220","(35220) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’; {And its harvests were subdued in humiliation}. He said: It was subdued for them. They take from it wherever they wish."
"35221","(35221) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The genius is the thick brocade."
"35222","(35222) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, he said: When God created the Garden of Eden He said to her: Speak to me, and she said: The believers have succeeded. (Bazzar 3507)"
"35223","(35223) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Mujahid; {On the couches we recline} He said: The beds are covered with curtains."
"35224","(35224) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abu Raja’, on the authority of Al-Hasan; {They will be made to drink of sealed nectar}. He said: This is wine."
"35225","(35225) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murā, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The nectar is the wine."
"35226","(35226) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murā, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah; {sealed}, he said: mixed, {its conclusion is musk} he said: its taste and scent, {tasnim} he said: a spring in Paradise to drink from. The close ones purely, and it is mixed with the companions of the right hand."
"35227","(35227) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Malik ibn Al-Harith: {And its source is from Tasnim, a spring from which one drinks. Al-Muqarraboon} and it is mixed for the rest of the people of Paradise."
"35228","(35228) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abu Raja’, on the authority of Al-Hasan; {And its mood is from Tasnim}. He said: hidden things that God has hidden for the people of Paradise."
"35229","(35229) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Saeed (h) and on the authority of Abu Ruq, on the authority of Al-Dahhak; In his saying: {its end is musk}, they said: its last taste."
"35230","(35230) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Quraysh bin Sharik Al-Ajli, on the authority of Ibn Sabit He said: I have been informed that at the right hand of the Most Gracious, and both of His hands are the right hand, will be a people on platforms of light, and their faces will be light. They wear green garments, covering the eyes of those who see them. They are not prophets, nor witnesses. They are people who love each other in glory. God when you disobey God on earth. (Tabarani 12686)"
"35231","(35231) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Omar told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Abi Abla told me. Al-Uqaili; Al-Alaa bin Ziyad was narrating on the authority of the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: Servants of God are not With prophets, and no witnesses, the prophets and martyrs will be blessed on the Day of Resurrection, because of their closeness to God, on the pulpits of Light, the prophets and martyrs say: Who are these? They say: These people loved each other for the sake of God, other than the wealth they exchanged, nor the ties of kinship between them. (Nasa’i 11236)"
"35232","(35232) Ali bin Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mukhtar, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Al-Kawthar A river that my Lord has promised me in Paradise, for which there is much good, and it is a basin to which my nation will return on the Day of Resurrection. Its meaning is as many as the stars."
"35233","(35233) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Al-Kawthar is a river in Paradise, its edges are of gold, and its stream is on rubies and pearls, its soil. It is sweeter than musk, its water is sweeter than honey, and whiter than snow."
"35234","(35234) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Al-Kawthar: daylight. In the courtyard of Paradise, its shore is a hollow circle, and there are as many jugs and vessels in it as there are stars. (Bukhari 4965. An-Nasa’i 11705)"
"35235","(35235) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far bin Burqan, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Marzuq, on the authority of Ata bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Abu Muslim Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal and Ubadah bin Al-Samit, who said: We heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He talks about his Lord, saying: My love is established for those who love each other for My sake, My love is established for those who exchange each other for My sake, My love is established for those who love each other for My sake. Upon those who visit each other for the sake of God, and those who love one another for the sake of God, upon platforms of light in the shade of the Throne, on the Day when there will be no shade but His shade.\n(Tirmidhi 2390 and Ahmad 236)"
"35236","(35236) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Hamid bin Ata, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Those who love one another for the sake of God are on a pillar of red ruby, at the top of the pillar are seventy thousand. rooms, supervising the people of Paradise. When one of them rises, his beauty will fill the homes of the people of Paradise, just as the sun fills With its light, the homes of the people of the world will be illuminated. He said: Then the people of Paradise will say: Bring us out to those who love one another for the sake of God. He said: Then they will come out and see in their faces the likeness of the moon on a full-moon night, wearing green garments, written on Their foreheads: those who love one another for the sake of God. (Musnad 416)"
"35237","(35237) Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad al-Ammi told us, on the authority of Abu Imran al-Juniy, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Samit, on the authority of Abu Dharr said: I said: O Messenger of God, what is the vessel for the basin? He said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, because my soul is greater than the number of stars and planets in the heavens, in the dark night. The sanatorium, whoever drinks from it will not thirst, its width is from Amman to Aila, its water is whiter than milk. And sweeter than honey."
"35238","(35238) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Sa’id bin Abi Aroub narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, On the authority of Maadan bin Abi Talha al-Amari, on the authority of Thawban; That the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked about saa’i in the basin? He said: There is not a month between these two places of residence to Amman, or something like that. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked. Did he say hello to his drink? He said: Whiter than milk, and sweeter than honey, the gutter of ink is pouring into it, or ink from the jinn. One is paper, the other is gold."
"35239","(35239) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Zakaria bin Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Atiyah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have a basin as long as the Kaaba to the Holy House, white.” Like milk, its vessel is as numerous as the stars, and I will be the most followed of the prophets on the Day of Resurrection."
"35240","(35240) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I entered The jinn, and when I was in a flowing river, its two edges were tents of pearls. He said: So I struck the clay with my hand, and when it touched it, I would exhale. So I said: O Gabriel, what is this? He said: This is Al-Kawthar which God has given you."
"35241","(35241) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murra, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: Anhar Paradise bursts from a mountain of musk."
"35242","(35242) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Saad Al-Tai, he said: I was informed that When God created Paradise, He said to it: “Adorn yourself,” and she did. Then He said to it: “Adorn yourself,” and she did. Then He said to it: Speak, and she said: Blessed is the one with whom you are pleased."
"35243","(35243) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: A prophet from among the prophets said: O God, the servant from among Your servants worships You and obeys You. He avoids your anger, the world is removed from him, and calamities are exposed to him, and the servant worships others and commits disobedience to you. So the world will be presented to him, and the affliction will be removed from him. He said: Then God revealed to him, “The servants and the lands are His, all of them.” He glorifies My praise, but as for My believing servant, he will have bad deeds. I will only expose him to the calamity and remove it from him. This world, then it will be an expiation for his sins, and I will reward him when he meets Me, and as for My disbelieving servant, good deeds will be for him. So I will remove the affliction from him, and expose him to the world, so that it will be a reward for his good deeds, and I will reward him for his bad deeds when He meets me."
"35244","(35244) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Qadamah, on the authority of Abu Imran Al-Juniy, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Qais, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, the believing servant is in Paradise. A tent of pearls, thirty miles long, for the believing servant. There are people in it who cannot see each other."
"35245","(35245) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Qadamah, on the authority of Abu Imran Al-Juniy, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Qais said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Gardens of Firdaus are four: two pieces of gold, Your jewelry and your vessel and what is in them, and two pieces of silver, your jewelry and your vessel and what is in them, and nothing in between. The people are clear that they look at their Lord except the veil of pride on His face. (Bukhari 4878 and Muslim 163)"
"35246","(35246) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Fadalah, on the authority of Luqman bin Amir, on the authority of Abu Imamah, he said: I heard him say: {Gardens of Firdaus as a residence}, he said: the secret of Paradise, he said: the middle of Paradise."
"35247","(35247) Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ka’b; {Gardens of Firdaus as a sojourn}, he said: Gardens of grapes."
"35248","(35248) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The people of Paradise will enter. The jinn is in the image of Adam, as tall as he is, sixty cubits, naked, stripped, kohl-bound, thirty-three sons, Their wives are virgins, and their men are rejected."
"35249","(35249) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayd, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The palm trees of Paradise have their trunks of gold. Its vines are emeralds and rubies, and its fronds are fragrant. It brings forth fresh dates like pearls, sweeter than honey, and whiter than milk."
"35250","(35250) Shababah bin Siwar told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ziyad, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah, He narrates on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: God is astonishing at a people. He brought them in chains until He let them in. Heaven\n(Bukhari 4557, Abu Dawud 2670)"
"35251","(35251) Affan told us, he said: Suleiman bin Mughirah told us, he said: Humaid bin Hilal said: It was mentioned to us; When a man is admitted to Paradise, he will take pictures of the people of Paradise, put on their clothes, and wear their apparel, and see His wives, his servants, and his dwelling place in Paradise, so he took him as a bracelet of joy. If he should have died, he would have died. He said: It will be said: Have you seen this bracelet of your joy? It will remain for you forever."
"35252","(35252) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Thabit told us, on the authority of Anas; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, for the people of Paradise there is a market place, to which you will come every group, in which are dunes. Musk. When they went out to it, a wind would blow. Hammad said: “I think it is.” He said: “north,” so it filled their faces and their clothes. And their houses will be covered with musk, so they will increase in elegance and beauty. He said: Then they will go to their families and say to them: You have increased After us there is beauty and beauty, and they say to them: And you have increased beauty and beauty after us. (Muslim 2178, Darami 2842)"
"35253","(35253) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Misra Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: I asked Ka'b: What is the secret of the montah? He said: Sidrā, to whom the knowledge of the angels comes, and with it they find the command of God not surpassed by their knowledge. And I asked him about the garden of refuge? He said: A paradise in which there are green birds, in which the souls of the martyrs ascend."
"35254","(35254) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Khaled Al-Asadi, on the authority of Shaqiq bin Salama, on the authority of Ibn Masoud; In His saying: {And He will be brought to Hell on that day} He said: He will be brought with it led by seventy thousand reins, with each rein of seventy thousand angels. They dragged her. (Muslim 2184. Tirmidhi 2573)"
"35255","(35255) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: Hell will exhale. On the Day of Resurrection, there will be no angel brought near, nor any prophet sent, but he will fall on his knees and say: O Lord, Myself Myself."
"35256","(35256) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Malik ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Mughith ibn Sumayyah, who said: Indeed, Hell Every day you exhale, nothing remains but hearing them, except the two burdens upon them are the torment and the reckoning."
"35257","(35257) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Salman, he said: Fire is black and dark, it does not give light. burning hot coals, and its flame will not be quenched. Then he recited: {Whenever they wish to escape from it out of distress, they will be returned therein and taste the torment. The fire}"
"35258","(35258) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Al-Hudhayl, who said: The fire burned them openly. She did not leave any flesh on a bone without throwing it into it. (Tabarani 9361)"
"35259","(35259) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Sa’id Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The people of Hell called out: “Oh, what is the matter with your Lord? Let your Lord destroy us.” So he left them for forty years, then he answered them. : {Indeed, you are staying.} He said: So they said: {Get us out of it, but if we return, then indeed we are wrongdoers}. He said: So he left them like this world, then He answered them: “Be humble in it, and do not speak to me.” He said: The people did not utter a word after that, if it was anything but exhaling. And the inhale.\n(Hakim 395)"
"35260","(35260) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Malik ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Mughith ibn Sumayyah, who said: When he comes With the man taken to the Fire. It was said: Wait until We anoint you. He said: Then he will be brought with a cup of snake and lion venom, when they are brought near to the fire. In it, the meat is spread out in one place, and the bones in one place. (Abu Naim 68)"
"35261","(35261) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Sami’, on the authority of Abu Razin; {It is revealed to mankind}, He said: It is made clear to its skin until you call it blacker than the night."
"35262","(35262) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama, on the authority of Khaythama, on the authority of Abdullah; {Indeed, the hypocrites will be in the lowest depths of the Fire}. He said: In coffins with ambiguities on them."
"35263","(35263) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hubaira, on the authority of Ali, who said: The gates of Hell are one upon another. Some, starting with the bottom and filling it, so it is the lowest of the lowly, then the next to it, then the next to it, until it is filled. Fire"
"35264","(35264) Ismail bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abu Harun, on the authority of Hattan bin Abdullah, he said: Ali said: Do you know? How are the gates of Hell? They said: Yes, similar to these chapters. He said: No, but we are like this, so he described dishes, one on top of the other.\n(Tabari 14)"
"35265","(35265) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, he said: Yahya bin Abdul Rahman bin Hatib told me, On the authority of his father, he said: We sat at the Ka’b al-Ahbar in the mosque while he was speaking, then Omar came and sat on the side of the people. So he called him and said: Woe to you, Ka’b! We have frightened him, so he said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, the Fire will draw near on the Day of Resurrection. It has a loud, long exhalation, so that when it approaches and draws near, it exhales with a deep breath. God has not created any prophet, nor truthful, nor witness, unless he kneels down, falling, until every prophet, every truthful man, and every witness says: Oh God, I will not burden you. Today, except for myself. If you, Ibn al-Khattab, had the authority of seventy prophets, you would think that you would not be saved. Omar said: By God, the matter is Very strong"
"35266","(35266) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, on the authority of Umm Al-Darda’, On the authority of Abu al-Darda’, he said: Hunger will be imposed on the people of Hell, until their torment is equal to the punishment they are in. He said: So they call for help and are helped by the lost animal, which does not make him fat or free from hunger, so they call for help and are helped by food that is sufficient for him. A branch, and they will remember that they used to fill the branch with drink, so they would seek relief and be relieved of water from a bath in the water. Like dogs of iron, so when they brought it close to their faces, it shattered their faces, but when they brought it to their stomachs, it cut off what was in them. Their stomachs. He said: Then they will call: {Call upon your Lord to lighten for us a day of torment}. He said: Then they will answer: {Have you not Your messengers will come to you with clear proofs. They said, “Yes.” They said, “Then supplicate.” And the supplication of the disbelievers is only in error. He said: Then they say: They called Malik, and they called: {O Malik, may your Lord destroy us}. He said: So he answered them: {Indeed, you are staying.} He said: So they say : Call upon your Lord, for there is nothing more merciful to you than your Lord. He said: Then they say: {Our Lord, remove us from it. But if we return, then we will They are wrongdoers. He said: Then He will answer them: “Be humble in it and do not speak.” He said: Then they will despair of all good. And they are seized with woe, distress, and destruction. (Tirmidhi 2586, Darqutni 1086)"
"35267","(35267) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Raqqashi, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The people of Hell will be weeping, and they will cry until the tears run out. He said: Then they will cry blood, until it falls into Their faces are a groove, if ships were sent into it, they would drift. (Ibn Al-Mubarak 295)"
"35268","(35268) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, saying: On the authority of Salam ibn Miskin, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of Abu Moses said: The people of Hell will weep in Hell, so much so that if ships were to sink, they would sink in their tears. Then they They will weep blood after the tears, and for a similar reason they are weeping over it. (Hakim 605)"
"35269","(35269) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Indeed, the most invulnerable to the people of Hell in torment is he who has sandals and tents of fire, whose brains will boil as if The cauldron boils, he does not think that anyone is more severely tormented than him, and indeed He is the easiest to torment them. (Muslim 1964. Ahmad 274)"
"35270","(35270) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: The closest to torment of the people of Hell is a man wearing sandals whose brains boil as if it were a cauldron, his ears. Coals, and his molars are coals, and his lips are flames of fire, and the entrails of his sides come out from his feet, and the rest of them are like grain. A little in a lot of water, and it fizzes. (Abu Naim 274)"
"35271","(35271) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Zuhair bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Abi Ayyash, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The closest torment to the people of Hell will be someone shod with two sandals of fire. His brain will boil with... The heat of our soles. (Muslim 1958, Abu Awan 283)"
"35272","(35272) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, he said: Thabit narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The one who is the easiest to be punished by the people of Hell is Abu Talib, and he is wearing two sandals. Fire (Muslim 1260; Ahmad 290)"
"35273","(35273) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he greeted him while he was on the pulpit, saying: I warn you of the Fire, until one of his robes fell from his shoulders, and he was saying: I warn you of the Fire, even if it were from my place, I could hear the people of the market, or whomever God wills from among them.\n(Taalisi 792, Ahmed 268)"
"35274","(35274) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Fire complained to its Lord and said: My Lord, He has devoured part of me, so He made for it two souls: one soul in The summer, and a breath in the winter, and the severity of the cold you find in its summer, and the severity of the heat you find in the summer. Toxins (Bukhari 3260, Muslim 185)"
"35275","(35275) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murra, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah; In His saying: {We have increased for them a punishment beyond the punishment}, He said: Increase scorpions, their tails are like tall palm trees. (Abu Ali 2659)"
"35276","(35276) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, he said: I narrated on the authority of Ka`b, he said: In Hell there will be furnaces, narrow as if the spear of one of you is thrust into the earth, they will be imposed on a people according to their deeds."
"35277","(35277) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Aoun bin Abdullah bin Atba, on the authority of Abu Hariri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Hell and Heaven quarreled, and Fire said: Among the arrogant are the arrogant. And the owners of wealth, and the nobles, and the jinn said: What is the matter with me that only the weak and the needy enter me? Then God Almighty said to Paradise: You are my mercy. I may admit to you whomever I wish. And He said to Hell: You are my torment. I may punish by you whomever I wish. And both of you I will fill."
"35278","(35278) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: A neck will emerge from the Fire on the Day of Resurrection, with a tongue that can speak, and it will say: Indeed, I have been commanded to do three: I have commanded whoever places another god with God, and every tyrant and stubborn one, and mentions another letter, so he withdraws from them and throws them into The depths of hell.\n(Abu Ya’li 1141. Ahmad 40)"
"35279","(35279) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Hell has a gate, and in it are snakes like necks. Al-Bakht, and scorpions like delm mules. He said: Then the people of Hell will flee into those robes. He said: Then those serpents will take And the scorpions on their lips, moving from between the shoulder blades to the nail. He said: Nothing will save them except flight to the Fire. (Abu Naim 290)"
"35280","(35280) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Scabies will be cast upon the people of Hell. He said: Then they rubbed each other until the bones became visible. He said: Then they said: Our Lord, why has this afflicted us? He said: Then it will be said: By hurting the believers."
"35281","(35281) Yahya bin Issa told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Yahya, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: If even a drop of Zaqqum from Hell were descended on the people of the earth, it would ruin the people’s livelihood. (Bayhaqi 544, Ahmad 301)"
"35282","(35282) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a bucket of the pus of Hell were dropped from the heavens, Then the people of the earth smelled His scent, and He spoiled the world for them."
"35283","(35283) Waki’ ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Indeed, this fire of yours seeks refuge from the fire of Hell."
"35284","(35284) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Raqqashi, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If a stone equal to seven successions were cast from the edge of Hell and it would dwell therein for seventy years, without reaching its bottom.\n(Abu Ali 4103)"
"35285","(35285) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Yazid Al-Raqqashi, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, who said: The Messenger of God heard One day, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, there was a loud noise, and he said: O Gabriel, who is this? He said: A stone that was thrown from the edge of Hell seventy years ago, and now it has settled at its bottom. (Ibn Abi Al-Dunya 16)"
"35286","(35286) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Harun bin Abi Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, he said: I heard Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri says: One day we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we saw him looking gloomy, and some of them said: Messenger of God, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, why do I see you like this? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I heard something like it that I have never heard before. So Gabriel came to me and I asked him about it? He said: This is a rock that was thrown into the fire seventy years ago, and today it has stabilized. Abu Sa`id said: And what He took the life of our Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. I did not see him laughing after that day until he saw dust."
"35287","(35287) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, who said: Abdullah bin Qays narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Uqish; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Among my nation are those who exalt themselves in the Fire, even to the point of being one of its corners. Of my nation there is one who will enter Paradise through his intercession more than harm."
"35288","(35288) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning his saying {Whenever their skins are cooked, We will replace them with other skins}, he said: It has informed me that one of them will be burned in Today seventy thousand times. (Ibn Abi Al-Dunya 117)"
"35289","(35289) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Khushina, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: They will be magnified in the Fire. Until their lips become to their beds, they will be loathed, and they will wander about in the Fire."
"35290","(35290) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Yahya al-Tawil, on the authority of Abu Yahya al-Qatat, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Omar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The people of the Fire will be magnified in the Fire, until one of them becomes a person on his way. Such and such, and the tooth of one of them is like Uhud. (Muslim 2189. Ahmed 26)"
"35291","(35291) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hubayra, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The molar tooth of the infidel is in Hell. For the example of someone."
"35292","(35292) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of Yazid bin Hayyan, on the authority of Zayd bin Arqam, who said: The molar tooth of the disbeliever is in Hell like Uhud."
"35293","(35293) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hariri, he said: Ibn Masoud said: To Abu Hurairah: Do you know how thick the skin of an infidel is? Abu Hurairah said: No, and Abdullah said: The thickness of the skin of an infidel is forty-two cubits. (Tirmidhi 2577, Hakim 595)"
"35294","(35294) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, who said: Hardening the skin of the infidel Forty cubits."
"35295","(35295) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Omar used to say: Increase He mentioned fire, for its heat is intense, and its bottom is far, and its vents are iron."
"35296","(35296) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Qays, on the authority of Yunus ibn Khabab, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Indeed, in Hell There is a cloud in which are serpents like the likes of Bukhari, and scorpions like the likes of dalam mules, so the people of Hell will flee from the Fire to that robes, then snakes and scorpions will meet them, and they will take away their lips and eyes. He said: They will not seek help except By returning to the Fire, and indeed, the most painful of them is the torment of one who has sandals on the soles of his feet, from which his brains and lips are boiled. And their molars are fire, and the rest of them wave within them like a little grain in a lot of water."
"35297","(35297) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Harith, on the authority of al-Abbas ibn Abdul Muttalib; That he said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Your uncle Abu Talib, protect you, and be angry with you? He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He is in a pit of fire, and had it not been for me, he would have been in the lowest level.\n(Bukhari 6208, Ahmed 206)"
"35298","(35298) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Al-Azhar bin Sinan Al-Qurashi told us, he said: Muhammad bin Wasi’ told me, He said: I entered upon Bilal bin Abi Barda, and I said to him: O Bilal, your father told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Indeed, in Hell there is a valley called: Hellfire. God has decreed that every mighty man should dwell therein. So, O Bilal, be careful not to be among those who live there. (Darimi 2816, Abu Ali 7213)"
"35299","(35299) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Qais, on the authority of Huzayl, who said: The souls of Pharaoh’s family are in the belly of a bird. Black, you go in the morning and go to the Fire, and that is its exposure. (Tabari 24)"
"35300","(35300) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Fudayl bin Ghazwan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Zaid, who said: I have heard that there are people who have long whips and do not have mercy on people. It is said to them: Put down your whips and enter the Fire. (Abu Yali 1479)"
"35301","(35301) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Amr bin Qais; It had reached him that Omar said to Ka’b: O Ka’b, frighten us. He said: Yes, God will gather the creatures on one level. Sight will pierce them, and the supplicant will hear them, and He will be brought to Hell, and on that day it will have three exhalations, so the first exhalation: No. A tear will remain in an eye unless it flows until blood spills out. As for the second: There will not remain a single person who will not kneel. He calls out: Lord of my soul, even to his close friend Abraham. As for the third: If you had a lifetime of work, seventy years. A prophet, you will have pity, until you know which of the two groups you are from."
"35302","(35302) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak; {And they have hammers of iron}, he said: hammers."
"35303","(35303) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Sinan, who said: I heard Abdullah bin Al-Harith say: Al-Zabaniyya. Their heads are in the heavens, and their feet are on the earth. (Tabari 257)"
"35304","(35304) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Harry, he said: The fire was stoked for a thousand years until it became white, then it was stoked for a thousand years and it turned red, then it was stoked for a thousand years Then it turned black, like a dark night. (Tirmidhi 2591, Ibn Majah 4320)"
"35305","(35305) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, he said: Asbat bin Nasr narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, Abdullah said: {And He came And on that day, in Hell."
"35306","(35306) Ismail bin Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abu Raja’i, on the authority of Al-Hasan; {And another form of it is pairs} He said: colors of torment."
"35307","(35307) Yahya bin Abi Bukair told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Anas bin Malik ; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The first person to be clothed with a garment of Hell will be Iblis. He will place it on his eyebrow. And he will drag her from behind him, and his offspring behind him, and he will call: O Thaboorah, and they will call: O Thaboorah them. He said: Then it will be said to them: {Do not call upon today one destruction, but call upon many destructions}. (Ahmad 152. Tabari 18)"
"35308","(35308) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abu Salih; {to grill} He said: the meat of the legs."
"35309","(35309) Yahya bin Abi Bukair told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Laith, and Al-A’mash, on the authority of Mujahid; {to grill}, he said: grilling the parties."
"35310","(35310) Yahya bin Ubaid told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Abu Salih; {And his wealth will not avail him when he declines} He said: In Hell."
"35311","(35311) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Al-Jariri informed us, on the authority of Abu Al-Saleel, on the authority of Ghunaim bin Qays, On the authority of Abu Al-Awwam, he said: Ka’b said: Do you know what he said: “And there is not among you but those who will come to it”? They said: We did not think that it would come unless it entered. He said: He said: No, but He will bring Hell and it will be spread out for the people as if it were Hell. God’s body, until when the feet of the creatures rested on it, be righteous and ungrateful to them, a caller called to it: Take your companions. And the offspring of my companions, so she will be defeated by every guardian of hers, for she is more knowledgeable than a father about his children, and the believers will be saved innocently. Their clothes. He said: And indeed, the keeper of Hell’s treasures is the distance of a year’s journey between him. He has with him a pillar of iron. It has two prongs, with which it is repulsed, so seven hundred thousand people are thrown into Hell, or whatever God wills. (Tabari 109)"
"35312","(35312) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Ibn Maqil; {And if you had seen, when they were frightened, they did not miss it.} He said: He frightened them, but they did not miss it."
"35313","(35313) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr, who said: A great man will be brought. The Day of Resurrection is long, and it will be put in the scale, and no equivalent of your compensation will weigh in the sight of God. Then he recited: {So we will not evaluate them for them. on the Day of Resurrection by weight}"
"35314","(35314) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Nu’aym bin Misra the grammarian narrated to me, on the authority of Uyaynah bin Al-Ghusn, he said: Al-Hasan said: The shackles were not placed on the necks of the people of Hell because they have disobeyed the Lord, but when the flame is extinguished on them I threw them into the fire. He said: Then Al-Hasan flinched and fainted."
"35315","(35315) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hassan bin Abi Al-Mukhariq, on the authority of Abu Abdullah Al-Jadali, He said: I came to the Holy House, and I saw Ubadah ibn al-Samit, Abdullah ibn Amr, and Ka`b al-Ahbar talking in a house. The Holy One, he said, and his servants said: When the Day of Resurrection comes, people will be gathered in one level, and sight will pierce them. And the caller will make them hear, and God will say: {This is the day of judgment We have gathered you and the ancients, but if there is a plot against you, then they will plot} Today, neither a stubborn tyrant nor a rebellious devil will escape from me.\n He said: Then Abdullah bin Amr said: We find in the Book: That on that day a neck will emerge from the Fire, and it will go out with a neck. Even when he was among the people, he said: O people, I have been sent to three people. I know who they are. A father for his child, and from brother to brother, no burden will free you from me, and you will not hide from me the least. Another god, and every stubborn tyrant, and every rebellious devil, said: Then he will withdraw from them and throw them into the Fire before... The calculation is for forty. Husayn said: Either forty years, or forty days.\n He said: And a people will rush to Paradise, and the angels will say to them: Stand for reckoning. He said: Then they will say: By God, it is not ours. We are not workers. He said: Then God says: My servants have spoken the truth. I am more deserving of him who fulfills his covenant. Enter Paradise. He said: So they will enter Paradise forty days before the reckoning, whether he said: a year or a day."
"35316","(35316) Abdah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak; {There is no doubt that for them is the Fire, and that they are dispersed.} He said: They will be forgotten in the Fire."
"35317","(35317) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Hudhi; {And We will drive the criminals to Hell thirsty} He said: thirsty."
"35318","(35318) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak; {And We will drive the criminals to Hell, thirsty.} He said: thirsty."
"35319","(35319) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, he said: His leaders said: I heard Abu Nadhri narrating, on the authority of Samarra bin Jundub; He heard the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Indeed, among them is he whom the Fire will take to his ankles, and of them Some of them will be taken to the knees by the Fire, and some of them will be taken to the ground, and some of them will be taken to the ground. His collarbone\n(Muslim 2185. Ahmad 10)"
"35320","(35320) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Fudail bin Ghazwan narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad Al-Rasibi, on the authority of Bishr bin Asim, He said: Omar ibn al-Khattab wrote a letter to Bishr ibn Asim, and he said: I have no need of it, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him, saying: The rulers will be brought to them on the Day of Resurrection, and they will stop on the bridge of Hell, so whoever is obedient to God God took him with His right hand until He saved him, and whoever is disobedient to God, the bridge will be pierced into a valley of fire. He was inflamed with fear. He said: Then Omar sent to Salman and Abu Dharr, and he said to Abu Dharr: You heard this hadith from the Messenger of God. May God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes, by God, and after the valley there is another valley of fire. He said: He asked Salman, but he did not tell him anything, so Omar said: Who? Did he take it with what was in it? Abu Dharr said: He whose nose and eyes are ennobled by God, and whose cheeks are lowered to the ground."
"35321","(35321) Ishaq bin Sulaiman al-Razi told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Salih, he said: On the Day of Resurrection, those to whom messengers were sent will be judged, and God will admit whoever obeys Him to Paradise, and He will admit whoever obeys Him. He disobeyed him, and there will remain a people of the children, and those who perished during the period, and those whose intellect was defeated, then God, Blessed be He, will say And God Almighty: Indeed, you have seen that I only admitted to Paradise whoever obeyed Me, and I admitted to Hell whoever disobeyed Me, and I command you to You will enter this Fire, and a neck will emerge for them from it. Whoever enters it will be saved, and whoever retreats will not enter it. It was his death."
"35322","(35322) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, who said: When Abu Talib fell ill, they said to him: Send to This is your nephew, and he will bring you a cluster from his garden, perhaps he will cure you with it. He said: Then the Messenger and Abu Bakr came. He was sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr said: God has forbidden them to the unbelievers. (Ibn Abi Hatim 8536)"
"35323","(35323) Affan bin Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, he said: Al-Azraq bin Qays narrated to us, he said: A man narrated to me. From Banu Tamim, he said: We were with Abu Al-Awwam, and he recited these verses: “On her are nineteen days.” So he said: What do you say? Nineteen thousand angels, or nineteen thousand angels? He said: So I said: No, but nineteen angels. He said: And from where do you know that? So I said, because God says: {And We have not made their number except as a trial for those who disbelieve}. He said: You are right, in the hand of every king appointed from It is an iron with two prongs, so he strikes the blow, and seventy thousand angels are swept away with it, whatever is between the shoulders of each angel. Among them is such-and-such and such-and-such."
"35324","(35324) Shababa told us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, who said: I have been informed that the family of Hell is a punishment: He has a sole of fire from which his brain boils, and his heart screams, and he says: No one will be tortured more severely than he has been tortured. With it"
"35325","(35325) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; {So damned are the Companions of the Blaze} He said: A valley in Hell."
"35326","(35326) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah; {And therein they are like one who grinds} He said: As the head is combed to the top. (Ibn Jarir 18)"
"35327","(35327) Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Abi Ayyub, who said: I heard a cyclist, Abu al-Samh, say: I heard Abu Al-Haytham, saying: I heard Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: On the unbeliever there are ninety-nine dragons in his grave, which will bite him and bite him until the Hour comes, even if only one of them is a dragon. He blew into the earth, which brought forth green. (Ahmad 38, Abu Ali 1324)"
"35328","(35328) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ashhab, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: {Indeed, her torment was love} He said: They knew. Every debtor separates from his debtor, except the debtor of Hell."
"35329","(35329) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Hasan; {Then a wall was set between them, with a door on the inside of which is mercy} He said: The Garden, {And the torment appearing before it} He said: The Fire."
"35330","(35330) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: He sent Moses, And Aaron, the son of Aaron, with an offering, and they said: Fire has consumed him, and they lied, so God sent fire upon them. So I ate them, so God revealed to them: This is what I do to my friends, so what about my enemies?"
"35331","(35331) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Haram bin Hayyan used to say: I have never seen its fugitives sleep like fire, nor have its seekers slept like heaven."
"35332","(35332) Abd al-A’la ibn Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn al-Mughirah narrated to me, on the authority of Suleiman bin Amr bin Ubaid Al-Awari, one of the Banu Layth, and he was in the custody of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri said: I heard him say: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: The path will be placed between... My appearance is Hell, upon him is a comb like the comb of a lion, then he will pass through the people, a Muslim will be saved, and he will be struck by it and then will be saved. And it is confined and reversed.\n When God has finished judging His servants, the believers will visit men who were in this world and would perform their prayers. And they pay their zakat, and observe their fast, and perform their Hajj, and fight their battle, and they say: Yes, our Lord. Servants of Your servants, they were with us in this world, performing our prayers, paying our zakat, and observing our fasts. And they attack us, but we do not see them? He said: Then He will say: Go to the Fire, and whoever you find therein, take him out of it, and they will find that the Fire has taken them in due measure. Their deeds, some of them took it as far as their feet, and some of them took it as far as half of their shins, and some She took him up to his knees, and among them was some whom she embroidered, and among them was some whom she took up to his breasts, and among them was some. She took him to his neck, and did not cover his face, so they cast them into the water of life.\n It was said: O Messenger of God, what is the water of life? He said: The people of Paradise will be washed, and they will sprout as seed sprouts in the scum of a stream, then the prophets will intercede for those who He bore witness that there is no god but God sincerely, and he said: Then God will be compassionate with His mercy upon whoever is in it, so he will not leave it. Therein is a servant who has a grain of faith in his heart unless he takes him out of it. (Ibn Majah 4280. Ahmed 11)"
"35333","(35333) Affan told us, he said: Saeed bin Zaid told us, he said: I heard Abu Sulaiman Al-Asri, he said: Uqba told me. Ibn Subhaban, who said: I heard Abu Bakra, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: People will be carried on the Sirat on the day Resurrection, then you will lie with them on both sides of the path like you will lie on a bed in the Fire. He said: Then God will be compassionate in His mercy upon whom He wills. He said: Then the angels and the prophets and the martyrs are given permission to intercede, so they intercede and are brought out, and they intercede and are brought out. So they will intercede and bring out whoever has in his heart the weight of an atom of faith. (Ahmad 43. Bazzar 3671)"
"35334","(35334) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: The path is on a bridge. Hell they will return to."
"35335","(35335) Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Thabit Al-Bunani, on the authority of Abu Uthman Al-Nadhi, on the authority of Salman Al-Farisi, he said: The path is laid and it has a limit like the limit of a razor, so the angels say: Our Lord, who will You allow for this? So he says: I may reward whomever I wish."
"35336","(35336) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shimr, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: He comes The people will be brought to the scales on the Day of Resurrection, and they will dispute with Him in the utmost intensity."
"35337","(35337) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Ali bin Ata’, he said: Tamim bin Ghaylan bin Salamah narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, that he said: Where have you been since the day Hell was brought? It has blocked what is between those who fail, and it was said: You will not enter. Heaven until you go through Hell? If you have light with you, the path will be straight for you, then, by God, you have been saved and have been guided. And if you do not have light, some people will cling to you. The hooks of Hell, or its dogs, or its youths, for, by God, you have been repulsed and adrift."
"35338","(35338) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr, he said: The path is refuted. His place is like the sharp edge of a sword, and the angels are with them, and the prophets are standing and saying around Him: Our Lord. He went up, he went up, there was a scratched person, someone stuck in the fire, and someone who was saved and saved. (Bukhari 8061, Muslim 163)"
"35339","(35339) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: When God created creation, He wrote with His own hand upon Himself: Indeed, Your mercy prevails over Your wrath.\n(Tirmidhi 3543, Ahmad 433)"
"35340","(35340) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salamah, on the authority of Al-Haytham ibn Hanash, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: If you had not sinned, God would have sought refuge with people who sin and He would have forgiven them."
"35341","(35341) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Suwayd, on the authority of Hudhayfah; If God Almighty had not touched a creation that disobeyed in the past, He would have created a creation that disobeyed, so He would forgive them on the Day of Resurrection."
"35342","(35342) Al-Mu’alla bin Mansour narrated to us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Muhammad bin Qays, on the authority of Abu Sarmah, on the authority of Abu Ayoub said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If you had not sinned, God would have brought a people who sinned and would forgive them.\n(Muslim 2105. Tirmidhi 3539)"
"35343","(35343) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Salman, he said: When Ibrahim was shown the kingdom of the heavens and the earth. He saw a servant committing an indecency, so he supplicated against him, and he was destroyed. Then he saw another, so he supplicated against him, and he was destroyed. Then he saw Another supplicated for him, and he was destroyed. Then God said: Bring down My servant, and do not let My servants perish."
"35344","(35344) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Khaythamah, on the authority of Nu’aym bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Ruba’i, on the authority of Hudhayf He said: The believers do not need intercession, but it is for sinners."
"35345","(35345) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: God has given power to the one who sins by the night to repent by the day, and to the one who sins by the day to He repents at night, until the sun rises from the west. (Muslim 2113. An-Nasa’i 11180)"
"35346","(35346) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Abu Wael, who said: God will protect the servant on the Day of Resurrection. He will cover it with his hand and say: Do you know what is here? He says: Yes, O Lord. Then he says: I bear witness to you that I have forgiven you."
"35347","(35347) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Salman, who said: God created a hundred merciful people. So He made it a mercy among the creatures. Every mercy is greater than what is between the heavens and the earth. Because of it, the parents show compassion to Him. They gave birth to her, and by her birds and wild animals drink water. When the Day of Resurrection comes, God will take them out of all creation. So He made it and the ninety-nine for the righteous. That is His saying: {My mercy encompasses all things, so I will record it for those who They fear}"
"35348","(35348) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Indeed, on the day He created the heavens and the earth, He created the heavens and the earth as a mercy, and He made part of the earth a mercy, so it is compassionate. Parents are against their children, and animals are against one another, and He delayed ninety-nine times until the Day of Resurrection, so if On the Day of Resurrection, He will have perfected her with this mercy a hundred times. (Ibn Majah 4294. Ahmed 55)"
"35349","(35349) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Jami’ bin Shaddad, on the authority of Mughith bin Sumayyah, who said: There was a man among Before you, he used to commit sins, so he thought one day and said: Oh God, forgive me, so he was forgiven."
"35350","(35350) Yahya bin Issa told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Sa’d the client of Talha, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: There is a man among us, it is said to him: Al-Kafl, who commits sins. A woman liked him, so he gave her fifty A dinar. When the man sat on her seat, she trembled, and he said to her: What do you have? She said: This is something I have never done. He said: Are you worried about this sin, and I have been doing it for so-and-so since? By God, I will never disobey God. He said: Then he died that night, and when the Children of Israel rose in the morning, they said: Who will pray for so-and-so? Ibn Omar said: He was found written on his door: May God forgive the guarantor.\n(Tirmidhi 2496. Ibn Hibban 387)"
"35351","(35351) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Mughith bin Sumayyah, he said: He was a man who worshiped In his fasting place for about sixty years, he said: Then it rained for the people, so he came out of his fasting place and saw the treachery and the greenery, so he said: If only I went down and walked and looked, and he did so. While he was walking, a woman met him and he spoke to her, and she continued to speak to him until He fell upon her, saying: He put a bag that was on him, in which was a loaf of bread, and the water came down to wash him, and his time came, and a beggar passed by. So he motioned to the loaf of bread and he took it, and the man died, and his deeds over sixty years were weighed, so his sin outweighed his deeds, then he was placed The loaf won, so he was forgiven. (Ibn Hibban 378)"
"35352","(35352) Omar bin Saad told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salamah, on the authority of Abu Al-Za’ara’, on the authority of Abdullah; Indeed, Abdullah was a monk in fasting for sixty years, and a woman came and descended beside him, and he descended to her. So he stayed there for six nights, then he fell into his possession, and he fled, so he came to a mosque, and he took refuge in it, and he stayed for three days without food. Something, then a loaf of bread was brought, he broke half of it, and gave half to a man on his right, and gave to another on his left. So God sent the angel of death to him and took his soul, so the work of sixty years was placed on his palm, and the bad deeds were placed on his palm. Enough, so the bad was outweighed. Then the loaf was brought and he outweighed the bad."
"35353","(35353) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: Abu Uthman narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Burda, he said: When he attended Abu Musa said: O my sons, remember the owner of the loaf of bread. He said: There was a man who was worshiping in a hermitage. I saw him. He said: Seventy years, and it does not descend except on the day of a Uhud. He said: So it descended on the day of a Uhud. He said: So it was like it, or Satan appeared in it. He appointed a woman, and he was with her for seven days and seven nights. He said: Then his cover was removed from the man, and he came out repentant. And every time he took a step, he prayed and prostrated, saying: Then the night took him to a shop with twelve poor people, so he overtook him. Exhausted, he threw himself between two of them.\n Then there was a monk who would send to them every night with loaves of bread, and he would give each person a loaf of bread. Then the owner of the loaf came. So he gave each person a loaf, and he passed by the one who came out repentant, and he thought that he was poor, so he gave him a loaf, and he said What is left to the owner of the loaf: Why didn’t you give me my loaf? I had no need of it. He said: Do you think I can hold it for you? Ask: Did I give any of you two loaves of bread? They said: No. He said: I am withholding from you, and by God I will not give you anything tonight. He said: So the penitent went to the loaf that he had given. Then he gave it to the man who had been left behind, and the repentant person became dead. He said: The seventy years were weighed against the seven nights, but they were not weighed. He said: The loaf was weighed over the seven nights. He said: The loaf was weighed. Abu Musa said: O my sons, remember the owner of the loaf."
"35354","(35354) Abu Muawiyah and Ya`li told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Al-Kanood, he said: Abdullah passed by Ali, a storyteller, while he was mentioning the Fire, said: O Reminder, do not despair of the people: {O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of May God have mercy on you."
"35355","(35355) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Musa ibn Uqba, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Ka`b, he said: When The angels saw the children of Adam, and they did not sin. They said: O Lord, they sin. He said: If you were like them, you would do it. As they do, they chose two angels from among you. He said: So they chose Harut and Marut. Then He, Blessed and Most High, said to them: Indeed There is a messenger between me and the people, and there is no one between me and you. Do not associate anything with Me, nor steal, nor commit adultery. Abdullah said: Ka’b said: They had not completed that day before they fell into what had been forbidden to them. (Ahmad 134. Ibn Hibban 6186)"
"35356","(35356) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Sufyan Al-Yashkuri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud said: A man who had committed a sin came to him and asked him about it, so he did so and went to the people to tell them, so she came He saw it from Abdullah, and when the man looked at Thuraq, he said: This is the time for your concern. You have not come to ask me about it. Paradise has seven gates, each of which opens and closes except the door of repentance. An angel is appointed over it, so work hard and do not despair."
"35357","(35357) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Ali ibn Mas’ad, who said: His leaders narrated to us, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, who said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Every son of Adam is a sinner, and the best of sinners are those who repent. (Tirmidhi 2499. Ahmad 198)"
"35358","(35358) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: Indeed, when God Almighty cursed Iblis, He asked him to look at it, so he looked at it until the Day of Judgment. He said: By Your glory, I will not leave the stomach or the heart of the son of Adam as long as it is in it. The spirit. He said: By Your glory, I will not withhold repentance from him as long as the spirit is in him."
"35359","(35359) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, who said: In the Psalms of David was written: Indeed, I, God, There is no god but Me, the King of kings. The hearts of kings are in My hand. Whatever people obey me, I have appointed kings over them. Mercy, and whatever people commit disobedience, I have appointed kings as a vengeance upon them. Do not concern yourselves with the curse of kings. And do not repent to them, but repent to Me, and I will make their hearts kinder to you."
"35360","(35360) Abdullah bin Numayr and Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qais, on the authority of Abdullah He said: While a man from among those before you was among an unbelieving people, and there were righteous people among them, he said: As long as I am in this disbelief, I will come to this righteous town and be a man from its people. So he set off. Then death overtook him, and the angel and Satan protested against him. This man said: I have more right to him. And this man said: I He was worthy of it, when God sent some of His soldiers to them, and said to them: Measure what is between the two cities, and I gave them both. He is closer to it, so he is from its family. So they measured what was between them and found him closer to the righteous city, so he was Some of them"
"35361","(35361) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam bin Yahya, who said: His leaders narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Siddiq Al-Naji, On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, he said: I will not tell you except what I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I heard it. My ears were aware, and my heart was aware, that a servant killed ninety-nine people, then repentance was presented to him, so he asked who knew the people of The land? He was directed to a man and he came to him and said: I killed ninety-nine people, so do I have any repentance? He said: After killing ninety-nine people? He said: Then his sword was drawn out and he killed him, and he completed a hundred with it.\n Then repentance was presented to him, and he asked who the most knowledgeable people on earth were? He was directed to a man and he came to him and said: I killed a hundred people, so is there any way I can repent? He said: Who will come between you and repentance? Get out of the evil town that you are in and to the good town, the town of such-and-such, and worship Your Lord is in it. He said: So he went out seeking the righteous city, and his appointed time was presented to him on the way. He said: So he settled in it. Your angels of mercy, and your angels of torment, and Iblis said: I have more right to him, for he has never disobeyed me before. He said: Then the angels of mercy said: He came out repentant.\n Hammam said: Humaid al-Tawil told me, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah al-Muzani, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, who said: So God sent He was given a kingdom, so they disputed over him, then he returned to the hadith of his leaders.\n He said: See which of the two towns was closer to him, so join him there.\n He said: Al-Hasan told me, he said: When he knew of death, he seized himself, so God brought the righteous life closer to him, and distanced it from it. The evil city, join it with the righteous people of the village. (Bukhari 3470, Muslim 2118)"
"35362","(35362) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam ibn Yahya, he said: His qatadā narrated to us, on the authority of Safwan ibn Mahrez, He said: I was taking Abdullah bin Omar by the hand, and a man came to him and said: How did you hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? What does he say about najwa? He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: God will bring the believer close to him on the Day of Resurrection until he humbles himself. He is wearing a shroud, covering him from the people, and he says: O my servant, do you know the sin of such-and-such? He says: Yes, O Lord. Then he says: O my servant, do you know the sin of such-and-such? So he says: Yes, O Lord, even when he confesses his sins to him, and sees in himself that he has perished, he says: Indeed, he has I have concealed it for you in this world, and I have forgiven you today. Then a record of his good deeds will be brought. As for the unbelievers and the hypocrites, So the witnesses say: {These are they who lied against their Lord. Indeed, the curse of God is upon the wrongdoers}"
"35363","(35363) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Aoun, who said: He tells him about forgiveness before sin: {May God forgive Why did you give them permission?"
"35364","(35364) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: A man went out from his village to visit a brother of his in another village. He said: So God provided for him. An angel, so he sat on his way and said: Where do you want? He said: I want a brother of mine to visit for the sake of God in this village. He said: Did he have any of the blessings that he had brought up upon you? He said: No, but I loved him for the sake of God. He said: For I am the messenger of your Lord to you. Indeed, He has loved you as you loved him.\n(Bukhari 350, Muslim 38)"
"35365","(35365) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Urwah bin Amir, who said: The man will be presented to him. His sins, so he passes by the sin and says: I was afraid of you, so God forgives him."
"35366","(35366) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata bin Yasar, He said: Indeed, for those who are masked, there will be a prison on which people will step on their necks on the Day of Resurrection."
"35367","Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us: Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Absi Al-Kufi, may God have mercy on him.\n(35367) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, he said: It was Jesus. The son of Maryam, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not change lunch for dinner, nor dinner for lunch, and he used to say: Indeed, with every day He provided for him, and he used to wear hair, eat trees, and sleep wherever he was in the evening."
"35368","(35368) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Al-Ala bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Shimr bin Atiyya, he said: He said: Isa bin Maryam Peace be upon him: Eat wild herbs, drink pure water, and escape from this world unscathed."
"35369","(35369) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Salih, referring to Jesus, son of Mary, peace be upon him, who said: He said: To its companions: Make mosques as residences, and homes as homes, and escape from this world in peace, and eat of wild herbs. He said: Al-A’mash added to it: “And drink of the turbid water.”"
"35370","(35370) Abbad bin Al-Awwam narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of a man who narrated to him, who said: The disciples said to `Isa bin Maryam: What do you eat? He said: Barley bread. They said: What are you wearing? He said: Wool. They said: What does it cover? He said: The earth. They said: All of this is severe. He said: You will not attain the kingdom of heaven until you achieve this upon pleasure. Or He said: upon What a shame"
"35371","(35371) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yaqoub, he said: Jesus bin Maryam said: No. If you talk a lot without mentioning God, then your hearts will be hardened, for a hard heart is far from God, but you do not know. Look at the sins of your servants as if you were lords, and look at your sins as if you were slaves, for people are but two men: Afflicted and recovering, so have mercy on those who are afflicted, and thank God for their recovery."
"35372","(35372) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamiya, he said: A woman passed by Isa, and she said: Blessed is the womb. He carried you, and breastfed you, and said: Jesus: Rather, blessed is he who reads the Qur’an and follows what is in it."
"35373","(35372) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salem, who said: Jesus, son of Mary, peace be upon him, said: Fear God and work for God, and do not work for your bellies, and look at these birds that neither reap nor sow, may God provide for them. If you claim that your bellies are larger than the bellies of birds, then these cows and donkeys neither plow nor sow. May God provide for them. And beware of the bounty of this world, for it is an abomination in the sight of God."
"35374","(35374) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Ala, on the authority of Khaythamiya, he said: Jesus, son of Mary, peace be upon him, said: Blessed are you. For the son of a believer, blessed be he. They will be preserved after him. And Khaythamiah recited: {And their fathers were righteous}"
"35375","(35375) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Thumamah, he said: He said: The disciples: O Jesus, what is sincerity to God? He said: If a man does a job without wanting anyone to praise him for it, and the one who is sincere to God is the one who begins with God’s rights. Before the rights of people, he gives priority to the rights of God over the rights of people, and if two matters are presented to him: one for this world, and the other for the Hereafter, he begins with a command. The Hereafter before the affairs of this world."
"35376","(35376) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Al-Mughiriya, on the authority of Thabit Al-Bunani, who said: A man said to Isa bin Maryam, peace be upon her: If you took a donkey and rode it for your needs, he would say: I am more honorable to God than that He make anything for me. They keep me busy with it."
"35377","(35377) Muhammad bin Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, who said: A man narrated to me before the skulls from People of the mosques, he said: I was informed that Jesus, peace be upon him, used to say: Oh God, I have become unable to obtain for myself what I hope for, nor I can pay for her what I hate, and what is good becomes in someone else’s hand, and I become dependent on what I have earned, and there is no poor person poorer. From me, so do not let my calamity affect my religion, and do not make this world my greatest concern, and do not impose over me those who do not have mercy on me."
"35378","(35378) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamiya, who said: Issa Ibn Maryam, peace be upon him, said to a man from His companions, and he was rich, said: He gave his money in charity, so he disliked that, so Jesus bin Maryam, peace be upon him, said: Because of the severity of what enters The rich, the jinn."
"35379","(35379) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Shibl bin Abbad narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Abi Sulayman, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, said: Mary, peace be upon her, said: When Jesus and I were alone, he spoke to me and I spoke to him. If a person distracts me from it, he blares in my stomach while I hear him."
"35380","(35380) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Shibl bin Abbad narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: Jesus, peace be upon him, did not speak except with the signs that he spoke until he reached the point of Boys"
"35381","(35381) Muhammad bin Abi Ubaidah told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr bin Murah, on the authority of Salem, he said: He said Jesus, son of Mary, peace be upon him: Indeed, Moses forbade you from adultery, and I forbade you from it, and I forbade you from speaking Yourselves by disobedience, for the likeness of that is like someone who stabs a log. If he does not break it, it will carve it. It weakens it, or like smoke in a house, if it does not burn it, it changes its color and stinks."
"35382","(35382) Abd al-Salam ibn Harb told us, on the authority of Khalaf ibn Hawshab, who said: Issa ibn Maryam, peace be upon him, said to the dialoguers: O salt of the earth, do not spoil it, for if something spoils, nothing can fix it except salt, and know that you have two qualities: laughter from Nothing strange, and the morning dawns without being awake."
"35383","(35383) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: Abu Al-Ashhab informed us, on the authority of Maimun ibn Ustad, he said: Issa ibn Maryam, peace be upon her: O community of disciples, take the mosques as residences, and take your homes as guest houses. You have a place in the world. You are only passersby."
"35384","(35384) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamiyah, who said: Jesus, son of Mary, peace be upon him, used to make Food for his companions. He said: Then he would rise up over them and then say: Thus, do with the Qur’a."
"35385","(35385) Affan bin Muslim narrated to us, Abu Awani narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that Jesus is the son of Maryam Peace be upon him, whenever the Sa’a was mentioned in his presence, he would shout and say: The son of Mary should not have the Sa’a mentioned in his presence except He shouted, or said: Silence."
"35386","(35386) Affan told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Dirar bin Murra Abu Sinan told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Hudhayl, he said: When Yahya saw Jesus, peace be upon him, he said to him: Advise me, he said: Do not get angry, he said: I cannot He said: Do not acquire money. He said: Perhaps."
"35387","(35387) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Abbas Al-Ammi, who said: It has reached me that David the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He used to say in his supplication: Glory be to You, O God, You are my Lord, You have exalted above Your Throne, and You have placed the fear of You upon those in the heavens and the earth, so the closest your creation is to you in station, the more fearful of you they are, and whoever does not fear you does not know, or what is your judgment. Whoever does not obey your command."
"35388","(35388) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abdullah Al-Jadlili, he said: What David raised his head to the heavens until he died."
"35389","(35389) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: When David committed the sin, it was only His sin, because when he saw her, he commanded her and isolated her and did not approach her, so the two opponents came to him and entered the mihrab, so when He saw them and stood up to them and said: Leave me. He did not bring you to me. He said: So they said: We only speak to you in a simple way. This is my brother who has ninety-nine female ewes, and he has one male female, and he wants to take it from you. So David said: By God, it is more deserving of it to be broken than from this to that, meaning from his nose to his chest. He said: So the man said: This is what David did, and David knew that he meant that, and he knew his sin, so he fell down and prostrated for forty days. And forty nights, and his sin was written on his hand, and he looked at it so that he would not even neglect it. Herbs grew around him from his tears and covered his head, and after forty days he called out: The forehead was sore and the eyes were frozen. And David did not return to him in his sin for anything, so they were called: hungry and you will be fed, or naked and you will be clothed, or oppressed. So he became Christian. He said: Then he loved, loved, and lost all the herbs he had when he did not mention his sin, and then he was forgiven. So if It was the Day of Resurrection, and his Lord said to him: Be before me. He said: O Lord, my sin is my sin, so God said: Be. Behind me, and he says: O Lord, my sin is my sin. He said: So he says to him: Take my feet, so he takes his feet."
"35390","(35390) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Mis`ar, on the authority of Ali ibn al-Aqmar, on the authority of Abu al-Ahwas, who said: The two adversaries entered upon Dawud. One of them is holding the head of its owner."
"35391","(35391) Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: It was only the temptation of David. The sight"
"35392","(35392) Affan narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed Al-Jariri, that David said: O Gabriel, Which night is best? He said: I do not know except that I know that the throne shakes from magic."
"35393","(35393) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Khaled Al-Ruba’i, who said: I was informed that the Conqueror of the Psalms is the one who is called: Psalms of David: The beginning of wisdom is the fear of the Lord."
"35394","(35394) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Al-Fazari, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: God revealed to David, peace be upon him: Say to the oppressors, “Do not mention me,” for it is my right to remember those who He reminded me, and his mention of them meant that I cursed them."
"35395","(35395) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, he said: God revealed to David Peace be upon him, to love me and my loved ones, and to love me to my servants. He said: O Lord, I love you and I love your loved ones. So how can I make you beloved to your servants? He said: Mention me to them, for they will not remember anything but good from me."
"35396","(35396) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ibn Abza, who said: David, the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Peace be upon you: Ayoub was the most forgiving of people, the most patient of people, and the most restrained from his anger."
"35397","(35397) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Mubarak told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He was David the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, says: Oh God, there is no sickness that makes me suffer, nor health that makes me forget, but it is in between."
"35398","(35398) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sulaym, on the authority of Thabit al-Bunani, on the authority of Safwan ibn Mahrez, who said: It was To David, the Prophet of God, peace be upon him. The punishment of God, the most severe of the punishments of God, nor the most severe. He said: One day he remembered her in an assembly, and he was overcome by weeping until he got up."
"35399","(35399) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sulaym, on the authority of Thabit, who said: David, the Prophet of God, peace be upon him, was He mentioned God’s punishment, and his limbs were dislocated, and nothing could tighten them except captivity. So when he mentioned God’s mercy, they were withdrawn."
"35400","(35400) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, he said: Alqamiya bin Marthad narrated to me, on the authority of Buraydah, he said: If The weeping of the people of the earth was equal to the weeping of David, but it was not equal to him."
"35401","(35401) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, who said: It was in the Psalms of David, “Indeed, I am God, there is no god but I, the King of kings, have the hearts of kings in my hand. Whatever people are obedient, I have placed kings as mercy upon them. And whoever people commit disobedience, upon whom kings have imposed vengeance, do not occupy yourselves with the curse of kings, and do not repent. To them, repent to Me, and I will sympathize with the hearts of kings towards you."
"35402","(35402) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, he said: Dawud said The Prophet, peace be upon him: A fool’s speech in a people’s club is like one who sings at the head of the dead."
"35403","(35403) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Al-Ahnaf bin Qays, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: David, peace be upon him, said: O Lord, the children of Israel are asking you about Abraham and Isaac. And Jacob, so make me, O Lord, a fourth for them. He said: Then God revealed to him: O David, Abraham was thrown into the fire. Because of me, he was patient in my cause, and that was a calamity that did not afflict you, and indeed, Isaac shed his blood for my cause, so he was patient, and that was a calamity that did not befall you. And indeed, I took his beloved Jacob until his eyes became bright, so he was patient, and that was a calamity that did not befall you."
"35404","(35404) Mu’awiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Mu’sab, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ka’b, he said: Whenever a fasting person broke his fast, he would face the Qiblah and say: O God, save me from every calamity that descended from the heavens to the earth in the night, three times. And when the visor of the sun rose, he said: O God, make for me an arrow in every good deed that has been sent down from the heavens three times. He said: So it was said to him, and he said: The call of David, so soften your tongues therewith and make your hearts aware of it."
"35405","(35405) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abza, who said: Dawud said: Yes. Helper in debt or wealth."
"35406","(35406) Qubaysah narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Dawud said: Oh My Lord, my life has been long, my years have grown, and my pillar has become weak. Then God revealed to him: O David, blessed is he who has a long life and does good deeds."
"35407","(35407) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamiyah, he said: Suleiman bin Dawud said: We have tried all kinds of living. It is soft and strong, and we found that the following is sufficient for it."
"35408","(35408) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythama, who said: The Angel of Death came to Suleiman bin Dawud. And he was a friend of his, so Solomon said to him: Why do you come to the Ahlul Bayt and arrest them all and leave the Ahlul Bayt? Beside them, do not seize any of them. He said: I do not know what I will seize from, but I will be under the throne and you will be thrown to me. A certificate containing names."
"35409","(35409) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythama, who said: The Angel of Death entered Solomon and made He saw a man who was sitting with him and kept looking at him. When he left, the man said: Who is this? He said: This is the angel of death. He said: I saw him looking at me as if he wanted me. He said: What do you want? He said: I want you to carry me on the wind until You will throw me into India. He said: So he called for the wind and carried it upon her, and she threw him into India. Then the angel of death, Solomon, came. He said: You used to keep looking at a man you were sitting with. He said: I used to admire him. I was ordered to arrest him in India, and he... With you"
"35410","(35410) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: Sulayman bin Dawud, peace be upon him, to his son: O my son, just as a peg enters between two stones, so sin enters between them. The seller and the buyer."
"35411","(35411) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Ifriqi, on the authority of Salman bin Amir Al-Shaabani, who said: Did you see Suleiman, and what He was given in his kingdom, for he did not raise his head to the heavens until God took him, out of humility before Him."
"35412","(35412) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Malik ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Suleiman ibn Dawud was The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, does not speak out of reverence for him. He said: The afternoon prayer had passed and no one could bear to speak to him."
"35413","(35413) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, On the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, he said: Ibn Sulaiman bin Dawud died, and he was greatly distressed until it became known about him. His judgment came, and one day two angels appeared before the adversaries, and one of them said: I have sown the seed of your calamity when it becomes severe. And he reaped the bitterness of this man and spoiled it, so he said to the other: What you say, and he said: He is right. She took the road and came to a fortified arm and looked. Right and left, then, behold, the road was on it, so I took on it. So Solomon said to the other: Why did you sow on the road, did you not know that it would be taken? People on the road? He said: O Solomon, why do you grieve for your son when you know that you are dead and that the people’s path is to the Hereafter?"
"35414","(35414) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Mis`ar narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd al-Ammi, on the authority of Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, that Suleiman bin Dawud He went out with the people to draw water, then he passed by an ant lying on its back, raising its legs to the heavens, and it was saying: Oh God. We are a creation among your creation. We are not in need of your provision. Either you give us water or you destroy us. So Solomon said to the people: Go back, for you have been watered by the supplication of others."
"35415","(35415) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, saying: It was mentioned on the authority of some of the prophets that, he said: Oh God, do not burden me with a request that You have not decreed for me, and whatever provision You have decreed for me, give me it with ease and well-being from You. And rectify me with what you have reconciled the righteous, for it is you who rectify the righteous."
"35416","(35416) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, that a prophet from God’s prophets, He said: Who are those who destroyed you? Who are those in the shadow of your throne? He said: They are the innocent ones, the pure ones. Their hearts, those who love one another for the sake of My Majesty, those who, when they are mentioned, I am reminded of them, and when I am mentioned, they are reminded of Me, those who seek salvation. Ablution for the bad things, and for those who are entrusted with my love as a child is entrusted with people, and those who come to Me. Remember just as a bird takes refuge in its nest, and those who become angry at my mahrams when they are deemed lawful, just as a tiger becomes angry when they are declared unlawful, Or he said: war."
"35417","(35417) Affan narrated to us, saying: Al-Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that David the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Oh God, I I ask you from my brothers, friends, neighbors, and acquaintances, who, if I forget, remind me, and if I remember, help me, and I seek refuge in You from Friends, brothers, neighbors, and those who sit with me - if I forget, they do not remind me, and if I remember, they do not help me."
"35418","(35418) Affan bin Muslim narrated to us, saying: Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that David the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Oh God, let no sickness make me suffer, nor health make me forget, but in between."
"35419","(35419) Affan told us, he said: Mubarak told us, he said: I heard Al-Hasan say: Ayoub, peace be upon him, was always afflicted with him. A misfortune. He said: Oh God, You have taken and You have given whatever You keep. My soul remains, I praise You for your good afflictions."
"35420","(35420) Affan told us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman al-Dab’i told us, on the authority of Thabit al-Bunani, he said: We have been informed that David the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He used to perform the prayers on his household: on his wives and children, and no hour of the night would come. And the Fire will come except when a man from the family of David is standing and praying, so these verses have become a sign for them: {Work, the family of David, with gratitude, and few of My servants The thankful}"
"35421","(35421) Affan told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Abdul Karim told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that David the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said: My God, if every hair of mine had two tongues to glorify You night and day, We would not have decreed of Your blessings. Ali"
"35422","(35422) Affan told us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Al-Ja’ad Abu Uthman told us, he said: We were informed that Dawud said: My God, what is the reward for him whose eyes overflow with fear of You? He said: His reward is that I will make him safe on the day of the greatest terror."
"35423","(35423) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Malik bin Mughal, on the authority of Al-Hasan Abi Yunus, on the authority of Harun bin Ri’ab, He said: I was told by Ibn Hanzala, the Prophet’s scribe, may God bless him and grant him peace, that God revealed to Moses: “Your people have adorned themselves.” Their mosques and ruined their hearts, and they became fat as pigs are fattened on the day of their slaughter, and if I looked at them, I cursed them. I will not answer their supplications, nor will I grant them their requests."
"35424","(35424) Suleiman bin Harb told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, that David May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he prostrated until green trees sprouted around him from his tears. Then God revealed to him: O David, what do you want? You want me to increase your money, your children, and your lifespan? He said: O Lord, if you return to me, I will forgive him."
"35425","(35425) Abu Asama told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwah told us, on the authority of his father, that Moses, peace be upon him, said: My Lord, tell me who is the most honorable of your creation. He said: The one who hastens to his desires as the eagle hastens to his desires, and the one who charges My righteous servants as he is charged. The one who treats people, and the one who gets angry when his mahrams are violated, is as angry as a tiger is for himself, for when a tiger is angry, most people do not care. Or did they say?"
"35426","(35426) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid, On the authority of his father, he said: Moses, peace be upon him, said: O Lord, You mentioned Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, why did You give that to them? He said: Abraham did nothing wrong with me except that he chose me, and Isaac was serious about himself and was better than anyone else. Jacob was not afflicted with any calamity but his good opinion of me increased."
"35427","(35427) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Qaboos, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Moses said: O Lord, which of Your servants I love most. To You. He said: The one who remembers Me the most. He said: O Lord, which of Your servants is richest? He said: He is satisfied with what You have given him. He said: Which Lord, which Lord of Your servants is most wise? He said: The one who judges himself in the same way he judges people."
"35428","(35428) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Marwan Al-Aslami, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ka’b He said: Moses said: Which Lord, are you near, so I will speak to you, or far away, so I will call you? He said: O Moses, I am sitting with the one who mentioned me. He said: O Lord, we are always in a state to glorify you, or to glorify you. We remind you of it. He said: And whatever it is. He said: Impurity and defecation. He said: O Moses, remember Me in every state."
"35429","(35429) Mu’awiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salam, he said: Moses said to his Lord: O Lord, what gratitude should be due to You? He said: Your tongue remains moist. Of My remembrance, he said: O Lord, I am in a state in order to remind You of sexual impurity, defecation, and spitting of water. Other than ablution. He said: Yes. He said: How should I say? He said: Say: Glory be to You and praise be to You. There is no god but You, so protect me from harm. Glory be to You. And by Your praise, there is no god but You, so protect me from harm."
"35430","(35430) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Khalaf ibn Hawshab, he said: Gabriel, peace be upon him, entered, or He said: The king was upon Yusuf, peace be upon him, while he was in prison. Then he said: Oh, the fragrant king, the one with clean clothes, Tell me about Jacob, or what Jacob did? He said: His sight has gone. He said: How sad has he become? He said: The grief of seventy bereaved people. He said: What is his reward? He said: The reward of a hundred witnesses."
"35431","(35431) Abu Usama told us, saying: Al-Ahwas ibn Hakim informed me, on the authority of Zuhayr ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Yazid bin Misra, who had read the books, said: God revealed what He revealed to Moses, peace be upon him, that he loved My devotionals \n To those who walk the earth with sincere advice, and those who walk on their feet to Friday prayers, and those who seek forgiveness at the pre-dawn meal. Those are the people who, if I wanted to afflict the people of the earth with torment, then I saw them, I would withhold My torment, and indeed the most hateful of My servants to Me. The one who imitates the believer’s bad deeds and does not imitate his good deeds."
"35432","(35432) Yahya bin Issa told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Luqman, peace be upon him, was a black slave. Big-lipped, cleft-footed."
"35433","(35433) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sharik, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulkiya, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, who said: He said: Luqman to his son: O my son, do not like a man whose arms are full of blood, for in the eyes of God he is a killer who will never die."
"35434","(35434) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ashhab, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Wasi’, that Luqman used to say to his son: My son, fear God, do not let people see that you are fearful while your heart is ungodly."
"35435","(35435) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ashhab, he said: Khalid bin Thabit Al-Ruba’i narrated to me, Ja’far said: And it was He reads the books. Luqman was an Ethiopian slave, a carpenter, and his master said to him: Slay a sheep for him. He said: So he slaughtered He had a tea, so he said: Bring me some of it, fresh and clean, so he brought it to him with the tongue and the heart, he said: And he said: There was nothing in it. Better than these two? He said: No, but he remained silent about him as long as he remained silent. Then he said: Slaughter a sheep for him. So he slaughtered a sheep for him. He said: Throw away the most impure meat, chewed. So he threw the tongue and the heart, and said to him: I told you, bring me the best of it, so you brought me the tongue and the heart, then I told you: bring it. It was two pieces of vileness, so it dropped the tongue and the heart, and he said: There is nothing better than these if they are good, and nothing more vile than these two. If they are malicious"
"35436","(35436) Shababah told us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Sayyar, he said: It was said to Luqman: What is your wisdom? He said: I do not ask about what is sufficient for me, nor do I burden myself with what does not concern me."
"35437","(35437) Yazeed bin Harun told us, he said: Ismail al-Makki and Mubarak told us, on the authority of al-Hasan, he said: Luqman said To his son: O my son, I carried the fire and iron, and I did not see anything heavier than a bad neighbor, and I tasted bitterness in all of it, and I did not see anything bitter. From arrogance."
"35438","(35438) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hatim bin Wardan narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Moses asked a group of work, and it was said to him: See what you want the people to accompany you with, so accompany the people with it."
"35439","(35439) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Sufyan bin Aslam Al-Muqqari told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, He said: Jacob's eyebrows had fallen on his eyes, and he was raising them with rags, so it was said to him: This has not reached you. He said: Long time and many sorrows, so God revealed to him: O Jacob, you have accused me. He said: O Lord, my sin. She has sinned, so forgive her."
"35440","(35440) Sa’id bin Shurahbil narrated to us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, who said: I sat one day To Abu Idris Al-Khawlani while he was narrating, and he said: Shall I not tell you who had the best food among people? When he saw that the people were looking at him, he said: Yahya bin Zakariya was the best of people in food. He only ate with... The beast hated to mix with people in their lives."
"35441","(35441) Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awani narrated to us, he said: Habib bin Abi Amri narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr. On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Moses, peace be upon him, said: (My Lord, indeed, whatever You have sent down to me is good, I am poor.) And He is the most generous of His creation. Ali, he lacked the ability to crack a date, and he was so hungry that his stomach stuck to his back."
"35442","(35442) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Uthman bin Abdullah bin Aws, who said: He was a prophet. Among the prophets he prays: Oh God, protect me with what you protect a child. (Ibn Al-Mubarak 1515)"
"35443","(35443) Mu’awiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of some of the Madanis, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, he said: The world presented itself to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: I do not want you. She said: If you do not want me, it will want me. Other than you"
"35444","(35444) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mas’udi, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, on the authority of Abdullah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: My parable and the parable of this world is that of a rider. He said in the shade of a tree in One summer day, then he went and left her. (Ahmad 441, Abu Ali 5207)"
"35445","(35445) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took He greeted me with my hand, or with part of my body, and said to me: O Abdullah bin Omar, be a stranger, or a passerby, and prepare yourself. Concerning the people of the graves, Mujahid said: Abdullah bin Omar said to me: When you wake up in the morning, do not talk to yourself about the evening, and when you arrive in the evening, do not talk to yourself about the evening. Talk to yourself in the morning, and take from your life before your death, and from your health before your illness, for you do not know what your name will be tomorrow. (Ahmad 41. Ibn Al-Mubarak 13)"
"35446","(35446) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Al-Safar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: The Messenger of God passed by me. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, while we were making amends for someone special for us. He said: What is this? I said: It is reserved for us and we will set it right. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I do not see the matter being more urgent than that. (Abu Dawud 5194, Tirmidhi 2335)"
"35447","(35447) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qays, who said: I heard a brother of Bani Imtaridh Fahr says: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: By God, the world in the Hereafter is only as one of you puts it. His finger is in the right hand, then he raises it and sees with what it will return. (Muslim 2193. Tirmidhi 2323)"
"35448","(35448) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Al-Mustabidh, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Similar to it except that he did not say it, then he raised it. (Ahmed 228)"
"35449","(35449) Abdul bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: It was a pillow. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who reclines on him, is made of human beings stuffed with fiber. (Muslim 1450; Abu Dawud 4143)"
"35450","(35450) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Yahya bin Ja’adah, who said: Some of the Companions of the Messenger of God returned. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Khabab, and they said: Give good news to Abu Abdullah, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, the basin, and he said: How is this? This is the lowest and highest part of the House, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us: Only one of you is sufficient for The world is as much as the rider’s provision. (Tabarani 3695, Abu Nu’aym 360)"
"35451","(35451) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, who said: Muawiyah entered upon his maternal uncle, Abu Hashim bin Utba. He returned and cried, and Muawiyah said to him: What makes you cry, my uncle? Is it pain that disgusts you or concern for the world? So he said : All no, but the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made a covenant with us and said: O Abu Hashim, perhaps it will overtake you. Wealth is given to people, for the collection of wealth is sufficient for you as a servant and a vehicle in the path of God, so he showed me that you have collected it. (Tirmidhi 2327. Ahmad 443)"
"35452","(35452) Hussein bin Ali Al-Ju’fi narrated to us, on the authority of Zayed, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Samurah bin Sahm He said: Muawiyah visited his maternal uncle and mentioned something like the hadith of Abu Muawiyah. He said: Sufyan al-Thawri added to it with his chain of transmission. : I wish there were barren surrounding us. (Ibn Majah 4103. Ahmed 290)"
"35453","(35453) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of his scholars, he said: Saad bin Abi Waqqas entered On Salman’s return, he cried. He said: Then Saad said to him: What makes you cry, Abu Abdullah? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died. Peace be upon him, and he was satisfied with you, and you met him and visited the basin. Salman said: But I do not cry out of fear of death, nor do I cry. Out of concern for the world, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a covenant with us and said: Let the message of one of you be like Al-Rakib added, he said: And around these are the lions. He said: And around him are only pillows, eyelids and rain, so Saad said: Oh Abu Abdullah, make a covenant with us that we will follow after you. He said: O Saad, remember God in your presence when you are concerned. And at your judgment when you rule, and at your hand when you swear. (Ibn Saad 90)"
"35454","(35454) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Mu’awiyah an-Nadhari narrated to us, on the authority of Nashhal, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Muzahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, He said: Abdullah said: If the people of knowledge had preserved their knowledge and placed it among their people, they would have prevailed with it over the people of their time. But they gave it up to the people of the world to gain something from their world by it, but they were unfair to its people. I heard your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, says: Whoever makes worries one single concern, God will suffice him for his hereafter worries, and whoever is divided into worries and circumstances In this world, God does not care which valley He falls into. (Musnad 345)"
"35455","(35455) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: When faith enters the heart, the heart opens up to it and is cheerful, and remembers these verses: {So whoever God desires to He will open his chest to Islam. They said: O Messenger of God, is there any sign by which he will be recognized? He said: Yes, turning to the abode of eternity, avoiding the abode of deception, and preparing for death before death. (Ibn Al-Mubarak 315)"
"35456","(35456) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Amr bin Qays, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abdullah bin Miswar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited: {So whoever God desires to guide you will open his chest to Islam} and they said: Oh. Messenger of God, and what is this explanation? He said: A light that is thrown into the heart and the heart expands to it. He said: So it was said: So is there any reason for that? A sign by which he is known. He said: Yes. It was said: What is it? He said: Returning to the abode of eternity and avoiding the abode of deception. And preparing for death before meeting death. (Ibn Jarir 27)"
"35457","(35457) Abu Muawiyah and Ali told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, on the authority of Abu Dharr, who said: The Prophet said to him May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Look, O Abu Dharr, who is the most handsome man you see in the mosque. He said: I looked and saw a man wearing a robe. So I said: This. He said: Then he said: Look at the most humble man you will see in the mosque. He said: Then I looked and saw a man with good morals. So I said: This, he said: This is better than filling the earth with this. (Ahmed 157)"
"35458","(35458) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Mushir, on the authority of Kharsha, on the authority of Abu Dhar, on the authority of the Prophet May God bless him and grant him peace. (Ahmad 1571, Ibn Hibban 681)"
"35459","(35459) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Faroukh, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Muzahim, who said: He came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And a man greeted him and said: O Messenger of God, who is the most abundant of people in this world? He said: He who does not forget the graves and the calamities, and leaves behind the best He adorned the world, and preferred what endures over what perishes, and did not count tomorrow as one of his days, and he counted himself among the dead. (Bayhaqi 10515)"
"35460","(35460) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far bin Burqan, on the authority of Ziyad bin Jarrah, on the authority of Amr bin Maimun, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He said to a man: Take advantage of five things before five things: your life before your death, your free time before your occupation, and your wealth. Before your poverty, your youth before your old age, and your health before your illness. (Abu Nu’aym 148. Ibn Al-Mubarak 2)"
"35461","(35461) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Aban bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Sabah bin Muhammad Al-Ahmasi, on the authority of Mara Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Be ashamed before God as men should be. He said: We said: We Let us be ashamed, O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Not that, but he who is ashamed before God deserves modesty. Let him guard the head and what it contains, and let him guard the stomach and what it contains, and let him remember death and calamity, and whoever desires the latter should leave it. The world is adorned, so whoever does that has become truly ashamed before God. (Tirmidhi 2458. Ahmad 387)"
"35462","(35462) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had A she-camel, and it is said to her, that a group of women should not outrun her. Then a Bedouin sitting on a camel came and overtook her, making it difficult for the Muslims. They said: O Messenger of God. The thorns preceded, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is God’s right that nothing of it should be raised unless He places it. , meaning the world."
"35463","(35463) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir, he said: I heard him say: Are you not in food? And drink whatever you want. I saw your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and whatever dung he found he could fill his stomach with.\n(Muslim 35. Ahmad 24)"
"35464","(35464) Abu Asama told us, he said: Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, on the authority of Abu Barza. He said, “I went to see Aisha, and she brought out for me a thick garment made in Yemen and a garment made of this cloth, which is made in Yemen.” You call her Al-Mulbadi, and she swore to me: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would die in them. (Bukhari 5818 and Muslim 1649)"
"35465","(35465) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amara, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Muammar, on the authority of a man from Banu Salem, or he understood, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was brought with a gift, so he looked and did not find anything to make it In it, he said: Put it in the bottom, for he is only a slave. He eats as a slave eats, and drinks as a slave drinks. If the world weighed in the eyes of God a wing of compensation, He would not give any disbeliever to drink water from it. (Ibn Abi Al-Dunya 365)"
"35466","(35466) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, he said: Abu Salamah told us, he said: Muadh bin Jabal said: A. The Messenger of God, he advised me, he said: Worship God as if you see Him, and prepare yourself from the dead, and remember God at every stone. And trees, and if you do evil, do good alongside it: secret for secret and public for public. (Hanad 1092)"
"35467","(35467) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, he said: Abu Salamah told us, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was May God bless him and grant him peace. He says: Mention frequently the one who destroys pleasures, meaning death."
"35468","(35468) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Peace be upon him, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Mention often the one who destroys pleasures, meaning Death (Ahmed 2921 Hakim 321)"
"35469","(35469) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Alqamah ibn Marthad, on the authority of Ibn Sabit, he said: A man was mentioned. He was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they praised him very well. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: How is he mentioned? To die, but he did not mention that about him, so he said: It is not as you remember. (Abu Naim 299)"
"35470","(35470) Ishaq bin Sulaiman al-Razi told us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far al-Razi, on the authority of al-Rabi’, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Death is sufficient to increase one’s life in this world and make one desire the Hereafter."
"35471","(35471) Hatem bin Wardan narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: If God had willed He would have made you rich, all of you, not one poor among you. And if God had willed, He would have made you poor, all of you, none of you rich, but afflicted. each other. (Bayhaqi 10072)"
"35472","(35472) Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Raja’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Malik, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: We were with the Prophet. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him during his funeral. When he reached the grave, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, knelt down on the grave and said: So I turned around and faced him. He said: He wept until the soil became wet, then he said: My brothers, for something like this, let the workers work. So prepare.\n(Ibn Majah 4195. Ahmed 294)"
"35473","(35473) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khalid narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, he said: I was informed Ibn Masoud said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O people, there is nothing that will bring you closer to And it will keep you away from the Fire, except that I have commanded you to do so, and there is nothing that will bring you closer to the Fire and keep you away from the Fire. Except that I have forbidden you from it, and the Faithful Spirit has breathed into my soul. Indeed, not a soul dies until it has received its provision. So fear God and be diligent in your request, and do not let the lack of provision force you to seek it by disobeying God, for He will not obtain what He With God except by obedience to Him. (Ibn Majah 2144)"
"35474","(35474) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned The people of the trenches seek refuge in God from the severity of calamity."
"35475","(35475) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khalid narrated to us, saying: My brother Numan narrated to me, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Saad, on the authority of Hafsa bint Omar, who said: She said to her father: O Commander of the Faithful, what is wrong with you if you wear a softer garment than yours? And you ate something better than yours. God has conquered the earth for you and made sustenance abundant for you. He said: I will dispute with you against yourself. Do you not know what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, faced with the hardship of life? And he reminded her of something of what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to meet until it made her cry. He said: I told you. I had two companions who took a path other than theirs, and if I took a path other than theirs, I would take a path other than theirs. Then, by God, I That I may share with them a life similar to theirs, that perhaps I may live with them their easy life, meaning his companion, the Prophet. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him and Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him. (Abdullah bin Hamid 25. Ibn Al-Mubarak 574)"
"35476","(35476) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to me, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Shurayh narrated to me, saying: Shurahbil ibn Yazid narrated to me. Al-Maafiri said: I heard Muhammad bin Hadi Al-Sadfi saying: I heard Abdullah bin Amr saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: The most hypocritical of my nation are its reciters. (Ahmad 1751, Ibn Al-Mubarak 451)"
"35477","(35477) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who raised him up: {Indeed, my guardians By God, there is no fear for them, nor do they grieve.} God remembers seeing them. (Tabarani 12325. Ibn Al-Mubarak 217)"
"35478","(35478) Khaled bin Mukhlid narrated to us, saying: Sa’id bin Muslim bin Banak narrated to me, saying: I heard Amer bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, he said: Awf bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Aisha. Beware of despicable deeds, for they have a seeker from God. (Ibn Majah 4243. Ahmad 70)"
"35479","(35479) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mu’awiyah bin Suwayd, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The strongest bonds of faith are love for God and hatred for God."
"35480","(35480) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Muwarriq Al-Ijli, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited: {The deity of you is multiplication until you visit the graves} He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You do not get any of your wealth except what you eat. So you wore it out, or you wore it and it wore out, or you gave in charity and you spent it. (Muslim 2273. Tirmidhi 2342)"
"35481","(35481) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: More severe. There are three deeds: remembering God in every situation, being fair to yourself, and consoling oneself with money.\n(Ibn Al-Mubarak 744)"
"35482","(35482) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God does not accept The work of a servant until he is satisfied with him. (Hannad 1124)"
"35483","(35483) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his followers, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to He recited: {And when We took from the prophets their covenant, and from you and from Noah} He said: He began with me in goodness, and I was the last of them in it. Resurrection"
"35484","(35484) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Assign yourself as many deeds as you can bear, for none of you knows the fate of your life."
"35485","(35485) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: It has informed me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He said: No servant spent forty days of serenity without the springs of wisdom appearing from his heart on his tongue."
"35486","(35486) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Amr narrated to us, saying: Safwan bin Sulaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Labid, he said: When this Surah was revealed to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: graves} until he reached {Then you will be asked that Day about bliss} They said: O Messenger of God, about what bliss shall we be asked? Rather, they are the two lions: Water and dates, and our swords are on our necks and the enemy is present, so what blessing should we ask about? He said: That will be it.\n(Ahmad 429, Hanad 768)"
"35487","(35487) Abdou bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Al-Ifriqi, on the authority of Muslim Al-Qurashi, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: I heard him say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If a servant does good and God inflicts calamity upon him, then God desires To purify him. (Bayhaqi 9790, Hanad 401)"
"35488","(35488) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ifriqi, on the authority of Saad bin Masoud, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Poverty is more beautiful to the believer than a beautiful excuse on the cheek of a horse. (Ibn Al-Mubarak 568)"
"35489","(35489) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was And peace be upon him, the servants took him until he came out upon the people as if he were a worn-out stone. And in the morning the people came, and it was said: O Messenger of God. Has not God forgiven you? He said: Shall I not be a grateful servant? (Bukhari 4837. Muslim 2172)"
"35490","(35490) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: God only admits to Paradise he who hopes for it, and He spares the Fire only he who fears it, and God only has mercy on he who Have mercy on him.\n(Ahmed 159)"
"35491","(35491) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Amir, he said: And perhaps he said: Our companions said, on the authority of Abu Dharr, He said: My friend advised me to do seven things: to love the poor, to get close to them, to look at those below me, and not to I look to those above me, and I extend my kinship even if it deprives me, and I multiply there is no power or strength except in God, and I I speak only the truth, and that you do not blame me for God’s sake, and that I do not ask the people for anything. (Muslim 1609. Ibn Majah 3180)"
"35492","(35492) Ismail bin Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ate. He and some of his Companions ate some barley bread that had not been sifted with meat, and they drank from a stream, and he said: This is A food of bliss, about which you will be asked on the Day of Resurrection."
"35493","(35493) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ali bin Ali bin Rifa’i, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He greeted him on his way, and he camped in a deserted and barren place, and he ordered his companions to disembark. He said: Then he ordered them to gather, so the man made He brings the small to the small, the great to the great, and the little to the little, until they are gathered together in great blackness, and he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: These are like your deeds, O children of Adam, in good and evil."
"35494","(35494) Abu Khalid and Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The Prophet mentioned his prayers. May God bless him and grant him peace: {On the Day when people rise up before the Lord of the Worlds} He said: They will be imprisoned until the discharge reaches their ears.\n(Bukhari 31. Muslim 2196)"
"35495","(35495) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, who said: My father said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God is with The tongue of every speaker, so let a servant see what he says. (Abu Naim 160)"
"35496","(35496) Abdou bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Saad Al-Tai, that he was informed that the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No believer feeds a hungry believer except that God has fed him from the fruits of the garden, and no believer has He gives a thirsty believer to drink except that God gives him something to drink of sealed nectar, and no believer covers a naked believer except that God covers him with Greens of Paradise (Tirmidhi 2449. Ahmad 13)"
"35497","(35497) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Abi Muslim, on the authority of Salih Abi Al-Khalil, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was not seen. May God bless him and grant him peace, laughing or smiling since it was revealed: “Is it then that you marvel and laugh at this hadith?” (Waki` 36)"
"35498","(35498) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sa’id bin Abi Hind, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: There are two blessings that many people are deprived of: free time and good health. (Bukhari 6412 and Tirmidhi 2304)"
"35499","(35499) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Asama bin Zaid, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Ask God for useful knowledge, and seek refuge in God from knowledge that is of no benefit."
"35500","(35,500) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ziyad bin Fayyad, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: I do not command you to be priests and monks."
"35501","(35501) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God does not He accepts the work of a servant until he is satisfied with him."
"35502","(35502) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Knowledge Two knowledge: knowledge in the heart, that is beneficial knowledge, and knowledge on the tongue, that is God’s proof upon His servants."
"35503","(35503) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Muslim al-Tahan, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Ja`far al-Madaini. He raised him up and said: What a marvel of all that he believes in the abode of eternity while striving for the abode of deception. Oh, what a marvel of all. For the arrogant and proud one, but he was created from your sperm, then he is returned as a dead body, and in the middle of that he does not know what will be done to him."
"35504","(35504) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He greeted Hajj on a saddle, and he led him forward and said: At your service. Indeed, the life of the Hereafter is the life of the Hereafter."
"35505","(35505) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of a man from Jinnah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And he said: The best thing a believer is given is good character, and the worst thing a man is given is a bad heart in beautiful images."
"35506","(35506) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: When Mu’adh came to Yemen, he addressed the people. So he thanked God and praised him, and said: I am the messenger of the Messenger of God to you, that you worship God and do not associate anything with Him, and that you establish Prayer and pay zakat, but it is Allah alone and the Garden and the Fire. Resurrection, so there is no coming, and eternity, so there is no death.\n(Ibn Al-Mubarak 1566, Hakim 83)"
"35507","(35507) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Islam began as something strange and will return to the way it began, so blessed are the strangers. It was said: And who are the strangers? He said: The conflict is between tribes. (Tirmidhi 2429. Ahmad 398)"
"35508","(35508) Affan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Al-Ala narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his father. Hariri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The religion began as something strange and will return to what it was, so blessed are you. For strangers\n(Muslim 1301, Ibn Majah 3986)"
"35509","(35509) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Al-Mughiriya, or Ibn Abi Al-Mughirah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Blessed are the strangers. It was said: And among the strangers. He said: My people. They make amends when people are corrupt."
"35510","(35510) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Islam began as something strange, and it will return as it began, so blessed are the strangers."
"35511","(35511) Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Ubad Allah ibn Umar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: If one of you dies, his seat will be offered to him in the morning and evening. If he is one of the people of Paradise, then The people of Paradise, and if he is from the people of Hell, then he is from the people of Hell, and it will be said to him: This is your seat until God resurrects you on the Day of Resurrection. Resurrection\n(Bukhari 6515. Muslim 2199)"
"35512","(35512) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, during his illness in which he died: I did not do the gold. I said: I have it, O Messenger of God. He said: Bring it. With it, I brought it to him, and it was between five and nine, so he put it on his palm, and he said with it, then he said: What Muhammad thought because of her that if he met God while this was with him, he would spend on her, O Aisha. (Ahmad 86. Ibn Hibban 715)"
"35513","(35513) Hussein bin Ali and Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Zayed, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Raba’i, On the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon me and he was looking good, so I thought that he was one of the He changed, so I said: O Messenger of God, I see you have a good face, is there anything wrong with you? He said: No, but I forgot the seven dinars that we brought yesterday in the bed room, so I spent the night without dividing them. (Ahmad 293. Ibn Hibban 5160)"
"35514","(35514) Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubair narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Saeed bin Abi Hussein Al-Makki, he said: He narrated to me. Abdullah bin Abi Mulkah, on the authority of Uqba bin Al-Harith, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left the prayer. The afternoon was fast, and the people were amazed at his speed, so he went out to them and recognized what was on their faces, and said: You mentioned righteousness in The house is with us, so I was afraid that he would spend the night with us, so I ordered him to share it with him. (Bukhari 751, Ahmed 8)"
"35515","(35515) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Fudail Ibn Ghazwan, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. He came to Fatima and found a curtain at her door, but he did not enter. He said: He rarely entered unless he started with her, so he came. Ali saw her orphaned and said: What is the matter with you? She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to me but did not enter upon me. Then Ali came to him and said: O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Fatimah was upset with her because you came to her but she did not enter. Ali, and he said: I am not with the world, or I am not with the number. He said: So he went to Fatima and informed her of the words of the Messenger of God. May God bless him and grant him peace. She said: Tell the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: What do you command me to do? He said: Tell her: Let her send it to the children of so-and-so. (Bukhari 2413 and Abu Dawud 4147)"
"35516","(35516) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to the house of His daughter Fatima, and he saw a curtain spread, so he came back and said: Then Ali came to him and said: Did I not tell you that you came to your daughter but she did not enter? He said: So he said: Have I not seen her covering her house with spending for the sake of God? Then it was said to Al-Hasan: And what was that covering? He said: A screen. A Bedouin, its price is four dirhams. She used to spread it at the back of the house."
"35517","(35517) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It was the price of the robes of the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He gave six salams and the like."
"35518","(35518) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Abi Labiba, on the authority of Sa`d, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: The best provision is that which is sufficient and the best is hidden remembrance."
"35519","(35519) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Ammar bin Qaqa’, on the authority of Abu Zur’i bin Amr bin Jarir, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Oh God, make the sustenance of the family of Muhammad sustenance.\n(Muslim 730 and Bukhari 6460)"
"35520","(35520) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shimr, on the authority of Mughirah bin Sa’d Al-Akhram, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not take the weak for the sake of the world. Abdullah said: For some rats. What is in the city? (Tirmidhi 2328 and Ahmad 377)"
"35521","(35521) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Zakaria bin Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin As'ad bin Zurarah, that Ibn Ka'b bin Malik narrated to him, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: What Hungry wolves sent among the sheep, spoiling them due to a person’s desire for money and honor for his religion. (Tirmidhi 2376 and Ahmad 456)"
"35522","(35522) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Iyad bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id. Al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said while he was on the pulpit: The thing I fear most for you is what will come out. God is from the plant of the earth, or the flower of the world. Then a man stood up and said: O Messenger of God, does good bring evil to you? So he remained silent. So much so that we thought that it would descend upon him and he was covered with puddles and sweat. Then he said: Where is the questioner? He did not want anything but good, so he said: Indeed Goodness only comes with goodness, but the world is green and sweet. Whenever the spring grows, it kills with despair, or it destroys Except for the one who eats vegetables, she eats until when her loins are full, she faces the sun and it sets, then she urinates, then she urinates and urinates, from He takes money according to his right, he will be blessed for it, and whoever takes money wrongly is like one who eats and is not satisfied. (Bukhari 14651 Muslim 727)"
"35523","(35523) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Omar bin Kathir, on the authority of Ubaid Sanut, On the authority of Khawla, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: The world is green and sweet, so whoever takes it as it deserves will be blessed. He is in it, and there is a Lord who is delving into the wealth of God and the wealth of His Messenger. Hell is for him on the Day of Resurrection. (Bukhari 3118 and Tirmidhi 2374)"
"35524","(35524) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah and Sa’id, on the authority of Hakim bin Hazzam, who said: I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he gave me, then I asked him and he gave me, then I asked him and he gave me, then he said: This money is green and sweet, so whoever takes it willingly will be blessed with it, and whoever takes it out of goodwill will not He will be blessed for it, and he is like someone who eats and is not satisfied, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand. (Bukhari 6441 and Muslim 717)"
"35525","(35525) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Ma’bud al-Jinni, on the authority of Mu’awiyah, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: This money is sweet and green, so whoever takes it as he deserves it will be blessed. Therein"
"35526","(35526) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Wahhab, on the authority of Abu Dharr, who said: A man and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose He, peace and blessings be upon him, was delivering a sermon, and he said: O Messenger of God, the hyena has eaten us. He said: So the people pushed him until he fell, then he got up again and called. With his voice, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned to him and said: I fear for you because of this that you will be injured. The world is upon you in abundance. I wish my nation did not wear gold. So I said to Zaid: What is a hyena? He said: The Sunnah.\n(Ahmad 1520 Bazzar 3984)"
"35527","(35527) Abu Muawiyah, Ibn Numayr and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Ma’roor bin Suwayd, on the authority of Abu Dharr, He said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was sitting in the shade of the Kaaba, and when he saw you, he said: They are the losers. By the Lord of the Kaaba, I came and sat down but did not dare to stand up, so I said: O Messenger of God, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, whoever they are. He said: They are the ones who have the most wealth, except for those who say such-and-such about wealth from before him and from behind him and from his right. And to the left of it. (Muslim 2864, Bazzar 3993)"
"35528","(35528) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Musa ibn Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Shall I not give you good news, O poor people, that the poor believers will enter Paradise before Their wealth is in half a day, five hundred years. (Ibn Majah 4124)"
"35529","(35529) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abi Nadhrah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mawla, on the authority of Buraydah Al-Aslami, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: A servant in this world is sufficient for one of you. And a compound. \n(Ahmad 2360, Darmi 2718)"
"35530","(35530) Muhammad bin Musaab narrated to us, he said: Al-Awza’i narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed by a dead person whose family had met him, and he said: When the world ends, it is easier for God than This is for his family. (Ahmad 329, Abu Ali 2586)"
"35531","(35531) Ghandar told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Layla speaking, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rabi`a, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was on a journey, when he saw an outcast sheep, and he said: Do you see? This is easy for her family. They said: Yes. He said: This world is easier for God than this for his family. (Nasa’i 1629. Ahmad 336)"
"35532","(35532) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed by He greeted a dead sheep and said: Why do you see what these people threw? They said: O Messenger of God, and will they benefit from it? She died, and he said: For the demise of this world is easier for God than this for its people. (Bukhari 962 and Muslim 2273)"
"35533","(35533) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: The poor believers will enter the jinn before the rich, on half the day of the fifth of the year. \n(Tirmidhi 2353. Ahmad 296)"
"35534","(35534) Affan told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, he said: Musa bin Anas told me, he said: I heard Anas say: The Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and cry much.\n(Muslim 1832, Ibn Majah 4191)"
"35535","(35535) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hatim bin Abi Saghira, on the authority of Ibn Abi Maliki, on the authority of Al-Qasim, he said: Aisha said: I said: O Messenger of God, how will the people be gathered on the Day of Resurrection? He said: Naked and barefoot. I said: And the women. He said: And the women. I said: O Messenger of God, so why should we be ashamed? He said: The matter is too severe to be seen. each other to each other.\n(Bukhari 6527. Muslim 2194)"
"35536","(35536) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, delivers a sermon and says: Indeed, you will meet God on foot, barefoot, naked and uncircumcised. (Bukhari 2524, Muslim 2194)"
"35537","(35537) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Al-Walid bin Juma’ told us, on the authority of Abu Tufayl, on the authority of Hudhayfah bin Asid, he said: Abu Dharr said: O people, speak, and do not swear, for the truthful and trustworthy one told me that the people will be gathered on the day There will be three groups of people standing: a group of people who are clothed and riding, a group that is walking and running, and a group that you will be drawn with. The angels on their faces. He said: We said: As for these two, we know them. What are those who walk and strive? He said: God casts calamity on the back until there is no back left until a man is given the garden that pleases the person on the outside. The book does not find it. (Ahmad 144, Bazzar 3891)"
"35538","(35538) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Mugheerah ibn Al-Nu’man, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave us an exhortation, and said: You will be gathered before God, barefoot and naked. We initiated the first creation - We will restore it as a promise upon Us: Indeed, We will do it.} So the first of the creatures to be cast in the garment of Abraham, the Khalil of the Most Gracious, said: Then a group of you will be taken to the north, and I will say: O Lord, my companions. It will be said: You do not know what they did after you. They have not ceased to be apostates, so I say as the righteous servant said: {And I was a witness over them} to His saying: {The Mighty, the Wise}"
"35539","(35539) Ahmad bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Wahib, he said: Abdullah bin Tawus narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his father. Harry, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The people will be gathered in three ways, willing and hoping, and two. On a camel and three on a camel. (Bukhari 6522. Muslim 2195)"
"35540","(35540) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulkiya, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Whoever is held accountable on the Day of Resurrection will be punished. I said: Didn’t God say: {He will certainly be given an easy reckoning} He said: That is not the account, but that is the presentation. Whoever is given the account on the Day of Resurrection will be tortured. (Muslim 2204, Ahmed 27)"
"35541","(35541) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Thabit told us, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Peace and blessings of God be upon him: He said: He will bring the person who has been most severely afflicted in this world among the people of Paradise, and God will say: Dye him. He dipped his hair in Paradise, and he dipped his hair there once, and God says: O son of Adam, have you ever seen evil or anything? You hate him, and he says: No, by Your glory, I have never seen anything that he hated. Then he will be brought with the most affluent people in this world. People of Hell. He will say: Dye him once in Hell. Then he will be dipped in it and say: O son of Adam, have you ever seen a stone? An eye and he says: No, by your glory I have never seen anything good.\n(Muslim 2162 and Ibn Majah 4321)"
"35542","(35542) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, he said: Ja’far bin Ziyad narrated to us, on the authority of Musa al-Jinni, on the authority of a man from Thaqif, On the authority of Anas, he said: I was serving the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said to him one day: Do you have anything to feed us? I said: Yes. O Messenger of God, leftover food from yesterday. He said: Did I not prohibit you from leaving today’s food for tomorrow? (Ahmed 198)"
"35543","(35543) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God was not satisfied. May God bless him and grant him peace for three consecutive days of whole wheat bread until he set off on his way. (Bukhari 5416 and Muslim 2281)"
"35544","(35544) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Al-Qasim, he said: Aisha said: If we We will stay for a month, or half a month, and no fire will enter our house for a lamp or for anything else. So I said: What were you doing? You live. She said: With the two lions: water and dates. We had neighbors from the Ansar, may God reward them, who were mourning, so perhaps They sent to us from Albania."
"35545","(35545) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of some of the Medinas, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, he said: The world presented itself to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: I do not want you. She said: If you do not want me, it will want me. Other than you"
"35546","(35546) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr ibn Qays, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Virtue Knowledge is better than the virtue of worship, and the foundation of your religion is piety."
"35547","(35547) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Fadl, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I said: O Messenger of God, Will you remember your family on the Day of Resurrection? He said: As for three things: at the Book, at the Balance, and at the Path. \n(Abu Dawud 4722. Ahmed 101)"
"35548","(35548) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Baz ibn Hakim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: I said: O Messenger of God Where do you command me? He said: Here, and he said with his hand towards the Levant. You will be gathered, foot and mounted, and you will be gathered on Your faces\n(Ibn Majah 2536. Tabarani 969)"
"35549","(35549) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Harun bin Abi Waki’, on the authority of his father, he said: When this was revealed The verse {Today I have perfected for you your religion} He said: The day of the greatest Hajj. He said: Then Omar cried, and the Messenger of God said to him, “Pray.” May God bless him and grant him peace: What makes you cry? He said: O Messenger of God, it made me cry that we were increasing our religion. As for when He was perfect, for nothing was ever perfect without being incomplete. He said: You are right. (Tiberius 80)"
"35550","(35550) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There are no two drops more beloved to God than a drop of water for His sake, or a drop of tears falling from the eyes of a man standing in the middle of The night is from the fear of God, and there are no two doses more beloved to God than a sad and painful dose that its companion received with good patience. And consolation, or a dose of anger that was felt upon her. (Ibn Al-Mubarak 672, Abdul Razzaq 20289)"
"35551","(35551) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The servants used to take punishment from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, and he goes out on his companions as if he were suffering from a bad grief."
"35552","(35552) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: The example of a believer is that of a plant that the wind continues to tilt, and the believer continues to be afflicted by calamity. The example of an unbeliever is like a cedar tree that cannot be shaken until it reaps a harvest."
"35553","(35553) Abdullah bin Numayr and Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Zakaria bin Abi Zaydi narrated to us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, he said: Ibn Ka’b bin Malik told me, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: For example The believer is like the raw material of the plantation, which the wind blows it over, blows it over and over again until it becomes irritated, and the likeness of the disbeliever. Like rice that has been dried out on its root, nothing is sufficient for it, even if it is damaged once."
"35554","(35554) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Burayd bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: A believer is like a building to another believer, some of which support others."
"35555","(35555) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Ali bin Ata, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: The likeness of a believer is like that of a bee: it eats good and produces good."
"35556","(35556) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: The believers are like one man: if his head complains, his entire body suffers from fever and sleeplessness.\n(Bukhari 6011, Muslim 2000)"
"35557","(35557) Ali bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Mubarak, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Thabit, he said: Abu Hazim narrated to me, he said: I heard Sa’l bin Saad narrated, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: The believer is among the people of faith in his position as the head. The body, the believer’s pain is for the people of faith just as the body feels pain for what is in the head. (Ahmad 340, Tabarani 4693)"
"35558","(35558) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, on the authority of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The likeness of a believer is like a body: if one part of it suffers, it suffers because of it as a whole.\n(Ahmad 274, Tayalisi 793)"
"35559","(35559) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Talha, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jahadi, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: No servant raises himself except that God lowers him, and no servant lowers himself except that God raises him up.\n(Muslim 2001)"
"35560","(35560) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ubaydah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: He said to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Recite the Qur’an to me. He said: I said: O Messenger of God, recite it to you and to you it was revealed. He said: I long to hear it from someone else. He said: So the women recited until when they reached the news: {But how will it be when We bring from every nation a witness? And We brought you as a witness over these. I raised my head, or a man winked at me and I saw his tears flowing."
"35561","(35561) Zayd bin Hubab told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Salih told me, he said: Amr bin Qais told me, on the authority of Abd Allah ibn Busr said that a Bedouin said to the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace: Which people are the best? He said: He who lives long and is good. His work"
"35562","(35562) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Kathir ibn Zayd, on the authority of Salamah ibn Abi Yazid, on the authority of Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Part of a person’s happiness is that his life is long, and God grants him turning to him.\n(Ahmad 333. Bazzar 3240)"
"35563","(35563) Ja’far bin Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of my father Hariri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The best of you are the ones who live the longest and do the best in deeds. (Bazzar) 1971)"
"35564","(35564) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Talha bin Yahya, he said: Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Talha narrated to me, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Shaddad, he said: Three groups of Banu Adhirah came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they converted to Islam. He said: The Prophet said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Who will suffice me with these? He said: Talhah said: I did. He said: So they were with me. He said: So Ali was struck. The people were sent. He said: One of them went out and was martyred. Then a mission was struck and the second went out and was martyred. He said: And the third remained. Until he died sick in his bed. Talhah said: I saw in sleep as if I had been admitted to Paradise and saw them and recognized them. By their names and marks. He said: Then the first of them entered the one who died on his bed, and the second of those who were witnesses came in. He influenced him, and when the last of them were the first, he said, “So he let me in from that.” He said: “So I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and mentioned That is for Him, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: There is no one in the sight of God who is better than a Mu’ammar who is carried out in Islam for his sake. And His greatness, His glorification, and His praise. (Nasa’i 10674 and Ahmad 163)"
"35565","(35565) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakra. On the authority of his father, he said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Which of the people is best? He said: He who lives long and is good. His deeds. He said: Which people are evil? He said: He whose life is long and his deeds are bad. (Tirmidhi 2330. Ahmad 48)"
"35566","(35566) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Rabi’ah. On the authority of Ubaid bin Khalid Al-Salami, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made my brother feel between two men, and one of them was killed and the other was killed. After him, we prayed for him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What you said. They said: We called upon God for him, O God. Join him with his companion. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: So how good is his prayer after his prayer and his fasting after His fasting and where was his deed after his deed? He doubted fasting and the deed that was between them as between the heavens and the earth. (Ahmed 219; Abu Dawud 2516)"
"35567","(35567) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: Al-Abbas said: Who knows best how long the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, remains? May God’s peace and blessings be upon us. I said: O Messenger of God, if you took a throne and spoke to the people, they would have harmed you. He said: I will not stop between They will trample my heels, they will tear off my cloak, and their dust will fall on me, until God gives me relief from them.\n(Bazzar 2466. Darami 75)"
"35568","(35568) Yahya bin Bukair narrated to us, saying: Muslim bin Saeed Al-Wasiti narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour bin Zazan, on the authority of Al-Hasan said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to console the people himself until he began to patch his garment with blood, and what he gathered Between dinner and lunch, three days of loyalty until God’s death."
"35569","(35569) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Baz ibn Hakim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: I said, O Messenger of God, This is our religion. He said: This is your religion, and wherever you do good, it is sufficient for you."
"35570","(35570) Yahya bin Bukair narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Muttalib bin Hantab, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever says, “May God disgrace the world.” The world says: “May God disgrace those who disobey us.” No\n(Hakim 313)"
"35571","(35571) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Nistas, on the authority of Sa’id al-Maqbari, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: The best of people is he who hopes for its good and believes from its evil, and the worst of people is he who does not hope for its good and does not believe. Evil\n(Tirmidhi 2263 and Hakim 269)"
"35572","(35572) Muhammad bin Fudail told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah Al-Qurashi, on the authority of?? Abdullah bin Ukaym said: Abu Bakr addressed us and said: As for what follows, I advise you to fear God and to praise God. And if you mix desire with terror and combine desire with request, then indeed God has praised him. Zakariya and his family, and he said: {Indeed, they hastened to good deeds and called upon Us with longing and fear, and they were for Us Submissive} Then know, servants of God, that God has taken your souls as a pledge of your rights, and has taken your covenants based on that, and has purchased A few of you will perish with many that remain, and this is the Book of God among you. His wonders will never cease nor will His light be extinguished. So believe in His words, and be sincere in His Book, and gain insight into it for the day of oppression. For He created you only for His servants, and He appointed How are you, the honorable writers? They know what you do. Then know, servants of God, that you will begin and go away during a time that has been absent. You have knowledge of it, so if you are able to fulfill the deadlines while you are in the work of God, then do so, and you will not be able to do that except by God. So race ahead in your appointed time before your time expires and He returns you to the worst of your deeds. Indeed, there are people who have made Their lives are for others, and they have forgotten themselves, so how about you not to be like them? The revelations are the revelations and the salvations are the salvations, for indeed Behind you is an earnest seeker whose return will come quickly. (Hakim 383)"
"35573","(35573) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq saw a bird landing on tree, and he said: Blessed are you, O bird. By God, I wish I were like you, falling on the tree and eating of the fruit, then You may fly, and there will be no reckoning or torment upon you. By God, I wish I were a tree on the side of the road, and a camel passed by me and took me away. Then he brought me into his mouth and touched me, then he made me scorn, then he brought me out with barren waters, and I was not human. (Ibn Al-Mubarak 240)"
"35574","(35574) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Zubaid, he said: When I attended Abu Bakr The deceased sent for Omar and said: I have left you with a will if you keep it: Indeed, Allah has a right at night that He does not accept during the day. Indeed, God has a right in the day that is not accepted by him at night, and that a voluntary offering is not accepted until you perform the obligatory prayer. The scales of those whose scales will be light on the Day of Resurrection will be light because they follow falsehood in this world and it will be light for them, and it is true. For a scale in which nothing can be placed except falsehood as long as it is light, and the scales are heavy only for those whose scales are heavy on the Day of Judgment. By following them, the truth is in this world, and it is a burden for them, and a truth for a balance in which nothing will be placed on the Day of Resurrection except the truth. That it should be heavy. Have you not seen that God mentioned the people of the Jinnah with the good deeds they did, and overlooked their bad deeds, and He said: The one who says: I will not inform these people, and he reminds the people of Hell of the evil of what they have done, and the good of what they have done will be returned to them. Then the one who says: I am better than these. And he mentioned the signs of mercy and the signs of punishment, so that the believer might be willing and in awe, and not wish upon God other than the truth, nor He will be thrown into destruction by his own hands. If you keep this saying of mine, there is no absent person more beloved to you than death, nor You need him, and if you miss this statement of mine, then there is no absent person more hateful to you than him, and you will never fail him."
"35575","(35575) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Misra, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, on the authority of Rafi’ bin Abu Rafi’, he said: I accompanied Abu Bakr and he had a fine garment that he would leave on when he rode, and we would wear it for him. And when We descended, and it was the garment for which you had reproached us, they said: We will sell the goods after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace."
"35576","(35576) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Amr informed us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, he said: When it was revealed: {Indeed Those who lower their voices in the presence of the Messenger of God - those are the ones whose hearts God has tested for piety} Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq said: O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I will not speak to you except as a brother in secrets until I meet God. \n(Harith 957, Hakim 462)"
"35577","(35577) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, he said, Abu Bakr was He addresses us and mentions the beginning of the creation of man, and says: He was created from the urethra of urine, from a stench. Then he mentions until one of us becomes filthy. Himself"
"35578","(35578) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Mis`ar, on the authority of Abu Awn, on the authority of Arfaja al-Salami, who said: Abu Bakr said: Weep. If they do not cry, then cry."
"35579","(35579) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Raba’i, on the authority of Abu Musa, who said: Amr bin Al-Aas said: By God, if Abu Bakr and Omar left this money and it was permissible for them to have any of it, then We were foolish and their opinion was lacking, and I swear to God that they were not foolish, nor lacking in opinion, and if they were two women it would be forbidden. We have already perished from this wealth that we acquired after them, and by God, their calamity was only caused by us."
"35580","(35580) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Abu Bakr stood up as a preacher, and said: Give good news, for I hope that May God complete this matter until you are satisfied with oil and bread."
"35581","(35581) Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abul Safar, who said: People from His brothers visited him during his illness, and they said to him: O successor of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, shall we not call a doctor for you? He looks at you. He said: He looked at me. They said: So what did he say to you? He said: He said: I will do what I want."
"35582","(35582) Khaled bin Hayyan told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Maimun, who said: Abu Bakr was brought a large crow. The two wings, and he said: There is no game caught, nor any tree branches, that were not lost in glorification."
"35583","(35583) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aslam, the servant of Omar, he said: When we came With Omar al-Sham, he put his camel to rest and went to relieve himself, so I threw my clods between the two sections of the saddle. When he came, he rode on the fur. So we met the people of the Levant receiving Omar, and they started looking, and I started pointing to him. He said: Omar says: Their eyes aspire. To the boats of those who have no manners, who want the boats of non-Arabs."
"35584","(35584) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: When Umar came to the Levant, the people met him while he was riding his camel. They said: O Commander of the Faithful, if you rode wearing a belt, the great men and their faces would meet you. He said: Then Omar said, “Should I not see you?” Here, the matter is from here, and he pointed with his hand to the heavens, “Leave the way of my camel.”"
"35585","(35585) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Qays ibn Muslim, on the authority of Tariq ibn Shihab, he said: When the age of the Levant came, The soldiers came to him wearing an garment, slippers, and a turban, and he was wading through the water with the head of his camel. They said: O Amir. Believers, the soldiers and the penguins of the Levant met you while you were in this state. He said: Then Omar said: We are a people whom God has honored with Islam, so you will not We seek glory in others."
"35586","(35586) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, who said: Omar wrote: Indeed, the world is green and sweet, so who He who takes it as he deserves it is destined to be blessed for it, and whoever takes it otherwise than that is like an eater who does not He is satisfied."
"35587","(35587) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdul-Rahman bin Awf, he said: When Omar was brought with the treasures of the Khosrau family, and behold, there was so much yellow and white that it almost made my eyes bleed. He said: Then Omar cried. At that, he said: Abdul Rahman said: What makes you cry, O Commander of the Faithful? Indeed, this day is a day of gratitude and happiness. He was happy, and Omar said: This has not increased among a people except that God will create enmity and hatred among them."
"35588","(35588) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Al-Mughiriya, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, who said: I saw between his shoulders Omar has four patches in his shirt."
"35589","(35589) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Barda, he said: He wrote Omar to Abu Musa: As for what follows, the happiest of the shepherds is he whose flock is happy with him, and the most miserable of the subjects in the sight of God is he who is miserable. You have tended it, and beware of being terrified and your workers are terrified, for your likeness before God will be like an animal. She looked at A green vegetable from the earth that it grew in, seeking that ghee, but it died in its ghee, and peace be upon you."
"35590","(35590) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Omar said: The flock leads to the imam whatever it leads to. The Imam is to God, and when he relents, they relent."
"35591","(35591) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Muhammad bin Shihab, who said: Omar said: No. Dissent from what does not concern you, stay away from your enemy, and keep from your friend except the trustworthy, for the trustworthy among the people is not equal to anything. And do not accompany the ungodly, lest he teach you of his immorality, and do not reveal your secret to him, and consult those who fear God regarding your affairs."
"35592","(35592) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Suqi, who said: I came to Na’im bin Abi Nad and he came out to me. A scroll, and there it was from Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah and Muadh bin Jabal to Omar bin Al-Khattab: Peace be upon you. Now then, We have made a promise to you, and your own affairs are important to you, and in the morning you have taken charge of the affairs of this nation, whether it is red or black. The honorable and the lowly, the enemy and the friend sit between your hands, and each has its share of justice, so see how you are with... That, O Omar, we warn you of a day in which faces will become stubborn, hearts will dry up, and arguments will be lost. He oppressed them with His tyranny, while the creation was subservient to Him, hoping for His mercy and fearing His punishment, and we used to narrate that a command This nation will return at the end of its time: that the brothers of the public will be enemies of the secret, and we seek refuge in God from Our letter was revealed to you just as it was revealed from our hearts. We wrote with it our advice to you, and peace be upon you. So he wrote to them: From Omar bin Al-Khattab: To Abu Ubaidah and Muadh bin Jabal: Peace be upon you both. As for what follows, you You wrote to me reminding me that you had promised me and that I had an important personal matter and that I had now taken charge of this matter. Mothers are red and black. He sits between the hands of the honorable and the lowly, the enemy and the friend, and each has his share of that. And you wrote: So see how you are at that time, O Omar. And there is no power or strength at that time for Omar except in God. And you have written, warning me of what you warned the nations before us, and in the past, the difference of night and day in the time periods of the people brought each person closer together. far away, and they bring to fruition all things new, and they bring every promise until the people go to their homes from the Garden and the Fire. And you wrote, mentioning that you were speaking, that the matter of this nation will return at the end of its time: that they be The brothers of the world are enemies of the secret, and you are not those. This is not the time of that, and that is a time when you will appear. In it is desire and fear. Some people’s desire for others is for the benefit of their world, and some people’s fear of others. You two wrote therein sincerely admonishing me by God that your book was sent down other than the revelation that came down from your hearts, and that you You have written about it and you have spoken the truth, so do not leave the letter to me, for it is indispensable to me, and peace be upon you both."
"35593","(35593) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Sulaym ibn Hanzali, on the authority of Omar ibn al-Khattab, that he used to say: O God, I seek refuge in You lest You take me by surprise, or leave me in heedlessness, or make me among the heedless."
"35594","(35594) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Yasar bin Numayr, Q? There is never any flour unless I am disobedient to it."
"35595","(35595) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of Abu al-Layth al-Ansari, who said: Omar said: Own the dough. It is one of the two mills."
"35596","(35596) Muhammad bin Marwan told us, on the authority of Yunus, he said: Al-Hasan might have mentioned Omar and said: By God, it was not. The first of them to embrace Islam, nor the best of them to spend in the way of God, but he defeated the people through asceticism in this world and strictness in it. God's command, and no blameworthy person should fear God's blame."
"35597","(35597) Affan told us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Malik bin Dinar, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Omar did not condemn him. Until he was killed, except with ghee, or spoilage, or disgusting oil."
"35598","(35598) Affan narrated to us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: It was Omar bin Al-Khattab. He passes by a verse in his rose, and the words choke him, and he weeps until he falls, then he stays at home until he is brought back. They think he is sick."
"35599","(35599) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Omar was walking on a road and with him was Abdullah bin Omar. Then his neighbor saw a woman wandering off, one time getting lost, and another getting up, so he said: How miserable this one is, who knows how lost she is? Abdullah said: This, by God, is one of your daughters. He said: Your daughters. He said: Yes. He said: Who is he? He said: The daughter of Abdullah bin Omar. He said: Woe to you, O Abdullah bin Omar! You have destroyed it in jest. He said: What shall we do? You have withheld from us what you have. So he looked at him. He said: I do not have the honor of you that you should win for your daughters as you win for the people. No, by God, I have nothing with you except your shares. Muslims"
"35600","(35600) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Burqan, on the authority of a man whom he did not name, on the authority of Umar ibn al-Khattab, that He said in his sermon: Hold yourselves accountable before you are held accountable, and weigh yourselves before you are weighed, and beautify yourself for the greatest display. On the day you are turned away, not a single thing will be hidden from you. (Abu Naim 52)"
"35601","(35601) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, he said: Abu Salamah told us, he said: Saad said: By God, what He was the first of us to Islam, nor was he the first to migrate, but you know by what virtue he has increased us in this world. That means Omar bin Al-Khattab."
"35602","(35602) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar, Ibn Idris, and Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Bukair ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Muammar ibn Abi Huyya, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Adiy ibn al-Khayar, said: Umar said: If the servant He humbled himself for the sake of God, and God exalted his wisdom and said: May God refresh your coffin, for in Himself it is small and in people’s souls it is great. And when a servant is proud of his promise that God will bring him and her to the earth, and say, “Alas, God will lose you,” then he is great within himself. And in people's souls it is so small that it is more despicable in their eyes than a pig."
"35603","(35603) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: When Omar left, Kum He made a pile of dirt, then he spread his garment over her and lay down on her."
"35604","(35604) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Muhammad, on the authority of a man from Ghifar, on the authority of His father, he said: I came with food that I brought from the neighbor on one of the al-Sadaqa’s camels, so Omar looked at it and was impressed by its virginity. I said: Take him, O Commander of the Faithful. He struck my shoulder with his hand and said: By God, I have no more right to him than a man from Banu Ghifar."
"35605","(35605) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, he said: It was In Omar's hands was a plate with crumbled bread in it, then a man like a Bedouin came and said: So he said: Eat. He said: So he made It is followed by the fat morsel at the south of the plate. Omar said: It is as if you are desolate, and he said: By God, I have never tasted ghee, nor seen it. He ate, and Omar said: By God, I will not taste ghee until the people are alive from the beginning."
"35606","(۳۵۶۰۶) حَدَّثَنَا مُحَمَّدُ بْنُ بِشْرٍ ، قَالَ : حدَّثَنَا مِسْعَرٌ ، عَنْ عَوْنِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللہِ بْنِ عُتْبَۃَ ، قَالَ : قَالَ عُمَرُ : جَالِسُوا Those who repent, for they are the most delicate thing I can cherish."
"35607","(35607) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Yahya ibn Ja’adah, who said: Omar said: Had I not walked in the path of God, or placed my forehead in the dust for God, or sat with people who reap good words as He picks dates, I would love to catch up with God."
"35608","(35608) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of a sheikh, saying: Omar said: Whoever wants the truth, let him excrete."
"35609","(35609) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydi, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Abu Uthman, he said: Omar said: The winter is a spoil. The worshiper"
"35610","(35610) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Ashras Abu Shayban told us, he said: Ata al-Khurasani told us, he said: he said Omar ibn al-Khattab detained his companions, so he came out to them in the evening, and they said: He did not detain you. He said: I washed my clothes, and when they dried, I came out."
"35611","(35611) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, who said: Omar wrote to Abu Musa: You will not attain the Hereafter with anything better than"
"35612","(35612) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abu Farwa, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Layla, who said: He came before Omar. Some people from Iraq saw it as if they were eating food, so he said: What is this, people of Iraq? If I had wanted him to be attacked just as he has been attacked by you, I would have done so, but we will spare from this world what we find in our hereafter. Did you not hear God say: {You took the good things of yours in your worldly life and enjoyed them}"
"35613","(35613) Abu Asama told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwah told us, on the authority of his father, he said: When the age of the Levant came, there was His shirt was torn from his seat, a thick white shirt, so he sent it to the owner of an armour, or a deer, he said. So he washed him, patched him up, and sewed for him a Coptic shirt, so he brought them all and threw the Coptic shirt to him, so Omar took him away. So he touched it and said: This is soft, so he threw it to him and said: Throw my shirt to me, for it will make them dry because of the sweat."
"35614","(35614) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Omar, who said: Omar used to say: May God protect him. The believer. Asim bin Thabit bin Al-Aflah vowed not to touch a polytheist, and that a polytheist would not touch him, but God prevented him after that. He died just as many of them did during their lives."
"35615","(35615) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ ibn Quza’i, he said: I heard Ibn Umar, he said: It was Umar ibn Al-Khattab. He brings bread, meat, milk, oil, vegetables, and vinegar, and he eats, then he sucks his fingers and says Thus, he wipes his hands with his hands and says: These are the handkerchiefs of the family of Omar."
"35616","(35616) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Abu Malih, he said: He said: Omar: The world in the hereafter is nothing but like the carcass of a rabbit."
"35617","(35617) Abu Asama narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, he said: Wadi’ al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Omar said: Do not object to what does not And keep away from your enemy, and beware of your friend, except the trustworthy among the people, and there is no trustworthy except the one who fears God, and do not accompany the ungodly. So learn from his immorality, and do not reveal your secret to him, but seek advice from those who fear God regarding your matter."
"35618","(35618) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, who said: Omar said about Al-Azliyah, a woman from among my associates. The bad"
"35619","(35619) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Habib, who said: People from Iraq came to Omar and among them was Jarir bin Abd. God, He said: Then he brought to them a bowl made of bread and oil. He said: Then He said to them, “Take.” He said: So they took a weak portion. He said: So he said to them: I may see what you are approaching, so what do you want, sweet, sour, hot, cold, and ejaculation in the bellies?"
"35620","(35620) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of some of his companions, on the authority of Omar, that he was invited to a meal. So when they came with a color, he mixed it with its companion."
"35621","(35621) Shababah bin Siwar told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, on the authority of Asim bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Aamir, He said: I saw Omar ibn Al-Khattab taking some straw from the ground, and he said: I wish this straw was so good! I wish I were nothing! My mother did not give birth to me. I wish I had been forgotten and forgotten."
"35622","(35622) Shabab told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, on the authority of Asim bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amir, on the authority of Ibn Umar. He said: Omar's head was on my lap, so he said: Lay it down, I have no mother for you. So he said: Woe to Omar's mother, if my Lord does not forgive me."
"35623","(35623) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Naama, on the authority of Hujar bin Rabi’ah, He said: Omar said: Indeed, immorality is like this and he covers his head to the eyebrows, but righteousness is like this and uncovers his head."
"35624","(35624) Affan narrated to us, he said: Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Thabit said: Anas said: The price has increased, the food has become very expensive in Medina. At the time of Omar, he started eating barley and his stomach disapproved of it, so he turned his hand to his stomach and said: By God, what It is only what you see, until God expands upon the Muslims."
"35625","(35625) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of his father, he said: I was I was walking with Omar ibn Al-Khattab and he saw dates lying out, so he said: Take them. I said: What should I do with dates? He said: Dates and dates. Until it is gathered together, so I took it and he passed by a date bin and said: Throw it in it."
"35626","(35626) Abd Allah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amir, he said: I went out with Omar, and what I saw him wandering around for a while until he came back. He said: I said: Why was he seeking shade? He said: He placed the tree on the tree. He takes shade with it."
"35627","(35627) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Asama, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Hamid bin Abdul Rahman, who said: Omar said: If only he had perished. A lamb lost on the shore of the Euphrates. I was afraid that God would ask me about it."
"35628","(35628) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Yasir bin Amr, who said: When Omar bin Al-Khattab came to Syria, he came With a rag, he rode on it, and when he shook it, he got down and struck his face, and said: May God make you ugly, and curse him who taught you this."
"35629","(35629) Yahya bin Issa told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: I entered upon Omar was sitting on a stump in his house and was talking to himself, so I approached him and said: What made you worry, Amir? The believers, and he said: Thus with his hand and pointing with it, he said: I said: What concerns you, by God, if we saw something from you? We deny it to our people. He said: Allah is the One besides whom there is no god. If you had seen from me something that you would deny, you would have affirmed it. So I said: O Allah, there is no god but Him. If we saw something from you that we would disapprove of, we would oppose you. He said: He was very happy about that, and he said: Praise be to God who has placed among you the companions of Muhammad, some of whom, if he sees something from me that he disapproves of, tell me about it."
"35630","(35630) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammam bin Yahya, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, On the authority of Anas, he said: I saw Omar bin Al-Khattab eating a saa’ of dates with his mouth."
"35631","(35631) Zayd ibn Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Mutarrif, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, on the authority of his father, he said: I was Omar was brought a saa’ of dates, and he said: O Aslam, tear off the peel from him, and rinse it, and he will eat it."
"35632","(35632) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir, who said: Omar was asked about sincere repentance, and he said: Sincere repentance means that a servant repents from a bad deed and then never returns to it again."
"35633","(35633) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, who said: Omar was asked about the saying of God: {And when the souls Married} He said: A good man will be paired with a righteous man in Paradise, and a bad man will be paired with an evil man in Hell."
"35634","(35634) Hussein bin Ali narrated to us, saying: Tu’ma bin Ghaylan Al-Ja’fi narrated to me, on the authority of a man, who was told: Mikail, a sheikh from the people of Khorasan, said: When Omar got up at night, he said: You may see my place and know my needs. So bring me back from You, O God, in my need, successful, successful, and responding to me. You have forgiven me and had mercy on me. Then He finished his prayer and said: Oh God, I do not see anything in this world lasting, nor do I see a condition in it that is right. Oh God, make me speak. In it with knowledge and remain silent in it with wisdom. O God, do not give me too much of this world so that I will be arrogant, and do not give me too little of it so that I will forget. For what is little and sufficient is better than what is abundant and sufficient."
"35635","(35635) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I entered upon Omar when he was stabbed, and I said: Give good tidings of Paradise, O Commander of the Faithful. I converted to Islam when the people disbelieved, and I struggled with the Messenger of God when the people abandoned him and he was arrested. The Messenger of God was satisfied with you, and no two people disagreed about your caliphate, and you killed a witness, so he said: Repeat against me, so you prepared against him. He said: By the One besides Whom there is no god, if I had the yellow and white that is on the earth, I would have ransomed myself with it from the time of rising."
"35636","(35636) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ismail and Sufyan, on the authority of Zubaid bin Al-Harith, on the authority of a man from Banu Amir. He said: Ali said: I only fear for you two things: long hope, and following one’s desire, for long hope makes one forget the hereafter, and Following desires averts one from the truth, and indeed this world has departed, turning away, and the Hereafter is coming, and to each one of them. Children, so be among the children of the Hereafter, for today is deed, but no reckoning, and tomorrow is reckoning, and no deed. \n(Ibn Al-Mubarak 255)"
"35637","(35637) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Al-Muhajir Al-Amiri, on the authority of Ali In the same way"
"35638","(35638) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Ali said: Blessed is every sleeping servant who knows the people, and does not People recognize him, and God recognizes him with His approval. These are the beacons of guidance. All dark temptations will be removed from them. And God will admit them into His mercy. They are not deceitful, nor hypocritical."
"35639","(35639) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Muhammad bin Talha told us, on the authority of Zubaid, he said: Ali said: The best of people This middle style joins the next one, and returns to the high one."
"35640","(35640) Waki’ told us, he said: Iyas bin Abi Tamimah told us, he said: I heard Ata bin Abi Rabah, he said: It was When Ali bin Abi Talib sends a concubine, a man appoints her to her and advises him, saying: I advise you to fear God, you must Meeting Him, and there is no end for you other than Him, and He is the ruler of this world in the Hereafter, and you should choose the one who brings you closer to God, for Concerning what God has as a successor in this world."
"35641","(35641) Waki` narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahhab, that Najja blasphemed Ali. In his clothing, he said: The believer follows his example and the heart is humble."
"35642","(35642) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Salih, who used to serve Umm Kulthum, the son of Ali, said: I entered upon Umm Kulthum while she was combing and a screen between her and me, so I sat waiting for her. Until he gave me permission, then Hasan and Hussein came and entered her while she was combing, and said: Why don’t you feed Abu Salih something? She said: Yes, he said: So they brought out a bowl containing broth with grains, and I said: Will you feed me with this while you are princes? Umm Kulthum said: O Abu Salih, what would it be like if you saw the Commander of the Faithful and he was brought with orange and Hasan went, or Hussein took it? He took it out of his hand, then he ordered it to be divided."
"35643","(35643) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, he said: Ali said: To his mother, Fatima bint Asad: Sufficient is Fatima, daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The servant outside: to give him water to drink. And the pilgrim, and the work at home is sufficient for you: kneading, baking, and grinding."
"35644","(35644) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: Fatima was guided. This night was given to me, and all that was beneath us was the skin of a ram."
"35645","(35645) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Qays, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: Ali said: Words if you had departed. The last thing in them is that you will have finished them before you realize the like of them: No servant hopes except in his Lord, and he fears nothing except his sin. And let not one who does not know be ashamed to learn, nor let a scholar be ashamed, when asked about what he does not know, to say: God knows best. And know that the position of patience in relation to faith is like the position of the head in relation to the body. When the head is gone, the body is gone, and when Patience is gone, faith is gone."
"35646","(35446) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr ibn Qays, on the authority of Adiy ibn Thabit, who said: A basin was brought to Ali. He was a traitor and he did not eat from it."
"35647","(35447) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr bin Kathir al-Hanafi, on the authority of Ali, who said: Be silent. Be angry and laugh less, hearts will not be able to overcome it."
"35648","(35648) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hudhayl, he said: I saw Ali wearing a shirt, When he extends it, it reaches half of his forearm, and when he extends it, it does not exceed his nail."
"35649","(35649) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Damra bin Habib, who said: The Messenger of May God’s blessings and peace be upon his daughter, so he comforted her by serving in the house, and he passed judgment on Ali as long as he was leaving the house."
"35650","(35650) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sakhbara, on the authority of Ali, who said: What No one has risen in the morning except Na'im, and the lowest abode is he who eats wheat, sits in the shade, and drinks from its water. Euphrates"
"35651","(35651) Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Abu Hayyan told us, on the authority of Mujamma, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymi, on the authority of Yazid ibn A partner, he said: One day Ali came out with his sword, and he said: Who will buy this sword from me? If I had a price A garment I did not sell."
"35652","(35652) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Uthman Abi Al-Yaqzan, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Ali {except the companions The right one} He said: They are the children of Muslims."
"35653","(35653) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan ibn Al-Hakam Al-Nakha’i, he said: My mother told me, on the authority of Umm Uthman, the mother of Ali’s son. She said: I came to Ali and between his hands were cloves bruised in the expanse, so I said: O Commander of the Faithful, give my daughter some of “These cloves are a necklace.” He said, “Thus and so,” and tapped his hand. “Give me a good dirham. This is the property of the Muslims. Otherwise.” So be patient until our share of it comes to us, so we give your daughter a necklace from it."
"35654","(35654) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: The example of the one who combined faith and the Qur’an. The example of the pure citrus, which has a pleasant scent and taste, and the example of one who has not combined faith and not the Qur’an, is the example of the anthelium. An evil smell and an evil taste."
"35655","(35655) Abu Asama told us, he said: Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Omar bin Ali told me, he said: My father told me, he said: It was said Perhaps Ali: What is the matter with you, Abu Hassan? You were next to the graveyard. He said: I find them to be honest neighbors who protect themselves from evil. And they remember the Hereafter."
"35656","(35656) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If Fatima used to knead, and if she cut her hair, It almost hits your eyelid."
"35657","(35657) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Juhayfy, he said: Abdullah said: The purity of the world has gone, but its emptiness remains. Death is a treasure for every Muslim."
"35658","(35658) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Juhaifah, on the authority of Abdullah: The world is like a hole, its purity has gone and its bleakness remains."
"35659","(35659) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murra, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, who said: According to one’s Knowledge is to fear God, and it is enough of ignorance to be amazed at one’s work."
"35660","(35660) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Qais, on the authority of Dhudhail, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Whoever wants the last. Harmful to this world, and whoever desires this world harms the hereafter. O my people, harm the mortal for the rest."
"35661","(35661) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Mughal, on the authority of Abu Safara, on the authority of Al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, he said: Abd said: God: I wish I were a bird with feathers on my shoulders."
"35662","(35662) Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: Abdullah said: If only its trees were You support"
"35663","(35663) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Suwayd, he said: Abdullah: I wish Ruthha were separated from me and attributed to her, so she was named Abdullah bin Ruthha, and that God forgave him. One sin, except that Abu Muawiyah said: I wish I had known that God would forgive me. Then he mentioned the like of it."
"35664","(35664) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of his brother, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, he said: Abdullah said: Whoever is able If any of you wants to put his treasure in heaven, where it will not be eaten by moths or caught by theft, let him do it, for a man’s heart is with His treasure\n(Abu Naim 135)"
"35665","(35665) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Omar ibn Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Burda, he said: He heard Abdullah ibn Masoud He woke up and lay down facing the front."
"35666","(35666) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Abdul-Malik bin Umair, he said: The family of Abdullah told me, That Abdullah advised his son Abdul Rahman, saying: I advise you to fear God, and let your house protect you, and control your tongue. And cry over your sin."
"35667","(35667) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Bayan, on the authority of Qays, who said: Abdullah said: I wish I knew that God He forgave me one of my sins, and I do not care which son of Adam gave birth to me."
"35668","(35668) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Salih ibn Khabab, on the authority of Husain ibn Uqba, who said: Abdullah said: The people who make the most mistakes on the Day of Resurrection will be the ones who delve into falsehood the most."
"35669","(35669) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Salih ibn Khabab, on the authority of Husain ibn Uqba, who said: Abdullah said: Indeed, Paradise is surrounded by calamities, and Hell is surrounded by desires, so whoever removes the veil will find what is behind it."
"35670","(35670) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, he said: Examples of degrading things Among the deeds is the example of a people who stayed in a house that did not have firewood, but they had meat with them, and they did not stop gathering until they gathered what they had cooked. Their flesh"
"35671","(35671) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, who said: Abdullah fell ill with an illness and became frightened. So we said: We have not seen you so distressed by an illness. We have not seen you so distressed by this illness of yours. He said: It took hold of me and brought me close to heedlessness."
"35672","(35672) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Qasim, he said: Abdullah said: Do not be hasty in praising people or censuring them. For a man admires you today and likes you tomorrow, and he likes you today and likes you tomorrow, and the servants change them. And God will forgive sins on the Day of Resurrection, and God will be more merciful to His servant on the day he comes to you than the mother of one who spread his bed for him. The land of Qayyah, then she stood up and touched his bed with her hand. If it had a sting, she would have it, and if it had a thorn, it would have been With it"
"35673","(35673) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Al-Qasim, he said: Abdullah said: I wished that I could be alone in this world. Like a smelly rider."
"35674","(35674) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, he said: Abdullah said: It is enough. With the fear of God, knowledge, and it is sufficient to be deceived by Him out of ignorance."
"35675","(35675) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Suwayd, he said: Abdullah said: By Him there is no god but Him, there is never before the family of Abdullah there is anything they hope that God will give them something good for, or repel. There is no harm in them except that God knows that the servant of God does not associate anything with Him."
"35676","(35676) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shimr bin Atiyya, on the authority of Mughirah bin Saad bin Al-Akhram, on the authority of His father, he said: Abdullah said: And He who has no god but Him does not harm a servant who is a Muslim in the morning and a Muslim in the evening. What? He was afflicted with this world."
"35677","(35677) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abbad bin Abbad bin Alqamiya Al-Mazini, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: A tablet The companions of Ibn Masoud were cold. He said: The man became ashamed to come in short clothes, or short clothes, so Abu Abdul-Rahman was in his abaya, then he woke up in it, then on the third day he rose in it in the morning."
"35678","(35678) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Abdullah said: I do not fear for you to make a mistake. But I fear for you in intentionally. I do not fear for you that you will become independent in your work, but I fear for you that You take it too much."
"35679","(35679) Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: Hisham Al-Dastawwi informed us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, He said: Abdullah said: Leave the tales, for it is sin."
"35680","(35680) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu al-Ahwas, who said: Abdullah said: The believer sees His sin is as if it were a rock that he is afraid will fall on him, and the hypocrite sees his sin as a fly that fell on his nose and flew away. So he went."
"35681","(35681) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, who said: We were sitting with Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, and a man said: Pointing to Al-Qasim, he said: Abdullah said: I wished that if I died, I would not be resurrected, so Al-Qasim said with his head like this, yes, yes."
"35682","(35682) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Zubaid, he said: Abdullah said: Speak good and you will be recognized for it, and do good. By Him you will be among its people, and do not be a hasty distributing seed. (Ibn Al-Mubarak 1438)"
"35683","(35683) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Sirri bin Yahya, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Abdullah said: If you stood between Heaven and Hell, so it was said to me: We will inform you of which of the two you are dearer to you, or you will be ashes. I would have chosen to be ashes."
"35684","(35684) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qais, on the authority of Ma’an, who said: Abdullah said: Do not separate, lest you be destroyed."
"35685","(35685) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: I wished that You have reconciled with nine bad deeds and a good deed."
"35686","(35686) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Aoun, who said: Abdullah said: The believer is a thousand, and no It is better for someone who does not get along well and does not get along. (Abu Naim 254)"
"35687","(35687) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Mara, who said: Abdullah said: Indeed, Allah gives him the world. Who loves and who does not love, and faith is only given to him who loves. If God loves a servant, He gives him faith. (Tabarani 8990)"
"35688","(35688) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, he heard it from Aoun bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: It is shown On the Day of Resurrection, people will have three records: a record of good deeds, a record of bliss, and a record of bad deeds. Then the record of good deeds is matched by the record of bliss, so the bliss takes away the good deeds, and the bad deeds leave their will to God. God Almighty, if He wills, He punishes, and if He wills, He forgives."
"35689","(35689) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Zaid, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: Learn, learn. If you know, then act."
"35690","(35690) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ma’n, he said: Abdullah said: A costume does not resemble a costume until you resemble it. Hearts hearts."
"35691","(35691) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Abu Issa, he said: Abdullah said: Indeed, from the head of Humility is to accept what is less than the honor of a gathering, and to extend greetings to whomever you meet."
"35692","(35692) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: You fast more, pray more, and strive more than the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they were Better than you. They said: Why, O Abu Abd al-Rahman? He said: They were more in this world and more in the hereafter."
"35693","(35693) Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Harun ibn Antarah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of His father, he said: Abdullah bin Masoud said: These hearts are weak, so occupy them with the Qur’an, and do not occupy them. Otherwise"
"35694","(35695) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Abdullah bin Abis told us, he said: Abu Iyas told me. On the authority of Abdullah, he used to say in his sermon: The most truthful hadith is the word of God, and the most reliable of nudity is the word of piety. The best religion is the religion of Abraham, the best story is the Qur’an, and the best Sunnah is the Sunnah of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. The most noble of hadiths is the remembrance of God, the best of matters are their punishments, the worst of matters are those they are newly invented, and the best of guidance is the guidance of the prophets. And the most noble of death is the killing of the martyrs, and the most deceitful is misguidance after guidance, and the best of knowledge is that which is of benefit, and the best of guidance is that which Follow, and the evil of blindness and blindness of heart.\n2. The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and what is little and sufficient is better than what is many and deplorable, and a soul you save is better than There are countless signs, the worst of sadness is when death approaches, and the worst of regret is regret on the Day of Resurrection, and among the people are those who do not He comes to prayer except one who is a deserter, and among the people is he who does not mention God except one who is emigrating, and the greatest of sins is a lying tongue, and the best is Wealth is the richness of the soul, the best provision is piety, the beginning of wisdom is the fear of God, and the best that is placed in the heart is certainty. Doubt is from disbelief, lamentation is from the work of the ignorant, deceit is from the coals of Hell, and treasure is like a pot of fire.\n3. Poetry is the psalms of Satan, wine is the gathering of sin, women are the snares of Satan, youth is a tangle of madness, and evil gains. Earning usury, the worst of all hardships is consuming an orphan’s wealth, happy is he who is advised by something other than that, and wretched is he who is miserable in his mother’s womb. For each of you, only what he is content with is sufficient for each of you, and he will only reach a place of four cubits, and the matter will continue in the end. And the best thing to do is its seals, and the worst of narratives is false narratives, and everything that is coming is nigh.\n4. And cursing a believer is immorality, and fighting him is disbelief, and eating his flesh is disobedience to God, and depriving him of his wealth is as depriving him of his blood, and whoever Whoever insinuates himself against God, He will make him a liar. Whoever forgives, God will forgive him. Whoever pardons, God will pardon him. Whoever is harsh, God will forgive him. Anger is rewarded by God, and whoever is patient in the face of calamities, God will punish him, and whoever knows calamity is patient in it. And whoever does not know Him will be rejected by Him, and whoever is arrogant God will cast him away, and whoever seeks to hear God will make him hear, and whoever The world is powerless, and whoever obeys Satan disobeys God, and whoever disobeys God will punish him."
"35695","(35695) Abdullah bin Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Zubaid bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Mara bin Sharahil, he said: He said: Abdullah: {Fear God as He deserves to be feared} and the right to fear Him is to be obeyed and not disobeyed, and to be remembered and not forgotten, and to He is grateful, but he is not ungrateful, and giving him money is a condition that you should give it to him while you are healthy and miserly, hoping to live and fearing poverty. The superiority of the night prayer over the daytime prayer is like the superiority of secret charity over public honesty."
"35696","(35696) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: Prayer is of no use. Except those who obey it. Then Abdullah recited: {Indeed, prayer forbids indecency and evil, but the remembrance of Allah is greater} and Abdullah said: Is the servant’s remembrance of God more righteous than the servant’s remembrance of his Lord?"
"35697","(35697) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: Abdullah said: It is sufficient for a person to be free from misery, or from Disappointment is that he spends the night while Satan has urinated in his ear, and in the morning he does not mention God."
"35698","(35698) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, who said: I heard Aoun bin Abdullah say: A man read with Abdullah bin Masoud: {Has there ever come upon man a period of time when he was not a thing mentioned?} Then Abdullah said: I wish that had been accomplished."
"35699","(35699) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Qurayh, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: Today no one of people, except that he is a guest, and his property is bare, so the guest is on the move and the bare property is returned."
"35700","(35700) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Qais bin Sakan, on the authority of Abd God Almighty in His saying: {And their light strives between their hands} He said: They give their light in proportion to their deeds. Among them are some His light is like a mountain, and the closest to them is a light. His light is on one’s thumb. It is extinguished once and then ignites again."
"35701","(35701) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Razin, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, He said: He will be expanded upon in this world, he will be expanded upon in the Hereafter, he will be restricted in this world, he will be limited in the Hereafter. He is extended to Him in this world, He is limited to Him in the Hereafter, He is comfortable and free from Him. (Ibn Al-Mubarak 74)"
"35702","(35702) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, in his saying: {Repent. To God is a sincere repentance. He said: Sincere repentance is that one repents and then does not do it again."
"35703","(35703) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah said: Whoever desires this world harms the hereafter. And whoever wants the afterlife harms this world."
"35704","(35704) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, who said: Abdullah said: I hate a man to see him. Empty, with nothing to do in this world or the work of the hereafter."
"35705","(35705) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamiya, he said: Abdullah said: Whoever loves to do justice to God Let him come to the people whom he likes to come to."
"35706","(35706) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamah, he said: Abdullah said: By the One besides whom there is no god, there is no A believing servant has been given something better than having a good opinion of God, and by Him there is no god but Him, no believing servant is good. If he thinks about God, he will give him that, for all goodness is in His hand."
"35707","(35707) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: Almost The meaning is that he will be tortured in his hole for the sin of the son of Adam. Then he recited: {And if God were to hold the people accountable for what they have earned}"
"35708","(35708) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu al-Ahwas, who said: Abdullah said: Do not overpower each other. This night you cannot stand it, so if one of you sleeps, let him sleep on his bed, for he will be safe."
"35709","(35709) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Abu Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Ibn Masoud. He said: Not one of the people on the Day of Resurrection will except that he wishes that he had been eating sustenance in this world, and it will not harm any of you. Whatever the state of the world in the evening and morning, let there be no grieving soul in your soul, and let one of you bite on a hot coal until it is extinguished. It is better than saying about a matter that God has decided: I wish this had not happened. (Abu Nu’aym 1371, Ahmad 117)"
"35710","(35710) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, he said: Abdullah said: It is written in The Torah: God has prepared for those whose sides turn away from their beds, such as no eye has seen, no ear heard, and no thought has occurred to me. The heart of a human being, and what no angel or messenger knows. He said: And We recite it: {So no soul knows what has been hidden from them of the Qur’an. Eyes}"
"35711","(35711) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Muslim Al-Bateen, on the authority of Adasa Al-Ta’i, who said: Abdullah was brought A bird was hunted honorably, and Abdullah said: I wish that while I hunted this bird, no human being would speak to me, nor would I speak to it. Until he met God."
"35712","(35712) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Khaythami, he said: Abdullah said: Look at the people when they lie down, and if you see a servant dying in the best way you see him, then hope for the best for him. You saw him die as evil as you saw him, so you feared for him, for if a servant was wretched, and if people liked some of his deeds, he would be judged. He has a devil, so he kills him and destroys him until the misery that is written for him overtakes him, and if he is happy, even if People used to dislike some of his deeds, and a king was appointed for him, so he guided and guided them until you realized the happiness that was destined for him. No"
"35713","(35713) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, he said: Abdullah said: Get accustomed to goodness. For goodness is in habit."
"35714","(35714) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamiya, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: Abdullah said: No soul is righteous. And do not reward him unless death is better for her than life, if he is righteous. God has said: {And what is with God is better for the righteous.} And if he is an immoral person, God has already said: {And do not those who think? They disbelieve. Indeed, We give them respite to them is better for their souls. We only give them respite to them so that they may increase in sin, and for them is a humiliating punishment}"
"35715","(35715) Shababah bin Suwar narrated to us, saying: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Kanf. A man saw a vision and told it to Ibn Masoud while he was fat. Ibn Masoud said: I hate it to be... The reciter is fat. Al-Amash said: I mentioned that to Abraham, and he said: Fat, he forgot the Qur’an."
"35716","(35716) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, who said: Abdullah said: With every joy. You are relieved"
"35717","(35717) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, who said: Abdullah was brought a drink, and he said: He gave him some food. He said: He is fasting. Then he said: Give him the black ones. He said: He is fasting. Until he passed by all of them, then he took them. So he drank it, then recited these verses: {They fear a Day in which hearts and eyes will be turned}"
"35718","(35718) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, who said: Abdullah said: The world is not similar to what is hidden in it. Except the thug has drunk its purity and its turbidity remains, and none of you will continue to be well as long as he fears God, and if it is itchy in his heart He came to a man about something and cured him of it, and I swear to God that you will almost never find it."
"35719","(35719) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Wa’il bin Rabi’i, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: There is no situation more beloved to God than for a servant to see Him while prostrating."
"35720","(35720) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Murā, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: God gives him the world. Who loves and who does not love, and faith is only given to him who loves. If God loves a servant, He gives him faith. Some of you are cowardly and refuse to suffer the night, and the enemy does not fight you, and is afraid of spending money, so let him increase it. Glory be to God, praise be to God, there is no god but God, and God is great."
"35721","(35721) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Aoun bin Abdullah bin Utba, who said: Abdullah said: The mountain To call out the mountain: Has anyone passed by you today who made remembrance of Allah?"
"35722","(35722) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murra, who said: Abu Al-Darda’ said: Worship God As if you were seeing it, and count yourselves from the dead, and know that a little will enrich you better than a lot. May God bless you, and know that righteousness does not fade away, and that sin is not forgotten."
"35723","(35723) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Raji bin Haywah, who said: Abu Al-Darda' gathered the people of Damascus and said: Listen to a brother of yours who is an adviser: Do you gather what you do not eat, and hope for what you do not realize? And you build what you do not live in. Where are those who were before you? They gathered together much, and built a distance, and built a strong one. They were all desolate, their hope became deceit, and their homes became graves."
"35724","(35724) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, who said: Abu Al-Darda’ would not pass by a village without He said: Where is your family? Then he says: They left and the deeds remained."
"35725","(35725) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, on the authority of Abdul Malik bin Umayr, he said: Abu Darda’ said Whoever mentions death a lot, his envy and joy will decrease."
"35726","(35726) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabab, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’, he said: Do not understand everything. Jurisprudence until you hate people besides God, then you return to yourself and you hate them even more."
"35727","(35727) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Dinar, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Qur’a, he said: Abu Darda’ said: Not It is good that your money and your children increase, but the best thing is that your dream becomes great, your deeds increase, and you compete with people in Servants of God, if you do good, you will praise God, and if you do evil, you will ask God for forgiveness."
"35728","(35728) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Umm Al-Darda’, On the authority of Abu Darda’, he said: Contemplating an hour is better than staying up all night."
"35729","(35729) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Umm Al-Darda’, He said: It was said to her: What was the best work of Abu Darda’? She said: Contemplation."
"35730","(35730) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Muawiyah ibn Salih, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, he said: Those whose tongues are still wet from the remembrance of God will enter Paradise while they are They laugh."
"35731","(35731) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Muhammad that Abu Aoun He told him that Abu Al-Darda’ used to say: I have not spent a night in the morning when people did not look at me except... I saw that God had bestowed upon me a blessing."
"35732","(35732) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Fayyad, on the authority of Abu Hazim, who said: Umm al-Darda’ said to Abu al-Darda’ : The old man comes and prays, and the young man comes and does not pray. Abu Al-Darda’ said: Each for a reward that has been prepared for him."
"35733","(35733) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Jaafar, he said: Saleh bin Abi Araib told me, on the authority of many Ibn Murra Al-Hadrami said: I heard Abu Al-Darda’ say: Shall I not inform you of the best of your deeds? The most beloved of them to your king. And it is better for you in your grades than to attack your enemy and have them strike your necks and you strike their necks. Of giving dinars and dirhams. They said: What is that, O Abu Darda? He said: The remembrance of God, and the remembrance of God is greater."
"35734","(35734) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abu Darda’, he said: I command you. Of the matter, and I do not do it, but I hope for it reward, and indeed the people I hate most to be treated unjustly are those who seek no help from me except By God"
"35735","(35735) Affan told us, he said: Wahib told us, he said: Musa bin Uqba told us, he said: Bilal bin Saad told me. Al-Kindi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, that whenever he mentioned the world, he would say: It is cursed, cursed is it. There it is."
"35736","(35736) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of Mu’awiyah ibn Qurayh, who said: Abu Darda’ fell ill, so they visited him and said: What thing do you complain about? He said: My sins. It was said: What thing do you complain about? He said: Jinnah. It was said: We will call a doctor for you. He said: He made me lie down."
"35737","(35737) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: A sheikh from among us, called: Al-Hakam bin Al-Fadhil, narrated to us, on the authority of Zaid bin He converted to Islam. He said: Abu Darda’ said: Seek what is best for you, and be exposed to the scents of God’s mercy, for God has abundant blessings. His mercy befalls whomever He wishes of His servants, and ask God to cover your faults and secure your splendor."
"35738","(35738) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Sulaym ibn Amir, on the authority of Abu al-Darda`, he said: What a good fast you made. A man's home is where he guards his tongue and his sight. Beware of the market, for it is distorted and distracted."
"35739","(35739) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Aoun bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Darda’, he said: Who He inspects and loses, and he who does not prepare patience for the calamitous matters will fail. He said: Abu Darda’ said: If you accuse people, they will repel you, and if you I left them and they did not leave you. He said: What do you command me to do? He said: Lend from your wealth for the day of your poverty."
"35740","(35740) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amr ibn Murr, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, who said: While Abu Al-Darda’ He was burning under a pot for him while Salman was there when Abu Darda’ heard a sound in the pot, then the sound rose with a whimper like a sound. The boy, he said: Then the pot was lowered and stopped, then it returned to its place and nothing had been poured from it, so Abu Darda’ made He called out: O Salman, look at the wonder. Look at something the likes of which you have never seen, nor has your father. Salman said: But Indeed, if you had been silent, you would have heard of the major verses of God."
"35741","(35741) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Al-Mughiriya, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, he said: Abu Al-Darda’ said: The thing I fear most when I stand on the account is that it will be said to me: You knew, so you did not do what you knew."
"35742","(35742) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr bin Murah, or someone else, On the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Jaad, he said: Two bulls passed by Abu Al-Darda’ while they were working, so one of them got up and the other got up, so Abu said Al-Darda': This is taken into account."
"35743","(35743) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ghaylan bin Bishr, on the authority of Ya’la bin Al-Walid, he said: I was I walk with Abu al-Darda’. He said: I said: O Abu al-Darda’, what you love for the one you love. He said: Death. He said: I said to him: If he does not die He said: His money and his children are declining."
"35744","(35744) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Saad Al-Ansari, who said: Abdullah bin Zaid bin narrated to me. Rabi`a al-Dimashqi said: Abu al-Darda` said: One night she entered the mosque, and when she entered, she passed by a man who was... He was prostrating and saying: O God, I am afraid and seeking refuge, so protect me from Your torment, and I am a poor beggar, so grant me protection from Your bounty, no. I am innocent of sin, so I apologize, and I am not strong, so I defend myself, but I am guilty, asking for forgiveness. He said: So Abu Darda’ became He teaches them to his friends out of admiration for them."
"35745","(35745) Yahya bin Abi Bukair told us, he said: Shuabi told us, he said: Yazid bin Khumayr al-Shami told us. He said: Suleiman bin Murthad informed me. He said: I heard his son Abu Darda’ narrating on the authority of Abu Darda’. He said: If only you knew what I know that you laughed a little, and you cried a lot, and you went out crying, not knowing whether you would be saved, or whether you would not be saved."
"35746","(35746) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Saksaki, who said: Our companions narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’, he said: If you wish, I will swear to you: The most beloved of God’s servants are those who love God, and those who love God are those who are considerate. The sun, the moon, the stars, and the shadows for the remembrance of God."
"35747","(35747) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, he said: Abu Darda’ wrote To Muslimah bin Mukhlid, who was a governor in Egypt: As for what follows, if the servant acts in obedience to God, God will love him, and if he loves him God loved him to his creation, and when God hated him, he made him hate his creation."
"35748","(35748) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, that he said: Why do I see your scholars leaving, and I see your generations not learning? Learn before the flag is raised, for if it is raised Knowledge is the go of scholars. Why do I see you eager for what I have entrusted you with, and neglecting what you have been entrusted with, because I know best. The worst of you are those who go out on horseback, they are the ones who do not come to prayer except in the back, and do not hear the Qur’an except in the desert, and do not Their freed ones will be freed."
"35749","(35749) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salem, who said: A man went up to Abu Darda’ and he was sitting on top of a house gathering. Out of love, he said: It was as if the man was ashamed of him and came back, so Abu Al-Darda’ said: Come, for one of your jurisprudents is he who is kind to you in your livelihood."
"35750","(35750) Ali bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Ibn Mubarak, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, he said: He informed me. Ismail bin Ubaidullah said: Umm al-Darda’ told me that Abu al-Darda’ had fainted, then he woke up and behold, his son Bilal. With him, he said: Get up and leave me, then he said: Who works for the same as my resting place? Who works for the same as this hour? And We will change their hearts and their eyes as they did not believe in Him the first time, and We will leave them blind in their transgression. She said, “Then he fainted and stayed there for a while, then he woke up and said something like that.” He kept repeating it until he was arrested."
"35751","(35751) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Ali bin Ata’, he said: Tamim bin Ghaylan bin Salamah narrated to me, he said: A man came to Abu al-Darda’ while he was sick, and he said: O Abu al-Darda’, you have arrived on the verge of parting with this world, so comfort me. With something that God will benefit me with, and I will remind you of, He said: You are a healthy mother, so perform the prayer and pay the zakat if it is yours. Money, fast during Ramadan and avoid immoral acts, then give good tidings. The man told Abu Darda’ again, and Abu Darda’ told him the same thing. Then the man shook off his robe, then said: {Indeed, those who conceal the clear proofs and the guidance We have sent down after We have made them clear to the people} To his saying: {And those who curse will curse them} Then Abu al-Darda’ said: Ali the man, so he came, and Abu al-Darda’ said: What did you say? He said: I was a man who was a teacher and you had knowledge that I did not have, so you wanted to tell me something that God would benefit me with, but you did not answer. I have to say anything except one thing, so Abu Al-Darda’ said to him: Sit down, then understand what I am telling you: Where are you from the day when you have no land? Except the width of two cubits by the length of four cubits. Your family will accept you, who did not like you being separated or sitting. And your brothers, they made perfect buildings for you and increased the dust for you, and they left you to do that, and two black angels have come to you. Two blue hairs, their names are Munkar and Nakir. So they made you sit down, then they asked you: Who are you and what were you like? And what do you say about this man? If you say: By God, I don’t know, I heard the people. They said: A word, so I said what the people said. By God, I responded. And if you say, “Muhammad is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace,” and God has sent down His Book to him, then I believe in him and in what he came. Through it, by God, you have been saved and converted, and you will not be able to do that except with confirmation from God, despite the hardship and fear you see, then Where are you from the day when you have nothing of the earth except the place of your feet, and a day whose duration was fifty thousand years, people? In it there is a standing position for the Lord of the worlds, and there is no shade except the shadow of the throne of the Lord of the worlds, and the sun is brought near, so if you are among the people of the shadow, then you have By God, you have been saved and have been guided, but if you were one of the people of the sun, by God, you have been returned and fallen. Then where are you from the Day that comes? Hell has blocked what is between those who fail, and it is said: You will not enter Paradise until you enter Hell. If you have light, it will set you straight. The path, by God, you have been saved and guided, and if there is no light with you, some of the hooks of Hell will cling to you, or Like her words, or her youth, by God, she has become weak and has fallen into disrepair. By God, Abu Darda’, what I say is true, so understand what I say. I say it"
"35752","(35752) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamiyah, he said: Abu Al-Darda’ said: I was a merchant before he was sent. Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and when Muhammad was sent, trade and worship became intertwined, but they did not come together, so the slaves took and left. Trade"
"35753","(35753) Ali bin Ubaid narrated to us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Muhammad bin Wasi’, who said: Abu Al-Darda’ said to his son: Son, let the mosque be your home, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says: Mosques are the homes of the righteous, so whoever has the mosque as his home, God will guarantee his soul, mercy, and passage on the Path. To heaven (Bazzar 434)"
"35754","(35754) Zayd ibn Harun told us, saying: Muhammad ibn Mutarrif Abu Ghassan informed us, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ Ibn Yassar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: Whoever goes to the mosque in the morning, or goes to... The mosque, God has prepared for him in Paradise as a place to stay whenever he comes in the morning or at the end. (Bukhari 662 and Muslim 463)"
"35755","(35755) Zaid bin Harun told us, saying: Uyaynah bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Ayyub bin Musa, on the authority of Abi Hazim, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, said: The mosques of the servants of God have pegs. They asked about them, and if they were sick, they treated them, and if they were in need, they helped them. (Ahmed 418)"
"35756","(35756) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Maqil, he said: We were We say that the mosque is a strong fortress from Satan."
"35757","(35757) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, he said: My uncle Musa bin Yasar narrated to me that Salman wrote To Abu Darda’: In the shadow of the throne there is a man whose heart is attached to the mosques out of his love for them."
"35758","(35758) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Al-Eizar, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, on the authority of Omar, he said: Mosques are the houses of God on earth, and it is the duty of the one who visits them to honor his visitors."
"35759","(35759) Shababi bin Siwar narrated to us, saying: Hariz narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Awf, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Masoud Al-Fazari, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, said: There is no man who goes to the mosque in the morning for something good that he learns, or teaches, except that God has ordained for him the reward of a mujahid, and he will not turn back except as a spoilsman."
"35760","(35760) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Salman, who said: Whoever performs ablution, does it well. Then he came to the mosque to pray there. He was a visitor to God, and it is the duty of a visitor to honor his visitor. (Tabarani 10324)"
"35761","(35761) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Umar ibn Abi Bakr, on the authority of Ubayyah, on the authority of Ka’b al-Ahbar, said: I find in the Book of God: There is no believing servant who goes to the mosque in the morning and does not return. And he goes only to learn something good, or to teach it, or to remember God, or to remind him of it, except that he is like him in the Book of God. Like a mujahid in the path of God."
"35762","(35762) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: Omar bin Al-Khattab entered upon Abu Ubaidah bin The surgeon, then, was lying on his saddle, leaning against the bag. He said: Then Omar said to him: Don’t you tell what your companions told? He said: : O Commander of the Faithful, this tells me the story."
"35763","(35763) Abu Asama told us, he said: Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah told us, he said: Thabit Al-Bunani told us, he said: Abu Ubaidah ibn al-Jarrah was the prince of the Levant, and he addressed the people and said: O people, I am a man from the Quraysh, and by God I am not I know whether I am red or black, prefer me with the fear of God, unless I wish to be in slaughterhouse."
"35764","(35764) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, saying: Hariz ibn Uthman narrated to us, on the authority of Nimran ibn Mikhmar al-Rahbi, he said: It was Abu Ubaidah ibn al-Jarrah was marching in the army and he said: There is no God who bleaches his clothes desecrates his religion. My Lord, He honors Himself, and He is in disgrace to Him. Unless you replace old evil deeds with modern good deeds, for if one of you whatever is between the heavens and the earth, then he does good. His evil deeds will prevail until they are vanquished."
"35765","(35765) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Thabit told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: I came to Abu Ubaidah. Ibn al-Jarrah, so he put me down in the vicinity of his house, and his wife in the vicinity of it, with a screen between us, and he was milking the camel. Then he brought the vessel and placed it in my hand, and a man from the freedmen said to him: Shall you go down to your house with your wife? He said: I will keep watch with him for a caravan that, if I were to meet one who was martyred, would have taken shelter on every vehicle."
"35766","(35766) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Khalid ibn Ma`dan, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah ibn al-Jarrah, he said : The heart of a believer is like a bird, turning over so-and-so and so-and-so."
"35767","(35767) Abd al-Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Yahya bin Abd al-Rahman bin Hatib, he said: He said: Abu Waqid Al-Laythi: We pursued the best deeds, but we did not find anything more helpful in seeking the afterlife than abstinence in this world."
"35768","(35768) Yazeed bin Harun and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qays, who said: Al-Zubayr said: Ibn Al-Awwam: Whoever among you is able to have any good deed hidden, let him do it."
"35769","(35769) Aswad bin Amir told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, that Al-Zubayr was sent to Egypt It was said to him: It has the plague, and he said: We only came to it for the plague and the plague."
"35770","(35770) Abbad bin Al-Awwam narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Jabir, who said: None of us realized that. The world has no one but Abdullah bin Umar."
"35771","(35771) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: No one is afflicted with this world except A decrease in his status with God, even if He is Most Generous to Him."
"35772","(35772) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: I have not seen anyone more pious than Ibn Umar."
"35773","(35773) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: It cannot be a man. He is one of the people of knowledge, such that he does not envy those above him, does not despise those below him, and does not seek a price for his knowledge."
"35774","(35774) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salim bin Abi al-Ja`d, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: It does not reach He is a servant of true faith until he considers people foolish in his religion."
"35775","(35775) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdul Malik bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, he said: I entered Ali Ibn Omar, and behold, he was spread out on his arm, covering himself with a pillow stuffed with fiber."
"35776","(35776) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Qays, on the authority of Atiyah, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The believer faces When he came out of his grave, he had the best image he had ever seen. He would say to her: Who are you? She would say to him: I am the one who was with you. This world, I will not leave it until I admit you to Paradise."
"35777","(35777) Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of his leaders, who said: It was said to Ibn Umar: They were the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. Do they laugh with each other? He said: Yes, and faith is firmer in their hearts than the firm mountains."
"35778","(35778) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of the one who narrated to him, who said: If Ibn Umar saw him, he would think that he was Something about following the footsteps of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"35779","(35779) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, that Ibn Umar said: I did not put bricks on bricks, nor planted palm trees. Since the death of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"35780","(35780) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who hated to lead in prayer. Miles of stone made by Marwan."
"35781","(35781) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Al-Salik, on the authority of Abu Sahl, who said: I heard Ibn Umar, he said in this verse: : {Every soul is pledged for what it has earned, except those on the right hand}"
"35782","(35782) Hushaym told us, he said: Ali bin Ata told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he said Lahmran: Do not impose a duty upon God that he will not fulfill, for on the Day of Resurrection there will be no dinars or dirhams, but He will reward you. People with their deeds."
"35783","(35783) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: I was informed on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to say: I My companions are on a matter, and if I dissent from them, I fear that I will not join them."
"35784","(35784) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Ibn Umar {or a creation of what grows within your breasts} He said: Death: If you were death, I would give you life."
"35785","(35785) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: {Then he attacked the mountain.} He said: A mountain. An earthquake in hell. (Ibn Jarir 201)"
"35786","(35786) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Sulaym, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He did not recite these verses. Never except that He cried: {Whether you reveal what is within yourselves or conceal it, Allah will call to account you for it}"
"35787","(35787) Affan bin Muslim told us, he said: Khalid bin Abi Uthman told us, he said: Salit bin Abdullah told us, he said: He said: Ibn Omar: Seek good, but do not see evil."
"35788","(35788) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabala bin Suhaim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, and about the pre-dawn meal. They ask for forgiveness. He said: They pray."
"35789","(35789) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham bin Saad told us, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: Ibn Umar used to work in private. He himself does not do something to people."
"35790","(35790) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Whenever Ibn Umar woke up at night Pray"
"35791","(35791) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Amr bin Maymun informed us, on the authority of his father, he said: It was said to Ibn Omar: Zayd bin Haritha died and left behind one hundred thousand dirhams. He said: But do not leave it."
"35792","(35792) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Waqid, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Abdullah ibn Umar said this verse: For those who believe, lest their hearts submit to the remembrance of God. (Abu Naim 305)"
"35793","(35793) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Mawdud, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he was on the way to Mecca, saying: At the head of his mount, he bends it and says: Perhaps a khof will fall upon a khuff, meaning the sandals of the Prophet’s mount, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"35794","(35794) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Adam bin Ali, who said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: They disobeyed the Sunnah of the polytheists."
"35795","(35795) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Fudayl bin Marzuq, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Ibn Umar: {By your Lord, We will surely ask them. All together} He said: On the authority of there is no god but Allah."
"35796","(35796) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Idris, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Ibn Umar: {And when the word falls upon them, We expel They have creatures of the earth that speak to them. He said: When they do not enjoin what is right, nor forbid what is wrong. (Hakim 485)"
"35797","(35797) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Nafi’, that when Ibn Umar recited the Qur’an, he hated to speak. Or he did not speak until he had finished what he wanted, or he did not speak until he had finished except on a day when I had charged him. While he was reading the Qur’an, he came to a verse and said: Do you know what it was revealed about?"
"35798","(35798) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Maimun, on the authority of his father, who said: Ibn Umar entered among some of his companions. Ali Abdullah bin Aamir bin Kuraiz while he was sick and they saw that he was dying, so they said to him: Give good news, for you have dug up the menstrual cycle. On Arafat, the pilgrim to the House of God begins, and wells are dug by the deserts. He said: And they mentioned some of the qualities of goodness. He said: So they said: We hope for the best for you, God willing. Ibn Umar was sitting and not speaking. When speech slowed down for him, he said: O Abu Abd. The Most Gracious, what you say, and He said: If the earning is good, then the expenditure is good, and it will be restored and you will know."
"35799","(35799) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Ibn Abjar, on the authority of Thawair, who said: Ibn Umar passed through Khirbih and a man was with him. So he said: Call out, so he chanted, but Ibn Omar did not answer him. Then he said to him: Call out, so Ibn Omar answered him: They left and I stayed. Their deeds"
"35800","(35800) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Al-Taymiyyah, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Salman, he said: When God created Adam, he said: One for me and one for you, and one between you and me. As for the one that is mine, you shall worship Me, not associating anything with Me. As for what you have done, I have rewarded you for it, and as for what is between you and me, it is from you to ask and pray, and upon me. The answer"
"35801","(35801) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Salman, he said: She was the wife of Pharaoh. She was tormented by the sun, but when they turned away from it, the angels shaded her with their wings, and she could see her home in Paradise."
"35802","(35802) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, that Salman and Abdullah bin Greetings, they met each other, and one of them said to his companion: If you meet your Lord, tell me what you find from Him, and if I meet you, I will inform you. Then one of them died, and his companion met him in a dream, and he said: Trust and give good news, for I have never seen anything like trust. They said: Three times"
"35803","(35803) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Salim ibn Abi al-Ja’d, on the authority of Zayd ibn Suhan, On the authority of Salman, he prayed two rak’ahs before dawn. He said: So I told him, and he said: Keep yourself awake and He will keep you asleep."
"35804","(35804) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shimr, on the authority of some of his sheikhs, on the authority of Salman, who said: The people are the most sinful. On the Day of Resurrection, they will speak the most about disobeying God."
"35805","(35805) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin al-Ghaz, on the authority of Ubadah bin Nasi, who said: Salman had a hidden cloak."
"35806","(35806) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Habib bin Shahid, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, that Salman used to make Food is from his own earnings, so he invites the lepers and eats with them."
"35807","(35807) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Hamid, who said: I entered with my maternal uncle Abbad Ali Salman. When Salman saw him, he shook hands with him, and behold, he was shearing the wicker, and he said: It was bought for him for a dirham, so he was sorry. I will sell it for three, then I will give it in charity for a dirham, and I will put a dirham in it, and I will spend a dirham, even if Omar prohibits it. You're done"
"35808","(35808) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Jarir, he said: We came down to Al-Saffah, and lo! A man was sleeping in the shade of a tree when the sun had almost reached him. He said: So I said to the boy: Go with this boot and I will give him shade. When He woke up and it was Salman. He said: So I came to him and greeted him. He said: He said: O Jarir, humble yourself for the sake of God, for whoever humbles yourself is for the sake of God. May God raise him up on the Day of Resurrection. O Jarir, do you know what the darknesses will be on the Day of Resurrection? He said: I said: I do not know. He said: People were unfair to each other in this world, then he took a stick that I could hardly see between his two fingers, and said: O Jarir, if you ask The jinn is like this stick. You did not find it. He said: I said: O Abu Abdullah, where are the palm trees and the trees? He said: Their roots are pearls. And gold, and the highest is fruit."
"35809","(35809) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Salman, who said: If the servant remembers God In the good times, and He praises Him in the prosperity, then adversity befell him, so he called upon God. The angels said: A well-known voice from a weak man. So they will intercede for him, and if the servant does not remember God in the good times, nor praise Him in the prosperous things, and harm befalls him, then he supplicates to God. The angels said: An objectionable voice, but they did not intercede for it."
"35810","(35810) Abu Al-Ahwas and Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Salih bin Khabab, on the authority of Husain bin Uqba, He said: Salman said: Knowledge, no. It is said to be like a treasure that cannot be spent."
"35811","(35811) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, he said: My uncle Musa bin Yasar narrated to me that Salman wrote To Abu Darda’, “Indeed, under the throne is a just Imam, one with wealth who gives in charity and hides his right hand from his left, and a man whom she invites.” A beautiful woman of honor and position in herself, and he said: I fear God, Lord of the worlds, and a man who grew up and was in company with him. And his youth and strength were in the work that God loves and is pleased with, and a man whose heart was hanging in the mosques out of his love for it, and a man He mentioned God, and his eyes overflowed with tears out of fear of God, and two men met, and he said: One of them is for the other. Indeed, I love you. In God, and He wrote to him: “Knowledge is like springs, and with it God benefits whomever He wills, and an example of His wisdom is not spoken of.” Like a body that has no soul, and like knowledge that is not practiced, like a treasure that cannot be spent, and like a scholar like a man who has lost his light. He has a lamp on the road, and he makes people shine with it, and everyone calls to it."
"35812","(35812) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Hamid bin Ja’far narrated to us, on the authority of his father, that Salman used to say: There are people who carry an illness and a cure, and the key to good and the key to evil."
"35813","(35813) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Shimr, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, he said: Salman came to my father. Al-Darda'a and he did not find him, so he greeted Umm Al-Darda'a and said: Where is my brother? She said: In the mosque, and he is wearing her cloak. Qatwaniyah, so she threw a pillow to him, but he refused to sit on it. He twisted his turban and threw it away, so he sat on it. He said: Abu al-Darda’ came and hung meat for two dirhams, so Umm al-Darda’ got up, cooked it and baked it, then brought the food. Abu Al-Darda’ was fasting, so Salman said: Who will eat with me? He said: Umm Al-Darda’ will eat with you, so he did not leave him until he broke his fast. Then Salman said to Umm al-Darda’, and she saw her in bad condition: What’s the matter with you? She said: Your brother does not want women, so he fasts during the day. And he would stand up all night, so he spent the night with him, so Abu Darda’ made him want to stand up, so he imprisoned him until it was before dawn, so he stood up. So he performed ablution and prayed rak’ahs. He said: Then Abu Darda’ said to him: You have prevented me from praying, so Salman said to him: Pray, sleep, fast, and break your fast. Your family has a right over you, and your eyes have a right over you."
"35814","(35814) Abu Asama told us, he said: Othman bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Abu Othman Al-Nahdi, on the authority of Salman and others. The companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The man will come on the Day of Resurrection having done a deed with which he hopes to be saved. He said: A man keeps coming to you and complaining about his wrongdoing, then some of his good deeds are taken and given to him until what remains of his. Good, and the accuser comes and complains of wrongdoing, and some of his bad deeds are taken and placed on top of his bad deeds, then he is cast down. Into the fire, or thrown into the fire."
"35815","(35815) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Salman, who said: If the two men spent the night together He gives the old man the whites, and if the other spent the night reciting the Qur’an and remembering God, I would have seen that the one who remembers God is better."
"35816","(35816) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Salim ibn Abi al-Ja`d, on the authority of Zayd ibn Suhan, On the authority of Salman, that when he woke up at night, he would say: Glory be to the Lord of the prophets and to the God of the messengers."
"35817","(35817) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bā, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Salamah, who said: When Salman He slaughtered a sheep from the sheep, cut its flesh, made its skin watered, and made its wool a rope. If he saw a man in need He gave it to a rope for his horse, and if he saw a man in need of water, he gave it to him."
"35818","(35818) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abu al-Bakhtari, who said: Salman was accompanied by a man from Banu Abs, then the quagmire came, and Salman said to him: Drink, so he drank, then he said to him: Drink, so he drank, then he said to him: Drink, So he drank, then he said to him: O brother of Banu Abs, do you think that this drink of yours has reduced anything from the water of the quagmire? And so is knowledge. It will not run out, so seek knowledge that will benefit you. Then he passed by a nearby river, and behold, he was fed and piled high, and he said: O brother of my son. He frowned, for He who was in control of its treasuries, while Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, was alive, and they used to go in the evening and in the morning, and what Among them was a bunch of wheat. Then he mentioned Jalawla, and what God had made good for the Muslims in it, so he said: O brother of Banu Abs. Indeed, God He gave you this and authorized you. He had power over it and Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, was alive."
"35819","(35819) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Nafi’ ibn Jubayr ibn Mut’im, that Hudhayf and Salman They said: To a foreign woman: “Are we a pure place where we can pray?” She said: Purify your heart and pray wherever you wish. He said: One of them for its owner: jurisprudence."
"35820","(35820) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: Salman Al-Farisi said to me: The market is the spawn of Satan. And its hatchery. If you can not be the first to enter it, nor the last to leave it, then do so."
"35821","(35821) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Ammar bin Ruzaiq, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Aws bin Damaj, he said: We said: To Salman: O Abu Abdullah, won’t you speak to us? He said: Remembering God is the greatest, providing food, spreading greetings, and prayer. And the people are sleeping."
"35822","(35822) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Salman, he said: Indeed, God is ashamed. That a servant extends his hand to Him and asks Him for something good, and He returns them both disappointed."
"35823","(35823) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Misra and Al-Mughirah bin Shubayl, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, he said: I had an older brother, nicknamed Abu Ezra, and he often mentioned Salman, so I used to miss him. When he met him, his brother mentioned him frequently. One day, he said to him: Do you have anything to do with Abu Abdullah? Al-Qadisiyah had descended. He said: And when Salman came from the battle, Al-Qadisiyah would camp, and when he came from Hajj, he would descend on Al-Madain as a conqueror. He said: I said: Yes, he said: So we set off until we entered upon him in a house in Al-Qadisiyah, and he was sitting, explaining His feet are rags, and he is sewing a ginger, or tanning his nails. He said: So we greeted him and sat down. He said: So he said: O son of My brother, you must follow the intention, for it is more conveyed."
"35824","(35824) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Omar ibn Qais, on the authority of Amr ibn Abi Qurayh al-Kindi, he said: He presented Salman’s father refused to marry his sister to her, but he refused and married her to his master. She is also called Buqayra. He said: So he informed Abu He read that there was something going on between Hudhayf and Salman, so he came to him to ask for him, and he was informed that he was in a place of his. So he went to him and found him with a gingerbread with greens in it. He had inserted his stick into the gingerbread’s loop while it was on his shoulders."
"35825","(35825) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Salman, who said: The sun will give a free person on the Day of Resurrection. Ten years, then come close to the people’s skulls until you are close to two corners. He said: Then they will sweat until the sweat drips into the ground at a level. Then it rises until the man gargles. Salman said: Until the man says: gargle, gargle."
"35826","(35826) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Abdullah bin Hubaira, he said: Abu Dardaad wrote To Salman: As for what follows, I invite you to the Holy Land and the land of Jihad. He said: Then Salman wrote to him: As for what follows, you have I wrote to you inviting me to the Holy Land and the land of Jihad, and by my life the land sanctifies its people, but one May His deeds sanctify Him."
"35827","(35827) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Abu Dharr, He said: By God, if you knew what I know, you would have cried much and laughed little, and if you had known what I know, you would not have rejoiced. Your wives, and do not throw yourselves on your beds, and go out into the ascents, bellowing and weeping. By God, if God had created me on the day He created me as a tree to be supported and whose fruit can be eaten."
"35828","(35828) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Mujjil, on the authority of Ibn Imran bin Hattan, on the authority of his father, he said: He said Abu Dharr: A righteous companion is better than a lonely person, and a lonely companion is better than a bad companion, and a person who does good things is better than a silent person. He who is silent is better than one who is filled with evil, a trust is better than a seal, and a seal is better than the thought of evil.\n(Ibn Hibban 1010 Hakim 343)"
"35829","(35829) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Dharr, who said: Dhu Two dirhams on the Day of Resurrection will be more severe in reckoning than the one who possessed the dirhams."
"35830","(35830) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymiy, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: It was said: To him: Don’t you take a land as Talhah and Al-Zubayr took? He said: Then he said: I will not do it by being a prince. A drink of water, wine, or milk is sufficient for me every day, and in sum, a handful of wheat."
"35831","(۳۵۸۳۱) حَدَّثَنَا مُحَمَّدُ بْنُ بِشْرٍ الْعَبْدِیُّ ، عَنْ عَمْرِو بْنِ مَیْمُونٍ ، عَنْ أَبِیہِ ، عَنْ رَجُلٍ مِنْ بَنِی سُلَیْمٍ ، یُقَالَ لَہُ : عَبْدُ اللہِ بْنُ سِیدَانَ ، قَالَ : صَحِبْت أَبَا ذَرٍّ ، فَقَالَ لِی : أَلاَ أُخْبِرُک بِیَوْمِ حَاجَتِی ، إنَّ یَوْمَ"
"35832","(۳۵۸۳۲) حَدَّثَنَا أَبُو مُعَاوِیَۃَ ، عَنْ مُوسَی بْنِ عُبَیْدَۃَ ، عَنْ عَبْدِ اللہِ بْنِ خِرَاشٍ ، قَالَ : رَأَیْتُ أَبَا ذَرٍّ بِالرَّبَذَۃِ ، وَعِنْدَہُ امْرَأَۃٌ لَہُ سَحْمَائُ ، أَوْ شَحْبَائُ ، قَالَ : وَہُوَ فِی مِظَلَّۃٍ سَوْدَائَ ، قَالَ : فَقِیلَ لَہُ : یَا Abu Dharr, if I were to take a woman who was superior to this, he said: And he said: By God, if I were to take a woman who would subdue me, I would love to إلَیَّ مِنْ أَنْ أَتَّخِذَ امْرَأَۃً تَرْفَعُنِی ، قَالُوا : یَا أَبَا ذَرٍّ ، إنَّک مُرْزَؤٌ مَا یَکَادُ یَبْقَی لَک وَلَدٌ ، قَالَ : فَقَالَ : إِنَّا نَحْمَدُ اللَّہَ الَّذِی یَأْخُذُہُمْ مِنَّا فِی دَارِ الْفَنَائِ وَیَدَّخِرْہُم لَنَا فِی دَارِ الْبَقَائِ ، قَالَ : وَکَانَ یَجْلِسُ عَلَی The sackcloth and the shackles cut him off. He said: They said: O Abu Dharr, if you took a rug that was softer than this rug of yours, he said: And he said: اللَّہُمَّ غُفْرًا ، خُذْ مَا أُوتِیت ، إنَّمَا خُلِقْنَا لِدَارٍ لَہَا نَعْمَلُ وَإِلَیْہَا نَرْجِعُ۔"
"35833","(35833) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of his father, who said: Abu Al-Darda’ was sent A messenger was sent to Abu Dharr. He said: Then the messenger came and said: To Abu Dharr: Your brother Abu Darda’ is greeting you and saying to you: Beware of fear. God and fear the people. He said: Then Abu Dharr said: What do I have to do with the people? I have left for them their whites and their yellows. Then he said to the Messenger: He went to the house, he said: So he went with him, he said: When he entered his house, he saw a piece of food on his cloak, not much, and it had Some of it spread out, he said: So Abu Dharr started sweeping it and wrapping it in the abaya, he said: Then he said: From the jurisprudence of the man He was kind in his livelihood. He said: Then a piece of food was brought and placed in his hands. He said: Then he said to me: Eat. He said: So the man made He hated to put his hand in food because of his lack of food. He said: Then Abu Dharr said to him: Put your hand, by God, because we I am more afraid of my abundance than I am of my lack of it. He said: So the man ate, then he returned to Abu Darda’ and told him what he had responded to. He said: Abu Al-Darda': The Khadra's have never given shade, nor have the Ghubrah's given less shade, to someone whose speech is more truthful than yours, O Abu Dharr."
"35834","(35834) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Al-Munkadir, he said: He sent Habib bin Muslimah, when he was in the Levant, came to Abu Dharr with three hundred dinars, and he said: Use it for your need, so Abu said Dhar: Go back with it, for he has not found anyone more deceived by God than us. We have nothing but a shadow to hide ourselves with, and a third of sheep that go about upon us. And our lady has given us alms for her service, and I am not afraid of the bounty."
"35835","(35835) Affan bin Muslim narrated to us, he said: Ali bin Masad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah Al-Rumi narrated to us, he said: I entered upon a mother He divorced, and she told him that she went to Abu Dharr and gave him some flour and wheat, so he put it in a party. Her dress, and he said: Your reward is from God. So I said to her: O Umm Talaq, how did you see the appearance of Abu Dharr? She said: Oh. Son, I saw him disheveled and pale, and I saw in his hand fluffy wool and two sticks that he had quarreled between as he was spinning from that Wool"
"35836","(35836) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Al-Numan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Aqna’. Al-Bailili, on the authority of Al-Ahnaf ibn Qais, who said: I was sitting in the mosque of Medina when a man approached, whom no group of people could see, but they fled. From there, he reached the circle that I was in, so I remained steadfast and they fled, so I said: Who are you? Then Abu Dharr, the companion of the Messenger of God, said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I said: People do not flee from you. He said: I forbid them from treasures. I said: Our gifts It has reached its peak and has risen, so we fear it. He said: As for today, it is not, but it is about to be the price of your debt. So they called them and her."
"35837","(35837) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of his brother Mutrif, he said: Imran bin Husayn: I am telling you a story in the hope that God will benefit you with it after today. Know that the choices of servants in the sight of God are those who are praised. (Ahmed 434)"
"35838","(35838) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Ashhab, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: Imran ibn al-Husayn was afflicted with afflictions that He said: Then some of those who came to him said to him: He will prevent me from giving you what we see of you. He said: So do not do it. By God, if I love him, I will love him."
"35839","(35839) Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Adiy, on the authority of al-Sanabihi, on the authority of Muadh, he said: It will not go away. The servant's two feet on the Day of Resurrection until he will be asked about four characteristics: about his body and how it has worn it out, and about his life and how it has worn it. How he spent it, and about his wealth from where he earned it and on what he spent it, and about his knowledge of how he used it. (Tabarani 111, Bazzar 3437)"
"35840","(35840) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: A man came to Muadh bin Jabal with his companions to greet him. And they bid him farewell and entrusted him, and Muadh said to him: I have enjoined upon you two things: if you keep them, then you will keep them. Your share of this world, and you are more in need of your share of the Hereafter, so prefer your share of the Hereafter over your share of worldly life, for he will come to you, or pass by you, having your share of the worldly life, and he will prepare for you in a regular manner, and then he will disappear. With you wherever you go."
"35841","(35841) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Qutba, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shimr, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, he said: Mu'adh had a sore in his throat, so he said: He choked me. He choked you, and I strengthened you. Indeed, I love you."
"35842","(35842) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Amr ibn Murr, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Salamah, who said: Muadh said: Pray. And sleep and fast and break your fast and earn, and do not sin, and do not die unless you are a Muslim, and beware of supplications, or supplications Oppressed"
"35843","(35843) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Jami’ bin Shaddad, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Hilal Al-Muharbibi, he said: He said: Muadh bin Jabal: Sit in us and we will believe in time, meaning we will remember God."
"35844","(35844) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Imran bin Zayd bin Nashit, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Khaled Al-Walbi, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: God says: O son of Adam, devote yourself to My worship. I will fill your heart with wealth and eliminate your poverty. Otherwise, I will fill your hands with work and alleviate your poverty. (Tirmidhi 2466. Ahmad 358)"
"35845","(35845) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: No. The believer is detained until he sees good news, and when he is arrested, he calls out, there is not a living creature in the house, small or large, except You will not hear his voice except the heavy ones: the jinn and mankind, hasten him to the Most Merciful of the Merciful. When he is placed on his bed, he will say: What As slowly as you walk, then when he is brought into its confines, he will sit and be shown his seat in Paradise, and what God has prepared for him, and it will be filled with His grave is of spirit, basil, and musk. He said: Then it will be said: O Lord, bring me forward. He said: Then it will be said: It has not come for you. Indeed, you have brothers. And sisters when they catch up, but he slept soundly. Abu Hurairah said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, no young man sleeps. He is a soft eater, and there is no girl in this world whose sleep is shorter, nor sweeter than his, until he raises his head to the glad tidings. On the Day of Resurrection"
"35846","(35846) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, he said: Ibn Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid bin Bab, he said: I used to express myself to my father. He saw someone treating him, and a man passed by him and said: Where do you want, so-and-so? He said: The market. He said: If you can buy death Before you come back, do it. He said: Then he turned to me and said: I fear God because of what I hasten to before Destiny."
"35847","(35847) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Malik, on the authority of Abu Hazim, who said: I passed with Abu Hurairah over a grave. He was recently buried, and he said: Two light rak'ahs of the kind of food you despise. This is more beloved to me than your worldly life."
"35848","(35848) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Abu Uthman, he said: He informed me on the authority of my father Hurairah, he said: God rewards the believer with a good deed with a thousand thousand good deeds. So I came to him and said: O Abu Hurairah, It has reached me that you say: God rewards the believer with a good deed with a thousand thousand good deeds. He said: Yes, and a thousand thousand good deeds, and in The Qur’an includes this: {Indeed, Allah does not wrong even the weight of an atom, and if it is a good deed, He will multiply it.} So who knows what that name is? The double {and He will give from Himself a great reward} He said: Paradise. (Ahmed 296)"
"35849","(35849) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of the common people, on the authority of Abu Hazim, who said: Abu Hurairah said: Whoever covers a creation God covers him with silk, and whoever covers him with something new, God covers him with silk."
"35850","(35850) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Fudail ibn Ghazwan, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that a man from The Ansar was a guest, and he had nothing but his sustenance and the sustenance of his youth, so he said to his wife: Make the child sleep. And he extinguished the lamp. He said: Then these verses were revealed: {And they prefer themselves over themselves, even though they were in poverty, and whoever is protected by scarcity. It is they who are the successful ones. (Bukhari 3798 and Muslim 172)"
"35851","(35851) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: If he dies When he is dead, the angels say: What he presented, and the people say: What he left behind."
"35852","(35852) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ubaid, a client of Abu Rum, who said: I passed with my father. He saw a palm tree and said: O God, feed us with dates that the sons of Adam do not enjoy."
"35853","(35853) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, the client of Talha, narrated to us, on the authority of Issa bin Talha, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: Fire shall not feed a man who has cried out of fear of God forever until the milk in him has returned. The udder, and dust for the sake of God and the smoke of Hell shall never gather in the nostrils of a Muslim man."
"35854","(35854) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Abdul-Wahid bin Qays, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Whoever extinguishes an evil from a believer, it is as if he had saved his life."
"35855","(35855) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Zuhayr, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: There is no good in Fluency in speech"
"35856","(35856) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Yahya, the client of Ja’di bin Hubira, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: A man passed by a dog lying next to a dog that was about to die of thirst, but he did not find anything He gave it to him to drink, so he took off his socks and scooped it out and watered it, so God held him accountable for it and admitted him into Paradise."
"35857","(35857) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salama, who said: I entered upon Abu Hurairah and he He was sick, so I hugged him from behind him and said: Oh God, heal Abu Hurairah. He said: Oh God, strengthen me."
"35858","(35858) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, who said: Abdullah bin Amr says: Leave what you are not familiar with, and do not speak about what does not concern you, and store your tongue as you store your expenses."
"35859","(35859) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Mu’awiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Sa’d al-Kala’i informed us. On the authority of Amr ibn Aidh al-Azdi, on the authority of Ghataif ibn al-Harith al-Kindi, who said: I and my companions sat with Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: I heard him say: When the servant was placed in the grave, he spoke to him and said: O son of Adam, did you not know that I Alone, the house of darkness, and the house of truth. O son of Adam, what has deceived you about me? You used to walk around me acres. He said: So I said: To Ghataif: O Abu Asmaa, what a sacrifice? He said: out of pride. Then my friend, who was older than me, said to him: So if he is a believer, he said: His grave was widened for him, his abode was made green, and his soul was taken up to Paradise."
"35860","(35860) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Kathir, On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: You will gather together and it will be said: Where are the poor and needy of this nation? Then they will stand out. He said: It is said: What do you have? He said: Then they say: O our Lord, we have been tested and patient, and you know best. He said: And I see it. He said: By the way. Money and authority other than us. He said: Then it will be said: You have spoken the truth. He said: Then they will enter the Garden before the rest of the people for a time, and there will remain a hardship. Judgment is upon those with wealth and authority. He said: I said: Where will the believers be at that time? He said: Chairs of light will be placed for them. And the clouds will shade them, and that day will be shorter for them than an hour of the day."
"35861","(35861) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: There is no Mullah They come together and remember God, except that God remembers them in an assembly more powerful and more honorable than theirs, and there is no assembly when they disperse that they do not disperse. Remember Allah, except that their gathering will be a regret for them on the Day of Resurrection."
"35862","(35862) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Sulayman al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, He said: We sent a woman to Abdullah bin Amr to ask him: What is the sin that God will not forgive? He said: There is no sin or deed from between the heavens and the earth from which a servant of God Almighty repents before death unless he repents. Aliyah"
"35863","(35863) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr He said: There is no one who does not meet God with a sin except Yahya bin Zakariya. Then he recited it: {And master and confinement} then he raised something. A small piece of land, and he said: He did not have anything like that with him. Then he slaughtered a slaughter."
"35864","(35864) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamiyah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: You came to him and he He looked at the Qur’an. He said: I said: What are you reading? He said: My party with which I stand tonight."
"35865","(35865) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah informed us, on the authority of Abu Imran Al-Juniy, that Abdullah Ibn Amr was sitting between us and there was fire between his hands as it gasped, so he said: By the one in whose hand is my soul, she seeks refuge in God. From the Great Fire, or he said: From the fire of Hell. He said: Then he saw the moon when it tended to set, and he said: By God, it is crying now."
"35866","(35866) Ja’far bin Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ziyad bin Alaqah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: I wished This is the tree."
"35867","(35867) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ali bin Ubaid, on the authority of Yahya bin Qamtita, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr said: The world is the prison of the believer and the paradise of the infidel. When the believer dies, his flock is evacuated and he wanders wherever he wishes. (Muslim 2272)"
"35868","(35868) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir, he said, I heard him say: The likeness of the son of Adam and the likeness of Death is like a man who had three friends, and he said to one of them: You do not have it, and he said: I have your money, so take from it what you want. And what you do not take is not yours. Then he said to the other: You do not have it. He said: I will take care of you. When you die, I will bury you and leave you alone. Then he said: For the third: What you have, so he said: I am with you wherever you are. He said: As for the first, his money is his. Whatever he takes is his, and whatever he does not take He does not belong to him. As for the second, it is his family. When he dies, they rise up over him, then they leave him alone. As for the third, he works for him wherever he is. He was with him, and wherever he went in, he went in with him."
"35869","(35869) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Jarir told us, he said: Someone who heard al-Nu’man bin Bashir told me: All destruction is to do evil deeds in a time of calamity."
"35870","(35870) Yazeed told us, he said: Hariz bin Othman told us, he said: Hibban bin Zaid Al-Sharaabi told me, he said and it was He was friendly to Al-Nu’man, and Al-Nu’man had used him to work on the Prophet. He said: Then he heard Al-Nu’man say: Indeed, God’s workers are guarantors of God. The workers of the children of Adam are not in charge of their security. He said: When al-Nu’man descended from his pulpit, he came to him and asked for his forgiveness, and said: What is the matter with you? He said: I heard you saying such and such."
"35871","(35871) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, who said: Abdullah fainted. Ibn Rawahiha, then his sister Amra started crying and saying: And his brother, and so-and-so and such-and-such, and she repeated it over him, so Ibn Rawahiha said When he woke up, I didn't say anything except that I was told: You are like that."
"35872","(35872) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qais, that Abdullah bin Rawahihi cried and his wife cried, and he said To her: What makes you cry? She said: I saw you crying, so I cried. He said: I was informed that I was coming, but I was not informed that I was coming."
"35873","(35873) Yahya bin Ali al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, who said: He said: Abdullah bin His souls: Oh God, I ask you for comfort that does not turn back and a bliss that does not run out."
"35874","(35874) Malik narrated to us, he said: Zuhair narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rawahih’s wife, Abdullah bin Rawahi had two mosques: a mosque in his house, and a mosque in his house, when he wanted to go out. He prayed in the mosque in his house, and when he entered, he prayed in the mosque in his house, and that was wherever he reached him. The prayer is closed."
"35875","(35875) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, he said: Al-Qasim narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Imamah, he said: Who He loves for the sake of God and hates for the sake of God and gives for the sake of God and withholds for the sake of God - then faith has been completed."
"35876","(35876) Shababah bin Siwar told us, he said: Jarir told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Misra al-Hadrami told us, he said: I heard Abu Imamah say: None of this nation will enter Hell except one who strays before God as the stray of a camel."
"35877","(35877) Shababah bin Siwar narrated to us, saying: Hariz narrated to me, saying: Al-Qasim narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu Imamah saying: Read the Qur’an, and do not be deceived by these suspended copies of the Qur’an. For God does not punish a heart that is aware of the Qur’an."
"35878","(35878) Shababah bin Siwar told us, he said: Jarir told me, on the authority of Habib bin Ubaid, he said: Abu Imamah was He tells us the hadith like a man who has to perform what he heard."
"35879","(35879) Abu Usama told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, he said: Ali bin Hakim told me, on the authority of Suleiman bin Abu Abdullah Al-Madani said: Abu Umamah Al-Baili, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was a He left his robe behind him on his journey, so I heard Ibn Umar saying: Whoever is pleased to look at a man who is performing Hajj, let him look at my father. In front of him"
"35880","(35880) Abdullah bin Sulaiman and Abdullah bin Numir told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, She said: I wished that when I died, I would be forgotten."
"35881","(35881) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Usama ibn Zayd, who said: Ishaq, the servant of Zaydah, narrated to me that Aisha, She said: Oh, if only it were a tree that glorified God and fulfilled its obligations, even though it was not created."
"35882","(35882) Shababah bin Siwar narrated to us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Arak, on the authority of Urwa, that he heard Aisha says: I wish I had not been created."
"35883","(35883) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Aisha said: Reduce sins, for you will never They met God with something similar to the small number of sins."
"35884","(35884) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Barda, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, She said: You call the best of servants to be humble."
"35885","(35885) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Tamim, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, he said: It was Aisha. She will divide seventy thousand and patch up her armor."
"35886","(35886) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Who is the account being discussed? On the Day of Resurrection, he will not be forgiven."
"35887","(35887) Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, he said: Abu Aqeel told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khalid told us, he said: Tell me. Abu Al-Safar said: Aisha said: People have lost the greatest pillar of their religion: piety."
"35888","(35888) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abbas, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: What The family of Muhammad was satisfied with whole food for more than three days. (Bukhari 5423, Muslim 2282)"
"35889","(35889) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: We used to stay for a month to get some kind of food. With fire, it is nothing but dates and water. (Bukhari 6458, Muslim 2282)"
"35890","(35890) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: No one is held accountable. On the Day of Resurrection, he will enter Paradise. Then I read: {But as for him who has been given his Book in his right hand, he will be given a proper account. An easy way} Then I read: {Criminals are known by their marks, and they are taken by their forelocks and their feet}"
"35891","(35891) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: If any of you wishes, let him multiply. He only asks his Lord."
"35892","(35892) Ja’far bin Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Aisha said: I wish I had a paper from This tree"
"35893","(35893) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed away. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, and there is nothing on my shelf that a human being would eat except a piece of barley on a shelf of mine. (Muslim 2282)"
"35894","(35894) Abu Asama told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told me, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Abi Mulki, he said: I heard Aisha say: A brave, bald man will be made over the infidel in his grave, and he will eat his flesh from his head to his feet. Then the meat is clothed and he eats from his feet to his head. Then the meat is clothed and he eats from his head to his head. His feet are like that."
"35895","(35895) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of Qays bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of Saad, he said: You saw us campaigning with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we had no provisions except the leaves of the rope and this brown sheep. One of us lays down as a sheep lays down, he has no confusion, then Banu Asad started taunting me for religion. I was disappointed and lost. Operation (Bukhari 37288 2277)"
"35896","(35896) Yazid bin Harun and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays bin Abi Hazim, who said: Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam said: Whoever of you is able to have any good deed hidden, let him do it."
"35897","(35897) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Salih bin Ibrahim bin Abdul Rahman bin Awf, He said: I asked a man from Jinnah. I said: What is the matter with Zaid bin Khalid Al-Janni? The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, informed him. He said: He did not do what they did, so he became displeased."
"35898","(35898) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Jarir, that he said to his people while exhorting them: What You are just like an ostrich that has been dispersed and they have taken a back, but if you do not find the back, then it is upon you, and indeed, the beginning of the earth is a desolation in its plains, then Our right will follow it, and the gathering will be here, and I will follow it."
"35899","(35899) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ata’ al-Wasiti, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, who said: He does not fear God. God is a servant who is ashamed of his tongue."
"35900","(35900) Affan narrated to us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman narrated to us, he said: Thabit narrated to us, on the authority of Anas, he said: We did not turn away from the Messenger May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so much so that our hearts deny us. (Tirmidhi 3618 and Ahmad 268)"
"35901","(35901) Affan bin Muslim narrated to us, he said: Suleiman bin Kathir narrated to us, he said: Al-Jald bin Ayyub narrated to us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Qurrah said: Anas bin Malik said to me: I have not seen anything like the one that has been conveyed to us on the authority of our Lord. We did not go out to him, on the authority of all If you avoid major sins for us, then we have nothing to do with them. God says: {If you avoid major sins that you are forbidden from, We will remit your bad deeds from you and admit you into a noble entrance. (Ibn Jarir 44)"
"35902","(35902) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Khalid, that Anas used to say: There is no soul. There is no morning without every spot calling out to its neighbour, oh my neighbour, whenever a prophet, or a truthful, or a servant passes by you today. A remembrance of God upon you. Some say: Yes, and some say: No."
"35903","(35903) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Bashir, on the authority of Anas, in his saying: {By your Lord, We will certainly ask them. All together for what they used to do. He said: There is no god but Allah."
"35904","(35904) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Anas, who said: Whoever takes a brother for the sake of God, the children of God He will have a tower in Paradise, and whoever wears a garment for his brother, God will clothe him with a garment in Hell, and whoever eats a garment for his brother, God will also clothe him with a garment in Hell. God has eaten him with it, He will eat him in the Fire, and whoever takes the place of his brother in the place of a hypocrite, God will put him in place on the Day of Resurrection. Hearing and seeing. (Bukhari 240, Abu Dawud 4847)"
"35905","(35905) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Anas, who said: Two men among the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, never met each other. May God bless him and grant him peace. So they separated until they made a supplication and mentioned Allah."
"35906","(35906) Ja’far bin Aoun told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Abu Talha, on the authority of Anas, who said: If you only knew what I know You would have cried a lot and laughed a little."
"35907","(35907) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, who said: We prolonged the hadith one night, then we entered upon Anas bin Malik. He said: You prolonged the hadith yesterday, but the hadith at the beginning of the night harms the end of it."
"35908","(35908) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, who heard Anas bin Malik say: He follows the dead. Three: his family, his money, and his work. His family and money return, and one remains, meaning his work."
"35909","(35909) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Husain bin Abdullah Al-Hafani, on the authority of Anas, He said: I do not know anything except prayer."
"35910","(35910) Yahya bin Ya’li told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Talq bin Habib, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, who said: Three Whoever is in it will find the taste and sweetness of faith: that God and His Messenger are more beloved to him than anything else, and that he be loved For the sake of God, and that he should be hated for the sake of God, and that if a fire were kindled for him, that he should fall in it, is more beloved to Him than that he should associate partners with God."
"35911","(35911) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Dirham, who said: I heard Anas bin Malik say in his saying: {And every human being. We forced a bird around his neck. He said: His book."
"35912","(35912) Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Raja’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Malik, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib: {My greeting to them on the day they meet Him is peace} He said: On the day they meet the angel of death, there will not be a believer who takes his soul except that he will submit. Aliyah"
"35913","(35913) Abu Muawiyah told us on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib, he said regarding his statement: {It is proven Allah is the one who believes with the word that is firm in the life of this world. He said: firmness in the life of this world when the two angels come to the man. In the grave, they said to him: Who is your Lord? He said: My Lord, God. They said: What is your religion? He said: My religion is Islam. They said: And who is your prophet? He said: Muhammad. He said: That is confirmation in the life of this world."
"35914","(35914) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: {Indeed, Allah I command you to return trusts to your family.} He said: Trusts in prayer, trusts in washing away from impurity, and trusts In measure, trust in weight, and the greatest of that is in deposits."
"35915","(35915) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I love for the sake of God, and I hate For the sake of God, and loyalty for the sake of God, and return for the sake of God, for the loyalty of God is only attained by that. No man can taste the taste of faith, even if it is abundant. His prayers and fasting until it is like this."
"35916","(35916) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He was told: A man of many I love you a lot of sins and a lot of deeds, or a man who has few sins and few deeds. He said: I do not equate anything with peace."
"35917","(35917) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Qaboos, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The righteous name and the righteous guidance. Economy is one of the twenty-five parts of prophecy. (Ahmed 296)"
"35918","(35918) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Uthman al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: {And he called out The companions of the Fire, the companions of the Garden, if you pour water upon us.} The verse, He said: A man calls upon his brother, and a man calls upon another man. He says: I have been burned, so pour water on me. He says: Then it is said to him: Answer it, and he says: Indeed, God has forbidden them to the disbelievers."
"35919","(35919) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in his saying: {The deceitful whisperer} He said: Satan is perched on the heart of the son of Adam, so when he is negligent and negligent, he is obsessive, and when he mentions God, he becomes deceived."
"35920","(35920) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bā, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mihran, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: {That A day for which all people will be gathered together, and that is a day witnessed. He said: The Day of Resurrection."
"35921","(35921) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Qaboos, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas {the night hours} he said: the middle of the night."
"35922","(35922) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Harun bin Antar, on the authority of his father, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas: Which work is best? He said: The remembrance of God is the greatest, and no people sit in a house where they deal with the Book of God among themselves and discuss it. Except that the angels will shade them with their wings, and they will be guests of God as long as they remain in Him, until they engage in conversation. Others"
"35923","(35923) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Abu Hakim Al-Bariki, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: {And the trumpet was blown. Then whoever is in the heavens and whoever is on earth was struck by it, except whomsoever God willed. He said: The first blow was blown on it, and they became bones and remains, then it was blown. In it is the second, and when they stand up they will look."
"35924","(35924) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas {May God exhort you to Return to the like of it. He said: May God make it difficult for you to return to the like of it."
"35925","(35925) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in his saying: {So fear God and put things right among yourselves.} He said: This is an encouragement from God to the believers to be fearful and put things in order. Between them."
"35926","(35926) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Qays, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: God guarantees to those who follow The Qur’an is that he should not go astray in this world, nor be miserable in the Hereafter, then he recited {So whoever follows My guidance shall neither go astray nor be miserable}"
"35927","(35927) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in his saying: {It has been sent to us by Our messengers, and they will not neglect} He said: The assistants of the Angel of Death are among the angels."
"35928","(35928) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas {If it falls The reality} He said: On the Day of Resurrection {There will be no liar in its event that lowers it or raises it} He said: It will lower some people and raise others up."
"35929","(35929) Haf?? bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: {Indeed, good deeds They remove evil deeds. He said: The five daily prayers."
"35930","(35930) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Yahya al-Qatat, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The earth You cry over the believer for forty mornings. (Ibn Jarir 29)"
"35931","(35931) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Qaboos, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Whoever sees me, God will see him.\n(Muslim 2289. Ibn Hibban 407)"
"35932","(35932) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Minhal, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas {The Most Gracious will make for them love} He said: He loves them and is loved by them."
"35933","(35933) Abu Asama told us, he said: Bashir bin Uqba told us, he said: Yazid bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: The son of Adam has thirty-three limbs, and each of them must pay zakat from praising God, praising Him, and remembering Him."
"35934","(35934) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas {so that you may not feel sad over what So come to you and do not rejoice in what He has given you.} He said: There is no one who does not grieve and rejoice, but he who endures calamity is patient and gives Good, thank you."
"35935","(35935) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Sami’, on the authority of Muslim Al-Batin, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas {Why is it that you do not hope for reverence for God?} What is the matter that you do not know the truth of His greatness?"
"35936","(35936) Affan narrated to us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman narrated to us, he said: Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah. Al-Ansari, he said: A man saw a skull and spoke to himself about something, he said: Then he fell down in his place, prostrating and repentant, he said: So it was said to him: Raise your head, for you are you and I am I."
"35937","(35937) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Tamim bin Tarfi, he said: I heard Al-Dahhak bin Qais says: O people, do your deeds for God, for God only accepts sincere work and does not pardon. One of you narrates an injustice and says: This is for God and for your faces, so it is not for God, but for their faces, and no One of you reaches out to his relatives and says: This is for God and for the relatives. Indeed, it is for the relatives. And whoever does a deed, let him make it for God, and no He associates anything with Me, for God will say on the Day of Resurrection: Whoever associates anything with Me in a work that he has done, it will be As for his partner, I have nothing to do with him."
"35938","(35938) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ad-Dahhak, who said: Al-Dahhak bin Qays used to say: O people, Teach your children and your parents the Qur’an, for for whomever God has decreed from a Muslim that he should admit him to Paradise, two kingdoms will be given to him. So they stopped him and said to him: Read and ascend the stairs of Paradise until they bring him down to where his deeds of the Qur’an ended."
"35939","(35939) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Maimun bin Mihran, he said: He said: I heard Al-Dahhak bin Qais says: Remember God in times of prosperity, and He will remember you in times of hardship, for Yunus was a righteous servant who remembered God, so when He fell into the belly of the whale. God said: {And had he not been of those who glorify Him, he would have remained in its belly until the Day they are resurrected} and indeed Pharaoh was a tyrannical servant who forgot to remember God, so when he overtook him, he said: I believe that there is no god but the One in whom I believe. Israel and I am one of the Muslims now, and I disobeyed before and was one of the corrupters}"
"35940","(35940) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Qurayh bin Khalid al-Sadusi, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal al-Adawi, on the authority of Khalid bin Umair. The infection,"
"35941","(35941) He said: Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Na’am, he heard it from Khalid bin Umair, he said: Utba bin Ghazwan addressed us. Abu Naamah said on the pulpit, and his Quran did not say anything, so he said: Indeed, the world has called for a fast and has left a shoe, and there is no longer any Thereof, except for sababah, like the sababah of a vessel. You are in a place from which you are moving, so move with the best that is in your presence. Indeed, You saw me on the seventh day of the night with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we had no food to eat except tree leaves until they ulcerated. Our friends. Qurra said: And I found a cloak. He said: And Abu Naam said: I picked up a cloak and tore it in two halves and put it on. Half of it and you gave Saad half of it, and not one of those seven is alive today except in one of the Egypts, and you will be tried. The princes after me, and indeed, by God, there was no prophecy except that it was reincarnated until it became a kingdom and a tyrant, and it was mentioned to me, Quran said: It is a stone, and Abu Naama said: It is a rock that will be hurled from the edge of Hell and it will descend to its resting place. He said He recited: I see it, he said: seventy, and Abu Naama said: seventy sheep, and let them be filled, and what is between the two sides of The gates of Paradise will last for forty years, and they will come upon the gates of Paradise on a day when there will not be a door from it except that it is Like intense, and I seek refuge in God that I should be great in myself, and small in the sight of God."
"35942","(35942) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Al-Majishun bin Abi Salamah, he said: Saad said Ibn Muadh: There are three things I am among, yet weak: I never heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say a word without knowing. It is true, and I have never prayed a prayer so that someone else distracted me from it until he left, and I have never followed a funeral so that I spoke to myself. Other than what someone said, or it will be said to her until we have finished with her. Muhammad said: So I narrated that to Al-Zuhri, and he said: May God have mercy on Sa`d if he was trustworthy, and I did not see anyone being like this except a prophet."
"35943","(35943) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, he said: Abdullah built a house In his house of milk, then he called Ammar and said: How do you see, O Abu Al-Yaqzan? He said: I see you have built a strong state and have moved far away. And you will die soon."
"35944","(35944) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, who said: Hudhayfy rose in Al-Mada’in. So he delivered a sermon, thanked God and praised Him, then said: {The Hour has approached and the moon is split open} Indeed, the Hour has approached, and the moon It has split. Indeed, the world has heralded separation. Indeed, the track is today, and the race is tomorrow, and the ultimate goal is Hell. The forerunner is the one who precedes to Paradise."
"35945","(35945) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Amiri, who said: I heard Hudhayfah saying: According to the believer from Knowledge is to fear God, and it suffices him from lying to say: I ask forgiveness from God, then he comes back."
"35946","(35946) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Salla, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: The people will gather in On a single level, sight penetrates them and the caller hears them, and a herald calls: O Muhammad, upon the heads of the first and the last, and he says May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: May God bless you and grant you peace, and goodness is in your hands, and evil is not yours, and the Mahdi is the one who You are guided, you are blessed and exalted. Hudhayfy said: This is the Praiseworthy Station."
"35947","(35947) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Hudhaifa, he said: He used to enter The mosque, and he will stand on the edge and say: O community of the Qur’an, take the path, for if you take it, you will have gone far ahead. And whether you take it to the right or to the left, you have certainly gone astray far astray."
"35948","(35948) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Musa bin Abdullah bin Yazid, on the authority of Umm Salamah, who said: He said: Hudhaifa: I wish I had someone to take over my wealth, then close the door on me and no one would enter until I join God.\n(Ibn Al-Mubarak 20)"
"35949","(35949) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abu Wa’il Shaqiq, on the authority of Khalid ibn Rabi’ al-Absi, who said: When The weight of its hut reached us. A group of Banu Abs and a group of Ansar went out to it. Abu Masoud was with us and said: So we came to him. Some night, he said: What is this hour? We said: Such and such hour. He said: I seek refuge in God from morning to Hell. Did you bring me with you with a shroud? We said: Yes. He said: Do not go to extremes with my sufficiency, for if your companion is better with God, He will substitute something better than him, otherwise he will be robbed. quickly (Abu Dawud 3146)"
"35950","(35950) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Muhammad bin al-Muntashir, on the authority of Ibn Harash, on the authority of Hudhayfa Ibn Al-Yaman, he said: In the grave there is a reckoning, and on the Day of Resurrection there is a punishment."
"35951","(35951) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: When Hudhayfah was brought with his shroud, he said: If it is poured Your brother is good, then perhaps, otherwise they will remain in disgrace with him until the Day of Resurrection."
"35952","(35952) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Hudhayfy: {For those who do good, good deeds And Ziyad} said: looking at the face of God."
"35953","(35953) Yahya bin Abi Bukair told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Misra, he said: I heard Ziyad narrated on the authority of Rabi’i ibn Harash, on the authority of Hudhayfah, that he said: O Lord, on the Day when death should come upon me, I will not doubt. As for Today I have been mixed up with things that I do not know what I am up to, and he advised Abu Masoud, saying: Adhere to what you know. And beware of distorting the religion of God."
"35954","(35954) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, on the authority of Abu Abdullah al-Filistini, on the authority of Abdul Aziz Ibn A brother of Hudhayfah. He said: I heard it from Hudhaifa forty-five years ago. He said: Hudhayfah said: The first thing you will lose from Your religion is humility, and the last thing you will lose from your religion is prayer."
"35955","(35955) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Jundub bin Abdullah Al-Bajli, then Al-Qasri said: I asked permission to come to Hudhayfah three times, but he did not give me permission. So I returned and his messenger had joined me, and he said: What's your response? I said: I thought you were sleeping. He said: I would not sleep until I saw where the sun rose from. He said: So I told him about it to Muhammad, and he said: I have More than one of the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, did so."
"35956","(35956) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shimr ibn Atiyya, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Ubaad ibn The silent one, he said: When the Day of Resurrection comes, God will say: Give away what I had of this world, and throw all of it into the Fire.\n(Ibn Al-Mubarak 544)"
"35957","(35957) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ammar bin Hamza, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, he said: He came A man went to Ubadah ibn al-Samit, and he said: A man who prays, seeking the face of God, and loves to be praised. He said: It is nothing. Indeed, God says: I am the best of partners, so whoever has a partner with me has it all, and I have no need for it."
"35958","(35958) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: I heard Maymun ibn Abi Shabib speaking on the authority of Ubad ibn The silent one said: I wish for my beloved that his wealth will decrease or that his death will be hastened."
"35959","(35959) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abu Musa, who said: Only those who are This dinar and dirham came before you, and they are yours. (Abu Nu’aym 261, Ibn Hibban 694)"
"35960","(35960) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Abi Imran al-Juniyi, on the authority of Ibn Abi Moses, on the authority of his father {And for whoever fears the standing of his Lord there are two gardens} He said: Two gardens of gold for those who came before them and two gardens of silver for those who follow them. (Hakim 474)"
"35961","(35961) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Abu Musa, who said: The sun is above the heads of the people. On the Day of Resurrection, their deeds will shade them or make them a sacrifice."
"35962","(35962) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, he said: We were with Abu Musa, he said: So we came at night to a ruined orchard, he said, so Abu Musa got up during the night and prayed, and he recited his recitation beautifully, then he said: Oh God. You are a believer who loves a believer. You are a dominant person and you love a dominant person. You are a believer who loves peace. You are a truthful person and you love a truthful person."
"35963","(35963) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: A soul emerges The believer said: “And it has a sweeter scent than musk.” He said: “Then the angels who take her will ascend with it, and they will meet them.” Your angels are below the heavens, and they say: Who is this with you? They say: So-and-so, and they remind him of his best deeds. They say: May God bless you and may those who are with you live. He said: So it will be opened for him. The gates of the heavens. He said: Then his face will shine, and the Lord will come to you, and a proof like the sun will come to his face. He said: As for the last, it will come out. His soul is like a corpse, and the angels who take it take it up, and the angels meet them without heavens, and they say: Who is this? So they say: So-and-so, and they remind him of his worst deed. He said: So they say: Return him, for God has not wronged him in the least. He said: And he recited Abu Musa: {And they will not enter Paradise until the camel enters the eye of a tailor}."
"35964","(35964) Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Abu Musa wrote to Amir from Abdullah bin Qais to Amer bin Abdullah, who was called Amer bin Abdul Qais. Now, I made acquaintances with you on a matter, and I was informed that you If you have changed, then fear God and keep your promise. If you have changed, then fear God and keep your promise."
"35965","(35965) Ali bin Musahir told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Kabsha, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: A good companion is better. Who is alone, and being alone is better than a bad companion. Indeed, the likeness of a good companion is like perfume, unless it is fragrant. With you from his scent. Indeed, the likeness of a bad companion is like a kiln. Unless it burns you, it fills you with his scent. Indeed, it is only It is called the heart because of its volatility, meaning that the likeness of the heart is like a feather attached to a tree in a clearing on the earth, and the wind stirs it up. Outwardly and inwardly. (Ibn Al-Mubarak 358)"
"35966","(35966) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit al-Bunani, on the authority of Anas, he said: We were with Abu Musa was in his house, and he heard the people talking, so he heard it eloquently and eloquently. He said: Then he said: O Anas, come, let us remember God. Hurry, for among these people, one of them almost slandered the human being with his tongue, then he said: O Anas, what has discouraged the people from What deterred them from the Hereafter? He said: I said: This world and desires. He said: No, but the Hereafter is absent and this world is hastened, and if they had witnessed it, they would not have treated them justly. And they did not incline."
"35967","(35967) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Mikhraq, on the authority of Abu Iyas, on the authority of Abu Kinanani, on the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, that he said: Indeed, this Qur’an is there for you a reward, and there is for you a reminder, and there is upon you a burden. So follow the Qur’an, and let it not follow you, for whoever follows the Qur’an will land therein on the gardens of Paradise, and whoever follows it will The Qur’an is shaken at the back of his mouth and casts him into Hell."
"35968","(35968) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abi Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Moses, he said: When the morning comes, Satan sends his soldiers and says: I will not stop him until he drinks. He said: You, he says: I will not stop him until he drinks. He committed adultery. He said: You. He said: I did not spare him until he was killed. He said: You."
"35969","(35969) Affan told us, he said: Wahib told us, he said: Dawud bin Abi Hind told us, on the authority of Abi Harb bin Abi Al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, said: Abu Musa gathered the Qur’an, and said: They will not enter upon you except those who have compiled the Qur’an. He said: So we entered. About three hundred men, so he admonished us and said: You are the people of this country and you, so do not let yourselves go too long or become hardened. Your hearts have hardened as the hearts of the People of the Book have hardened."
"35970","(35970) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Burda, he said: My father sent me to Medina, and he said: The truth. Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I asked them, and know that I am asking you. I met Ibn Salam, and behold, he was a humble man."
"35971","(35971) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: When Ibn al-Zubayr stood up for prayer, it was as if he had A peg"
"35972","(35972) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I have never seen a prostration greater than yours, meaning Ibn Al-Zubayr."
"35973","(35973) Abdullah bin Numir told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwah informed us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, he said: {Take pardon} He said: He was not commanded to do so except out of the morals of the people, and by God I will certainly take it in them as long as I am with them."
"35974","(35974) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Shayban, on the authority of Abu Nawfal ibn Abi Aqrab, who said: We entered upon Ibn al-Zubayr while he was continuing on the fifteenth day of prayer."
"35975","(35975) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Marzban, he said: Muhammad bin Ubaid Allah Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: I saw Ibn Al-Zubayr addressed them and said: You have come from various countries seeking a great matter, so you must make good and sincere supplications. The intention"
"35976","(35976) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of Wahhab ibn Kaysan, who said: A man from the people of Iraq to Ibn al-Zubayr when he was sold out: Peace be upon you, for I praise God to you, there is no god but Him. As for what follows: The people who obey God and the people of goodness have signs by which they are known, and among them they are known for enjoining what is right and forbidding what is wrong. evil, and work in obedience to God, and know that the imam is like a market. Righteousness is due to their righteousness, and if he is an immoral person, then the immoral people will come to him for their immorality."
"35977","(35977) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Utai, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka'b, he said: The food of the son of Adam is given as an example, and if he salts it and spices it, he knows what it will become."
"35978","(35978) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, Abd al-Rahman bin Awf. He brought food, so Abd al-Rahman said: Hamza was killed and we did not find anything to cover him with, and he was better than him, and Mus`ab bin was killed. Umair, who is better than me, did not find anything to cover him with, and we have suffered from it as we have suffered from it. Then Abd al-Rahman said: Indeed, I fear that our good deeds in this world have been hastened for us."
"35979","(35979) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ma’in, on the authority of Aoun bin Abdullah, who said: There was a man among us in a garden. In Egypt, during the turmoil of Ibn al-Zubayr, he was sitting, worried and sad, crying on the ground. When he raised his head, there was a man with a mask standing. In his hands, he said: The owner of the apron, why do I see you so worried and sad? It was as if he disdained him, so he said: Nothing, so he said: The one who wears the Messenger: If you have this world, then this world is a present offering. The righteous and the immoral may eat from it, and the Hereafter is a true term. It is ruled by a powerful King who separates truth from falsehood. He even mentioned that it has joints like the joints of meat. He made a mistake in some of it and he wronged the truth, so when he heard about that, he said: My concern for what is in it is for the Muslims. He said: Then he said: For God We will save you with your compassion for the Muslims. Ask, who is the one who asked God and He did not give him, and prayed to God and He did not answer? And he put his trust in Him, but He did not suffice him, and he trusted Him, but He did not save him. He said: So I began to say: Oh God, protect me and protect me from me. He said: She appeared and I was not harmed by anything from her."
"35980","(35980) Qubaisa bin Uqba narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, on the authority of Ibn Abjar, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhayl, He said: Abu Juhayfy told me, and he said to me: O Salamah, nothing remains of what I knew except this prayer, and there is no There is no soul that You would be pleased to redeem me from death, not the soul of a fly. He said: Then he wept."
"35981","(35981) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Aqmar, on the authority of Abu Juhaifa, who said: Sit with the great, mingle with the wise, and ask the scholars."
"35982","(35982) Muhammad bin Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, who said: They passed by my father’s funeral. Abd al-Rahman Ali Abi Juhayfah, and he said: He was relieved and he was relieved from it."
"35983","(35983) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Abi Hazim, on the authority of al-Nu’man Ibn Abi Ayyash, on the authority of Abu Saeed {For he will have a straitened livelihood}. He said: The torment of the grave."
"35984","(35984) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Hayyan, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of Abu Sa`id {to return you to Ma`ad}, he said: The afterlife: Paradise."
"35985","(35985) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Abu al-Waddak, on the authority of Abu Sa`id, who said: Abraham met him. He will be his father on the Day of Resurrection, and he will cling to him, and Abraham will say to him: I commanded you and I forbade you, but you disobeyed me. He said: But today I will not disobey you. He said: Then Abraham will go to Paradise and he will be with him. He said: Then it will be said to him: O Abraham, He called him, he said: So he says: God promised me that he would not let me down today, he said: Then Abraham comes, coming from his Lord as a king. So he greeted him, and Abraham was terrified for him, and he spoke to him and was busy until he distracted him from his father. He said: Then the king will go. And Abraham walked towards the Garden, he said: Then his father called him: O Abraham, he said: Then he turned to him, and he had changed His creation, he said: Then Ibrahim says: Uff, aff, then he straightens up and leaves him."
"35986","(35986) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ya’la, who said: Al-Rabi’ ibn Khuthaym was He passed by the council saying: Speak good and do good and persevere in good deeds, and do not let your hearts be hardened and let your time not be prolonged. And do not be like those who said: We heard, but they do not hear."
"35987","(35987) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ali, he said: It was spring when It was said to him: How did you become? He said: We have become weak and sinful, eating our livelihood and waiting for our time."
"35988","(35988) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ya’la, on the authority of Rabi’, he said: I do not like The servant’s appeal to his Lord says: My Lord, You have decreed mercy upon Yourself, You have decreed such and such upon Yourself. He is not slow, but he does not delay. I saw someone saying: My Lord, I have fulfilled what I owe you, so fulfill what you owe me."
"35989","(35989) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ya’la, on the authority of Rabi’ bin Khathim, who said: What Being absent and waiting for a believer is better than death."
"35990","(35990) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Mundhir, on the authority of al-Rabi’ ibn Khuthām that he commanded His death, and he said: This is what Al-Rabi’ bin Khuthham acknowledged about himself and bore witness to, and God is sufficient as a witness. And as a reward for His righteous servants and a reward. Indeed, I am satisfied with God as Lord, Islam as religion, and Muhammad as Prophet, and I am satisfied with myself. And for whoever obeys Me, I say that I should worship Him among those who worship Him, and praise Him among those who praise Him, and that I should be sincere to the community of Muslims."
"35991","(35991) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of his father, who said: I did not hear Al-Rabi’ bin Khathim mentioning Nothing of the matter of this world, except that I heard him say once: How many mosques do the orphans have?"
"35992","(35992) Abu Asama narrated to us, he said: Sufyan Al-Thawri narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Bakr bin Ma’iz, he said: He said to me: Al-Rabi’ bin Khuthaym: O Bakr, be careful with your tongue, except for what is yours, and not against you, for I have accused people based on my religion. Obey God in what you know, and whatever He has chosen over you is all within His knowledge, because we are more afraid of you than I am of you. Concerning error, the best of you today is not good, but it is better than the last evil of it. You do not follow good as long as you follow it. And do not flee from evil as it should be avoided. You have not comprehended everything that God revealed to Muhammad, nor do you know everything that you read. What are secrets? Which are hidden from the people, and to Him there is a valley. They sought a cure for them. Then he would say to himself: And what is the cure for her that she repents? Then don't come back."
"35993","(35993) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Bashir, the servant of Al-Rabi’, who said: Al-Rabi’ was praying. That night, he passed by these verses: “Or is it sufficient for those who commit evil deeds?” He repeated them until the morning."
"35994","(35994) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Spring was coming in its midst, and it was in His mosque is a road, and beside it were women who used to pass through the mosque, so he did not say such or such."
"35995","(35995) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Razin, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ ibn Khuthaym {And then you will not be given enjoyment. Except a little. He said: It is a little between them and the appointed time."
"35996","(35996) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Razin, on the authority of Rabi’ bin Khuthaym: {Yes, he who earns evil And his sin surrounded him. He said: They died in their disbelief, and perhaps he said: They died in disobedience."
"35997","(35997) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Mundhir, on the authority of Rabi’ bin Khuthaym, that he used to sweep the lawn. By himself, he said: Then it was said to him: This is enough for you. He said: I would like to take my share of the fortune."
"35998","(35998) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ ibn Khuthaym, who said: Speak less, except by nine. : Glorifying, glorifying, glorifying, and praising God, asking you for good, seeking refuge from evil, and enjoining good. And forbidding evil, and reciting the Qur’an."
"35999","(35999) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mundhir, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, that he said to his family: Make something good for me, so he did. So he called a man who was suffering from dementia, and Rabe’a began to bite him and his saliva flowed. When he ate and left, his family said to him: We are burdened. We made it, then I fed it to a man who did not know what he ate. Al-Rabi’ said: But God knows."
"36000","(36000) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Malik bin Mughul narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Al-Rabi’ bin Khuthaym never sat in He has been sitting since he was wrapped in a garment and said: I fear that a man will be wronged and I will not help him, or that a man will slander another man, so I will be charged. Witness is upon him, and I will not lower the gaze, nor guide me to the path, or the pregnant woman fall, and I will not carry the burden for her."
"36001","(36001) Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Sayyar, on the authority of Abu Wael, who said: My brother and I set out for Al-Rabi’ bin Khathim. So, when he was sitting in the mosque, he said: He did not bring you. They said: We have come so that you may remember God, so we will remember Him with you, and praise God. So we thanked Him with you, so he raised his hand and said: Praise be to God that you did not say: We have come for you to drink so we will drink with you, or We have come for you to commit adultery. So we committed adultery with you."
"36002","(36002) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, who said: He narrated to me someone who heard Al-Rabi’ saying: How strange the angel of death is. And three people will come to him: a king who is in hiding in his fortresses, so he will come to you and remove himself and leave his kingdom behind him, and a physician. Nahrir heals people, so he comes to him and takes away his soul. (Abu Naim 115)"
"36003","(36003) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Rabi’ ibn Khuthām, that a horse was stolen from him during the night. And he was praying, his value was thirty thousand, but he did not leave, so in the morning he collected her dowry, then in the morning, he said: Oh God. He stole from me, but I was not going to steal from him. He said: Rabi’ was reciting the Qur’an out loud, but when he heard a knock, it became frightened."
"36004","(36004) Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, who said to al-Rabi’: Shall we not pray for you? A doctor, and he said: Look at me, then he thought, and said: {And Aad, and Thamud, and the Companions of the Land, and many centuries between that, and each of them struck us. To Him are parables, and all of us have purified Himself.} So he mentioned of their eagerness for this world and their desire for it. He said: It was his illness, and he was Among them are doctors, but neither the healer nor the healer remains. The one who is cursed and the one who is denied has perished. By God, you will not call for a physician for me."
"36005","(36005) Ubaidah bin Humaid narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, he said: We entered upon Al-Rabi’ bin Khathim, and he called With these supplications: O God, all praise is due to You, and to You the whole matter is returned, and You are the God of all creation, in Your hand. All good, we ask you from all good, and we seek refuge in you from all evil."
"36006","(36006) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of the concubines of Al-Rabi’, she said: When Al-Rabi’ came, his daughter cried, and he said: My daughters, why are you crying? Say, O human being: He met my father with goodness."
"36007","(36007) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymiy, who said: It was narrated to me by someone who accompanied Rabi’ ibn For twenty years, he did not hear a word of reproach from him."
"36008","(36008) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Mundhir, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Khathim, in his saying: {But if he was one of Those who are brought near are joy and comfort and a garden of bliss. He said: He has {and you will enter Hell}. He said: It is stored up for him."
"36009","(36009) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Nasir Abi Tu’ma, who said: It was spring when a beggar came to him, and he said: Feed this beggar sugar, for spring loves sugar."
"36010","(36010) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Rabi’ bin Khathim, regarding his saying: {Ya O man, what has deceived you about your Lord, the Most Generous? He said: Ignorance."
"36011","(36011) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, on the authority of Masruq, who said: There is nothing. It is better for the believer than someone who has been relieved from the worries of this world and safe from the punishment of God. (Abu Naim 97)"
"36012","(36012) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: He performed a stolen Hajj, so he only slept prostrating."
"36013","(36013) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Masruq said: There is nothing in this world that I regret except prostration to God."
"36014","(36014) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughul, on the authority of Abu Al-Sifar, on the authority of Mara, who said: She did not give birth. Hamdaniya is like stolen."
"36015","(36015) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, who said: A servant never took a single step without... His good or bad deeds are recorded for him."
"36016","(36016) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Masruq, who said: There is no good deed that is greater in the sight of God than a word."
"36017","(36017) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, who said: A person has the right to have Gatherings where he is alone, where his sins are mentioned and he asks for forgiveness from them."
"36018","(36018) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Muslim, or someone else. Al-A’mash doubted, on the authority of Masruq, he said: It is better. I am not suspicious when the servant says: There is no grain of wheat or dirhams in the house."
"36019","(36019) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, who said: The closest thing to it is The servant turns to God while prostrating."
"36020","(36020) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, he said: Masruq said: Who was pleased with that? He knows the knowledge of the ancients and the last, and the knowledge of this world and the hereafter, so let him recite Surah Al-Waqi’iyyah."
"36021","(36021) Affan bin Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Awani narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Amir, that a man was sitting To a stolen person who knows his face but does not give his name. He said: So he sent for him. He said: He was the last to bid him farewell, and he said: You are Quray. The Qur’aans and their master, and indeed your adornment for them is adornment, and your adornment for them is disgraceful, so do not talk to yourself about poverty or a long life."
"36022","(34022) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, who said: When he came from the chain, people came to him. Kufa, and some merchants came to him and began to praise him and say: May God reward you well, as he had pardoned you from Our wealth, so he recited this verse: {Is he who We have promised him a good promise? He will meet it as if We have given him enjoyment of the enjoyment of the life of this world}"
"36023","(36023) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, who said: It is enough for a person to be astonished by ignorance. With his knowledge and according to his knowledge, he should fear God."
"36024","(34024) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, who said: There was a man in the desert who had a dog. And a donkey and a rooster. He said: The rooster wakes them up for prayer, and the donkey is the one they carry water on, and they benefit from it. And they were carrying their tents for them, and the dog was guarding them. Then a fox came and took the rooster, and they were saddened by the disappearance of the rooster. The man was righteous, so he said: Perhaps he will be good. He said: So they stayed as long as God willed, then a wolf came and tore open the donkey’s belly and killed it. They were saddened by the disappearance of the donkey, and the righteous man said: Perhaps it will be good. Then they remained after that as long as God willed, and then he was struck. The dog, and he said: The righteous man: Perhaps it will be good. So when they looked in the morning, they saw that he had been taken captive by those around them, and they remained He said: Those were taken for what they had of voice and commotion, and they did not have anything to bring about. Their dogs, their donkeys, and their roosters are gone."
"36025","(34025) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Masruq, who said: A righteous man with insight came out of his darkness in the darkness of the night. So he wanted to give it in charity, and he met a man who had a lot of money and gave it to him. When morning came, he said: Don’t you marvel at so-and-so? And his wealth increased, a man came to him with a bag of dirhams and he gave them to him. This reached the man and he was upset with him and said: What I see it being accepted from me when I gave it to this rich man.\n2. He said: And he went out the other night to Sora and gave her to a prostituted woman. When morning came, they said: Don’t you marvel at so-and-so? So-and-so came to her with a gift, and he gave it to her, and she did not withhold her foot from anyone. So this was reported to him, and he was upset with him, and he said: I don’t see it. He accepts from me.\n3. He said: Then he was brought in a dream and it was said to him: May what you have been given this wealth be accepted from you. We wanted to see him, that among the people Whoever gives charity, desires that, but as for the woman, she only desires a need, so we wanted to spare her."
"36026","(36026) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Anas ibn Sirin, who said: Masruq used to pray until you sat down. His wife behind him is crying."
"36027","(36027) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Ibn Umairah, on the authority of Masruq, he said: Wad The people of calamity on the Day of Resurrection will have their skins cut off with scalpels."
"36028","(36028) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, who said: We came to Murr to ask about him, and they said: Murr of the pure, So when he is in his highness, he has worshiped there for twelve years."
"36029","(36029) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of al-Haytham, who said: He used to pray every day. Two hundred rak'ahs."
"36030","(36030) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, he said: Mary was asked: About what remained of your prayer. He said: The half. Two hundred and fifty rak'ahs."
"36031","(36031) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Murā, {and their hearts were air}. He said: not broken. You are aware of something."
"36032","(36032) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: He was nothing but one of the monks."
"36033","(36033) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: He was asked about Al-Aswad, and he said: He was fasting. A distinguished pilgrim."
"36034","(36034) Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Hassan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of some of his companions, he said: If the lions To fast on the extremely hot day in which it is seen that the red-skinned camel staggers from the heat."
"36035","(36035) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, he said: Hanash bin Al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Ali bin Mudrak narrated to us, that his illness He used to say to the lions: Why are you torturing this body? He would say: I only want comfort for him."
"36036","(36036) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Hanash bin Al-Harith narrated to us, saying: I saw Al-Aswad bin Yazid gone. One of his eyes from fasting."
"36037","(36037) Al-Fadl narrated to us, on the authority of Hanash, on the authority of Riyah Al-Nakha’i, who said: Al-Aswad used to fast while traveling until he changed his clothes. Its color is from thirst on a hot day other than Ramadan."
"36038","(36038) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Shabak, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, that he used to say To his companions: Go with us, so that we may increase in faith."
"36039","(36039) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: Al-Sha’bi was asked about Alqamiya, he said: He was with the slow one. And the quick overtakes you."
"36040","(36040) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, on the authority of Abul-Safir, on the authority of Murā’, he said: Alqāmī was among the The Lords."
"36041","(36041) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Alqamiya recited the Qur’an one night."
"36042","(36042) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya: {Indeed, the earthquake of the Hour is a great thing} A partner said: This is in this world before the Day of Resurrection. Jarir said: This is at the hands of the Hour."
"36043","(36043) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When he saw one of his companions, he was upset, or he said: : Remembrance of ease among the days like this."
"36044","(36044) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abu Muammar, he said: We entered upon Amr bin Sharhabeel, and he said: Go with us to the most similar people, greeting and guiding Abdullah, so we entered upon Alqamah."
"36045","(36045) Abu Asama told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, he said: Ammar told us, on the authority of Abu Muammar, he said: We were sitting at Amr ibn Shurahbil, and he said: Take us to the people who are most like people in guidance, guidance, and handsomeness, and confuse them with Abdullah, but we did not know From there until we set out for Alqamah."
"36046","(36046) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Hammam woke up walking on foot, and some of the people said: A group of pigeons to inform you that they did not use their pillows during the night."
"36047","(36047) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There was a man from among us, called: Hammam bin Al-Harith did not sleep unless he was sitting in the mosque during his prayers, so he used to say: Oh God, heal me from sleep with ease. And grant me a watchful mind in obedience to You."
"36048","(36048) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Ibn Maqil: (And if you could see, when they were frightened, then do not miss it) He said: He frightened them and did not miss it. They miss it."
"36049","(36049) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Amr bin Shurahbil, he said: Today I am not easy to die in a light state or situation, and I will not leave behind a debt, nor will I leave behind dependents for whom I fear loss, had it not been for the horror. The informed"
"36050","(36050) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Misra, he said: It was When he went to bed, he wept, then said: I wish my mother had not given birth to me. It was said: Why. He said: Because we were told that we were sent to her but we were not informed. We confiscated it."
"36051","(36051) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Shurahbil, he said: He died A man whom they thought was pious, so he was brought to his grave and it was said: Indeed, they will flog you with a hundred lashes from the punishment of God. He said: What You are flogging me, for I was afraid and fearful, so it was said: Fifty, and they did not cease to criticize him until he came to flogging, and he was flogged. Then the grave was engulfed in fire, and the man was destroyed. Then he was brought back, and he said, “Why did you flog me?” They said: “I prayed on the day you know that you were upon me.” Other than ablution, and the weak and needy asked you for help, but you did not help him."
"36052","(36052) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Wael, who said: I have never seen a Hamdan more beloved to me. I will be flaying his skin from Amr bin Sharhabeel."
"36053","(36053) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Salih, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Misra, who said: Whoever does this Verse, righteousness has been completed: {It is not righteousness that you turn your faces toward the east and the west}"
"36054","(36054) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: Sulaym bin Al-Aswad Abu Al-Sha’athi entered upon my father and asked him to return. He said: Indeed, in death there is comfort. Abu Wael said: I have a companion better for me than you: five prayers a day."
"36055","(36055) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, he said: Abu Wa’il said to me: O Sulaiman, by God, if we had obeyed God, we would not have obeyed him. He disobeyed us."
"36056","(36056) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Asim, that Abu Wa’il used to say while he was prostrating: If you pardon me, you will be pardoned. Too long of you, and if you torture me, you will torture me without injustice or without precedence, then he will cry."
"36057","(36057) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, he said: Ibrahim al-Taymi was mentioned in Abu Wael’s house, so he Abu Wael flutters like a bird flutters."
"36058","(36058) Ja’far bin Aoun told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, who said: The readers of our time are nothing like this except this. Dilhams, ripened, or sheep that grazed chickpeas and their bellies bloated, and some of them were slaughtered, but if they were not cleaned, they would not be cleaned."
"36059","(36059) Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, saying: Qutbai narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, that he used to perform ablution. He says to Satan: “Get everything you need now.”"
"36060","(36060) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: Abraham said to me, “You have a brother, for I have met the companions of Abdullah, and they are available, and they are preparing you from among their choices."
"36061","(36061) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam, who said: You came to a supporter and he was prostrating. He was asleep. He said: So I came to him and he was saying: Oh God, heal me from sleep with a little, then he continued in his prayer."
"36062","(36062) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, he said: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, he said: A person who supported himself was shot with an arrow. In his head, he removed the arrow from his head, then placed his hand on its place, then said: Indeed, it is a small one, and God May He bless the little ones."
"36063","(36063) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, who said: He stained his garment with the blood of Ma’add. He said: So he washed it, but no traces of it left. He said: He used to pray in it and say: He will add more love to me than the blood of Ma’adid."
"36064","(36044) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara, who said: Ma’add descended next to a tree, and said: By God, what Do I care whether I prayed for this person instead of God, or whether I obeyed a created being in disobedience to God?"
"36065","(36065) Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, he said: Ma’add had a brother, he said: He used to come to the market and buy. And he sells and spends on his family and on Maadid’s family. He said: And he used to say: He is better than me, we are among his family. He spends on us."
"36066","(36066) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Razin, in his saying: {And purify your garments} He said: Your deed is made good. So, if a man did a good job, it would be said: So-and-so has clean clothes."
"36067","(36067) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, and Abu Razin {so they will be distributed}, saying: The first of them will be imprisoned over the last of them."
"36068","(36068) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Sami’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Razin, in his saying: {So let them laugh. a little, and let them cry much.} He said: God says: The world is a little, so let them laugh in it as much as they want. In the afterlife, they wept uninterruptedly, and that was a lot."
"36069","(36069) Ali bin Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Sami’, on the authority of Abu Razin, in his saying: {Indeed, it is one of the Pride. He said: Hell is a warner to mankind. He said: God says: I am a warner to you from it."
"36070","(36070) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Sami’, on the authority of Abu Razin: “Wavings to humans” he said: waving His skin until you call it blacker than the night."
"36071","(36071) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Razin, who said: Al-Ghasaq is what flows from pus"
"36072","(36072) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, he said: I heard them say: Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid never did any work except And he wants the face of God."
